WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.633 --> 00:00:02.068
Harry: From calorie
count to portion sizes,

00:00:02.068 --> 00:00:03.503
we wanted to find out all the differences

00:00:03.503 --> 00:00:06.272
between MrBeast Burger
in the UK and the US.

00:00:06.272 --> 00:00:07.941
This is "Food Wars."

00:00:09.976 --> 00:00:12.412
In the US, a MrBeast Beast-style burger

00:00:12.412 --> 00:00:14.681
comes in double and triple.

00:00:14.681 --> 00:00:17.117
The Beast-style burger in the
UK also comes in two sizes,

00:00:17.117 --> 00:00:18.451
the double and a triple.

00:00:18.451 --> 00:00:19.919
It's dripping grease.

00:00:19.919 --> 00:00:22.422
Holy sheesh!

00:00:22.422 --> 00:00:24.391
Can you see how wet this is?

00:00:24.391 --> 00:00:26.059
Let's weigh a triple burger now

00:00:26.059 --> 00:00:28.128
to see whose burger is bigger.

00:00:28.128 --> 00:00:30.463
Look how gross these
scales are, by the way.

00:00:30.463 --> 00:00:33.333
A Beast-style triple in
the UK weighs 270 grams.

00:00:33.333 --> 00:00:35.835
Joe: The US triple Beast-style burger

00:00:35.835 --> 00:00:38.872
weighs 290 grams.

00:00:38.872 --> 00:00:41.641
In the US, MrBeast Burger has one size

00:00:41.641 --> 00:00:42.742
of crinkle-cut fries.

00:00:42.742 --> 00:00:46.312
They come in either
unseasoned or seasoned.

00:00:46.312 --> 00:00:48.248
In the UK, we also just
have one size of fries.

00:00:48.248 --> 00:00:50.417
And they come as either seasoned

00:00:50.417 --> 00:00:52.352
or as unseasoned.

00:00:52.352 --> 00:00:55.755
Speaking of fries, the menu
offers a Chris-style burger.

00:00:55.755 --> 00:00:56.990
Who's Chris?

00:00:56.990 --> 00:00:59.092
His burger has fries on it,

00:00:59.092 --> 00:01:01.194
and for this they charge
you an extra dollar,

00:01:01.194 --> 00:01:03.897
or in the UK an extra British pound.

00:01:03.897 --> 00:01:07.367
This got me wondering, how
many fries come on this burger,

00:01:07.367 --> 00:01:09.936
and does that warrant
an extra dollar charge?

00:01:09.936 --> 00:01:12.005
Let's count and find out.

00:01:12.005 --> 00:01:13.907
One, two, three.

00:01:13.907 --> 00:01:16.076
[fast-forwarding]

00:01:16.076 --> 00:01:17.844
That seems reasonably generous.

00:01:17.844 --> 00:01:20.113
27 fries on my Chris-style burger.

00:01:20.113 --> 00:01:21.314
But what about the cost of the fries?

00:01:21.314 --> 00:01:23.550
Let's count how many
fries come in an order.

00:01:23.550 --> 00:01:25.018
One, two, three.

00:01:25.952 --> 00:01:27.754
Counting that one, 92.

00:01:27.754 --> 00:01:29.522
Let's go by volume. For an extra dollar,

00:01:29.522 --> 00:01:32.492
you get 33 grams of fries.

00:01:32.492 --> 00:01:34.260
An order of fries,

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:37.330
total is 133 grams.

00:01:37.330 --> 00:01:38.932
How do we figure this out?

00:01:38.932 --> 00:01:41.067
You're paying 4 pence.

00:01:41.067 --> 00:01:42.302
3 per chip.

00:01:42.302 --> 00:01:44.904
We had 33 grams,

00:01:44.904 --> 00:01:48.408
equal a dollar for the Chris style, right?

00:01:48.408 --> 00:01:49.242
How much was it?

00:01:49.242 --> 00:01:53.613
£1.17 worth of chips in the burger.

00:01:53.613 --> 00:01:55.248
I think technically you're paying, like,

00:01:55.248 --> 00:01:58.418
an extra pound for this one
compared to the Beast burger.

00:01:58.418 --> 00:01:59.252
So you actually are,

00:01:59.252 --> 00:02:01.354
you are getting slightly
more than you pay for.

00:02:01.354 --> 00:02:02.622
[crew laughing]

00:02:02.622 --> 00:02:04.457
By 17p.

00:02:04.457 --> 00:02:06.092
So if our math is correct,

00:02:06.092 --> 00:02:08.695
it looks like on the Chris-style burger,

00:02:08.695 --> 00:02:12.298
per gram, each fry costs 3 cents.

00:02:12.298 --> 00:02:15.468
But if you get the
crinkle-cut fries on the side,

00:02:15.468 --> 00:02:18.138
each fry per gram costs 4 cents.

00:02:18.138 --> 00:02:20.573
So you're actually getting
a better deal on fries

00:02:20.573 --> 00:02:23.543
if you get them in the Chris
burger than separately.

00:02:23.543 --> 00:02:24.577
That's pretty nice.

00:02:24.577 --> 00:02:27.714
That took way longer than it
should have, and I'm sorry.

00:02:29.949 --> 00:02:31.117
Here is everything you'll find

00:02:31.117 --> 00:02:32.819
at a MrBeast Burger in the UK.

00:02:32.819 --> 00:02:35.221
Here's everything you can find in the US

00:02:35.221 --> 00:02:36.556
at a MrBeast Burger.

00:02:36.556 --> 00:02:37.790
There's a slight problem with our usual

00:02:37.790 --> 00:02:39.225
exclusives approach to this section,

00:02:39.225 --> 00:02:41.161
which is namely that
the UK doesn't have any.

00:02:41.161 --> 00:02:43.663
Everything on the menu here
is also available in the US.

00:02:43.663 --> 00:02:44.931
However, I do have a suspicion

00:02:44.931 --> 00:02:46.432
that some of these things
might be slightly different.

00:02:46.432 --> 00:02:47.567
So we're going to take a look.

00:02:47.567 --> 00:02:51.404
The only food exclusive
the US has over the UK

00:02:51.404 --> 00:02:56.242
is in the US, you can get a
MrBeast Impossible burger,

00:02:56.242 --> 00:02:58.244
made with the Impossible beef.

00:02:58.244 --> 00:03:00.780
That's because at the
time of recording this,

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:03.283
Impossible beef is not
available in the UK.

00:03:03.283 --> 00:03:04.751
That's because it
contains a key ingredient

00:03:04.751 --> 00:03:07.187
called soy leghemoglobin, aka heme.

00:03:07.187 --> 00:03:08.354
According to Impossible Foods,

00:03:08.354 --> 00:03:10.123
it's what makes some meats taste so meaty

00:03:10.123 --> 00:03:11.658
and creates the bleeding effect.

00:03:11.658 --> 00:03:13.493
Heme is classified as GRAS,

00:03:13.493 --> 00:03:15.528
generally recognized as safe, in the US.

00:03:15.528 --> 00:03:17.230
However, it does not
have regulatory approval

00:03:17.230 --> 00:03:18.932
in the UK or the EU just yet,

00:03:18.932 --> 00:03:21.034
although Impossible Foods do
say they're working on it.

00:03:21.034 --> 00:03:23.236
Besides that, the only
drink you can get in the US,

00:03:23.236 --> 00:03:25.405
can't get in the UK is Sierra Mist.

00:03:25.405 --> 00:03:27.407
UK, consider yourself lucky.

00:03:27.407 --> 00:03:29.876
Sierra Mist sucks.

00:03:29.876 --> 00:03:31.411
Start down this end with the classic.

00:03:31.411 --> 00:03:33.680
So, we have the MrBeast-style double.

00:03:33.680 --> 00:03:35.748
Two smashed patties. There's cheese,

00:03:35.748 --> 00:03:37.717
and then there's also pickles,

00:03:37.717 --> 00:03:40.920
chopped onions, some
mustard, and some ketchup.

00:03:40.920 --> 00:03:42.655
I love smash burgers,

00:03:42.655 --> 00:03:44.524
and I wish more places did smash burgers.

00:03:44.524 --> 00:03:47.427
You end up with these incredibly
crispy bits on the outside.

00:03:47.427 --> 00:03:50.496
Do you see this? That's just pure flavor.

00:03:51.764 --> 00:03:53.967
Mm. It's like beef candy. It's brilliant.

00:03:56.502 --> 00:03:57.770
Really good.

00:03:59.839 --> 00:04:01.741
That's pretty good. I do like this.

00:04:01.741 --> 00:04:03.876
I don't know if I would consider
this a smash patty, though.

00:04:03.876 --> 00:04:05.245
Tasty, juicy.

00:04:05.245 --> 00:04:06.846
Then of course we have
the Beast-style triple,

00:04:06.846 --> 00:04:10.817
which has the same toppings
but an extra beef patty.

00:04:10.817 --> 00:04:15.255
The Chris style. What up,
Chris? Whoever you are.

00:04:15.255 --> 00:04:17.924
Fries and bacon on the sandwich.

00:04:19.926 --> 00:04:21.394
Yeah, sort of just OK.

00:04:21.394 --> 00:04:23.529
So, this is the UK Chris-style burger.

00:04:23.529 --> 00:04:26.466
We have bun, we have
fries with some cheese,

00:04:26.466 --> 00:04:27.867
two beef patties,

00:04:27.867 --> 00:04:30.169
and on the bottom, just
one piece of bacon,

00:04:30.169 --> 00:04:32.105
and it's kind of that, like, cheap bacon.

00:04:32.105 --> 00:04:36.609
I associate this with buffets,
particularly when you go

00:04:36.609 --> 00:04:39.479
to an all-inclusive
resort in central Europe.

00:04:39.479 --> 00:04:41.114
I have to try this one. It looks so good.

00:04:44.183 --> 00:04:46.185
Mm-hmm. They didn't skimp on the fries.

00:04:46.185 --> 00:04:47.320
This thing is dense.

00:04:47.320 --> 00:04:49.222
So, this is the Karl's deluxe in the UK.

00:04:49.222 --> 00:04:50.890
What they've done is, for some reason,

00:04:50.890 --> 00:04:52.992
only flipped one of the burger buns,

00:04:52.992 --> 00:04:54.060
and then they've kind of used that to

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:55.762
create a grilled-cheese effect,

00:04:55.762 --> 00:04:57.497
which in the UK we call a cheese toastie.

00:04:57.497 --> 00:04:59.532
But then within that you have a beef patty

00:04:59.532 --> 00:05:01.634
with cheese on both sides

00:05:01.634 --> 00:05:03.002
as well as some grilled onions.

00:05:03.002 --> 00:05:05.004
The Chandler style.
There's nothing on this.

00:05:05.004 --> 00:05:06.706
Just burgers and cheese. Like,

00:05:06.706 --> 00:05:08.708
this food is made for 10-year-olds.

00:05:08.708 --> 00:05:10.910
Chandler, come on, man. What's going on?

00:05:10.910 --> 00:05:12.912
This is a very, very basic cheeseburger.

00:05:12.912 --> 00:05:17.817
It's just bun, cheese,
meat, cheese, meat, bun.

00:05:17.817 --> 00:05:19.452
It just feels a little bit
like when you're a little kid

00:05:19.452 --> 00:05:22.722
and all you want is a
hamburger with bread and beef.

00:05:25.525 --> 00:05:28.328
It's too dry. Come on,
Chandler. Live a little, man.

00:05:28.328 --> 00:05:31.297
Get some sauce involved. Maybe
even some pickles. Who knows?

00:05:31.297 --> 00:05:32.999
I don't know what the
Nashville tastes like

00:05:32.999 --> 00:05:34.167
over there in the UK.

00:05:34.167 --> 00:05:36.235
Sticking tenders in here. But this one,

00:05:37.770 --> 00:05:39.372
crunchy.

00:05:39.372 --> 00:05:40.640
And, of course, they also have the option

00:05:40.640 --> 00:05:42.542
of just a regular chicken sandwich.

00:05:44.944 --> 00:05:46.946
In a weird way, it kind of
reminds me of the McChicken,

00:05:46.946 --> 00:05:48.881
but, like, not as flavored.

00:05:48.881 --> 00:05:49.916
Any fast-food place,

00:05:49.916 --> 00:05:52.018
this would be the
dollar-menu chicken sandwich.

00:05:52.018 --> 00:05:53.920
This is $9?!

00:05:53.920 --> 00:05:55.421
Bro!

00:05:55.421 --> 00:05:57.123
No, no, no, no, no, no, no.

00:05:57.123 --> 00:06:00.426
This is the Nashville hot ... [laughs]

00:06:00.426 --> 00:06:03.629
This is so offensive to
the people of Nashville.

00:06:03.629 --> 00:06:05.965
People of Nashville, look away now,

00:06:05.965 --> 00:06:09.035
because the UK is about to
start another revolutionary war.

00:06:09.035 --> 00:06:12.171
So, the problem is, in the
UK, no one really knows

00:06:12.171 --> 00:06:14.307
what Nashville hot chicken
is supposed to look like.

00:06:14.307 --> 00:06:16.743
So fast-food chains can
get away with serving

00:06:16.743 --> 00:06:18.711
things like this, and
people don't know enough

00:06:18.711 --> 00:06:19.712
to call them out on it.

00:06:19.712 --> 00:06:20.947
What is this? Come on.

00:06:20.947 --> 00:06:22.749
What they've done, as far as I can tell,

00:06:22.749 --> 00:06:25.585
is just take standard chicken tenders,

00:06:25.585 --> 00:06:26.886
and then I think they've added

00:06:26.886 --> 00:06:29.622
maybe some of the seasoning
from the seasoned fries

00:06:29.622 --> 00:06:32.325
and then tried to pass that
off as a hot chicken sandwich.

00:06:34.327 --> 00:06:36.095
I'm not good with spice.

00:06:36.095 --> 00:06:37.930
There's nothing going on there.

00:06:37.930 --> 00:06:41.300
Zero Scovilles. That's not
Nashville, nor is it hot.

00:06:41.300 --> 00:06:43.169
You can also just get a
chicken-tender sandwich.

00:06:43.169 --> 00:06:44.937
I don't understand what the
difference is, particularly.

00:06:44.937 --> 00:06:46.139
This one has pickles on it.

00:06:46.139 --> 00:06:47.807
I just wish we could up
our chicken game in the UK.

00:06:47.807 --> 00:06:49.442
At the moment we're not
doing the best job of it.

00:06:49.442 --> 00:06:51.244
And unfortunately, MrBeast Burger

00:06:51.244 --> 00:06:53.212
is not our hero when it comes to that.

00:06:53.212 --> 00:06:55.982
So, Karl making a second
appearance on the menu.

00:06:55.982 --> 00:06:57.650
Apparently he has a grilled cheese

00:06:57.650 --> 00:07:00.253
that is two top buns, flipped over,

00:07:00.253 --> 00:07:01.521
with cheese smashed in the middle of it.

00:07:01.521 --> 00:07:03.055
This is 6 bucks.

00:07:03.055 --> 00:07:04.924
Oh, that's really funny.

00:07:04.924 --> 00:07:06.192
How much is a loaf of bread

00:07:06.192 --> 00:07:08.528
and a bunch of slices of American cheese?

00:07:08.528 --> 00:07:10.062
You can make, like, 20 of these.

00:07:10.062 --> 00:07:11.864
This thing looks quite sad.

00:07:11.864 --> 00:07:14.767
I think both of the buns
are supposed to be flipped.

00:07:14.767 --> 00:07:16.502
Quite interesting aesthetic.

00:07:17.503 --> 00:07:19.772
The cheese hasn't really melted properly,

00:07:19.772 --> 00:07:21.374
so it's not stuck to this.

00:07:21.374 --> 00:07:24.177
So it's just a very smooth,
shiny layer of cheese.

00:07:24.177 --> 00:07:26.379
These are your seasoned fries.

00:07:26.379 --> 00:07:27.447
Eh, you know.

00:07:29.415 --> 00:07:31.684
It does give me a slight
Nando's vibe to it,

00:07:31.684 --> 00:07:33.419
in terms of the heat level

00:07:33.419 --> 00:07:35.154
and some of the flavor profiles as well.

00:07:35.154 --> 00:07:37.290
Like, almost like a
peri-peri seasoning on this.

00:07:37.290 --> 00:07:39.225
MrBeast burger also offers

00:07:39.225 --> 00:07:41.461
something called Beast-style fries,

00:07:41.461 --> 00:07:43.463
which comes loaded with
caramelized onions,

00:07:43.463 --> 00:07:46.232
American cheese, pickles,
mayo, ketchup, and mustard.

00:07:46.232 --> 00:07:47.567
This is it right here.

00:07:47.567 --> 00:07:49.735
I don't know about this, guys.

00:07:49.735 --> 00:07:51.871
Maybe not the most visually appealing.

00:07:51.871 --> 00:07:55.208
However, I like the idea of
fries and pickles together.

00:07:55.208 --> 00:07:56.042
Cheers.

00:07:58.811 --> 00:08:00.713
I really like these.
These are really good.

00:08:00.713 --> 00:08:03.449
And one dessert, a chocolate chip cookie.

00:08:06.219 --> 00:08:07.520
This is a pretty good cookie.

00:08:07.520 --> 00:08:08.354
That's not bad.

00:08:10.490 --> 00:08:13.392
[crunching]

00:08:14.460 --> 00:08:18.231
[thudding]

00:08:18.231 --> 00:08:20.433
This is, like, pretty stale.

00:08:20.433 --> 00:08:22.368
Obviously we're a bit lacking
in exclusives in the UK,

00:08:22.368 --> 00:08:24.737
but maybe I can take some
preexisting menu items

00:08:24.737 --> 00:08:27.773
and combine them to create
a Harry-style burger.

00:08:27.773 --> 00:08:29.308
Trademark Harry Style.

00:08:29.308 --> 00:08:31.377
The Chandler style, which
was the very plain one.

00:08:31.377 --> 00:08:34.814
I'm going to take some of the
fake Nashville hot chicken,

00:08:34.814 --> 00:08:36.616
which is not very hot at all.

00:08:36.616 --> 00:08:38.217
Land that straight on top.

00:08:38.217 --> 00:08:39.886
Actually, I think this will benefit from

00:08:39.886 --> 00:08:41.287
some of the moisture on this bun,

00:08:41.287 --> 00:08:42.522
so I'm going to keep that as well.

00:08:42.522 --> 00:08:44.757
So, we're going for MrBeast-style fries,

00:08:44.757 --> 00:08:48.160
'cause I quite liked the Chris
style with the fries on it.

00:08:48.160 --> 00:08:49.795
Here goes. The Harry Styles.

00:08:53.699 --> 00:08:56.335
You know what? We might
have done something there.

00:08:56.335 --> 00:08:59.171
I actually don't mind the
combination of chicken and beef.

00:08:59.171 --> 00:09:00.573
I think that kind of works.

00:09:00.573 --> 00:09:01.674
Oh, God, what have I done?

00:09:01.674 --> 00:09:04.644
They were too preoccupied with
whether or not they could,

00:09:04.644 --> 00:09:06.345
they didn't stop to think about
whether or not they should.

00:09:06.345 --> 00:09:08.548
But honestly, don't
hate it. Give it a try.

00:09:08.548 --> 00:09:10.716
So, for my signature burger,

00:09:10.716 --> 00:09:11.551
here's what I'm going to do.

00:09:11.551 --> 00:09:12.485
I think this is a really good idea.

00:09:12.485 --> 00:09:13.519
I'm excited about this.

00:09:13.519 --> 00:09:16.222
I'm going to take a Karl's grilled cheese

00:09:16.222 --> 00:09:19.158
and a second Karl's grilled cheese,

00:09:19.158 --> 00:09:21.561
and mine's going to be
the Beast-style burger,

00:09:21.561 --> 00:09:24.230
but instead of buns,
it's two grilled cheeses.

00:09:24.230 --> 00:09:27.533
Check this out. Grilled cheese.

00:09:27.533 --> 00:09:29.735
Double patties. Should
I put fries on it too?

00:09:29.735 --> 00:09:30.903
Yuelei: Yeah.
Joe: Why not?

00:09:30.903 --> 00:09:32.238
We'll make it a Chris style,

00:09:32.238 --> 00:09:36.275
because these fries have all
the seasoning and stuff on it.

00:09:36.275 --> 00:09:37.143
They have all the ketchup

00:09:37.143 --> 00:09:38.945
and have all the sauces
and everything on it.

00:09:38.945 --> 00:09:40.479
Ooh, and there's caramelized onions too.

00:09:40.479 --> 00:09:42.848
OK, there. They got the Beast burger,

00:09:42.848 --> 00:09:44.584
or, the Beast-style burger.

00:09:44.584 --> 00:09:46.619
This is the Joe-style burger.

00:09:46.619 --> 00:09:48.087
We can also call this,

00:09:48.087 --> 00:09:50.256
I've been told I look like old MrBeast.

00:09:50.256 --> 00:09:53.326
So this could be old-MrBeast-style burger,

00:09:53.326 --> 00:09:56.662
or MrBeast-with-no-serotonin burger,

00:09:56.662 --> 00:09:58.331
or I-kind-of-look-like-that-guy-

00:09:58.331 --> 00:09:59.732
from-"Game-of-Thrones" burger.

00:09:59.732 --> 00:10:01.801
So whatever you want to
call it, but here we go.

00:10:01.801 --> 00:10:03.402
Oh, man, this, I'm excited about this.

00:10:03.402 --> 00:10:04.804
Look how good this looks!

00:10:07.540 --> 00:10:09.308
I'm an absolute genius.

00:10:09.308 --> 00:10:10.876
This is so good.

00:10:10.876 --> 00:10:12.011
Mm.

00:10:12.011 --> 00:10:13.746
Oh, man!

00:10:13.746 --> 00:10:16.382
Jimmy, put this on the menu.

00:10:16.382 --> 00:10:18.384
Put this on the menu.

00:10:18.384 --> 00:10:19.218
One more.

00:10:20.620 --> 00:10:22.622
I really want to keep eating this.

00:10:22.622 --> 00:10:24.290
One more bite. I'm sorry.

00:10:27.560 --> 00:10:30.863
Here's a US Beast-style
double burger combo.

00:10:30.863 --> 00:10:34.200
Over here, it will run you $15.29.

00:10:34.200 --> 00:10:36.769
That same combo in the UK is £14.99.

00:10:38.938 --> 00:10:39.772
Yes.

00:10:41.073 --> 00:10:42.975
Leon's having none of it.

00:10:42.975 --> 00:10:44.310
But what about the delivery fees?

00:10:44.310 --> 00:10:46.912
Using the MrBeast Burger site, in the US,

00:10:46.912 --> 00:10:50.182
the same combo with tax,
delivery fees, and tip

00:10:50.182 --> 00:10:52.885
costs $28.72,

00:10:52.885 --> 00:10:56.122
increasing the cost by 87.8%.

00:10:56.122 --> 00:10:56.956
Oof!

00:10:56.956 --> 00:10:59.725
So, if possible, you may
want to go pick up your food.

00:10:59.725 --> 00:11:01.260
It's a similar deal here in the UK.

00:11:01.260 --> 00:11:02.662
We checked this order on Deliveroo,

00:11:02.662 --> 00:11:04.964
and they charge a £2.49 delivery fee

00:11:04.964 --> 00:11:07.166
and a £2.05 service charge,

00:11:07.166 --> 00:11:09.201
which jacks the price
up by almost a third.

00:11:09.201 --> 00:11:10.503
One big difference worth pointing out

00:11:10.503 --> 00:11:12.104
is the tipping culture
in the UK and the US.

00:11:12.104 --> 00:11:14.006
It's much less common to tip in the UK

00:11:14.006 --> 00:11:15.207
than it is in America.

00:11:15.207 --> 00:11:17.109
In the UK, if you go to a
restaurant for some food,

00:11:17.109 --> 00:11:18.944
it's usually common to give maybe a 10%

00:11:18.944 --> 00:11:22.415
or a 12.5% service charge if
the service has been good.

00:11:22.415 --> 00:11:23.783
But you can even opt out of that

00:11:23.783 --> 00:11:24.617
if you don't want to pay it.

00:11:24.617 --> 00:11:26.152
Particularly where delivery is concerned,

00:11:26.152 --> 00:11:28.220
I think tipping is even
less common in the UK.

00:11:28.220 --> 00:11:29.455
I got a notification, actually,

00:11:29.455 --> 00:11:30.723
on my Deliveroo app the other day

00:11:30.723 --> 00:11:32.792
to say that 6% of people in my area

00:11:32.792 --> 00:11:34.493
have been tipping their drivers recently.

00:11:34.493 --> 00:11:36.062
So that's six out of every 100 people

00:11:36.062 --> 00:11:37.196
are tipping a delivery driver.

00:11:37.196 --> 00:11:38.297
When I say that we don't have as much

00:11:38.297 --> 00:11:39.632
of a tipping culture in the UK,

00:11:39.632 --> 00:11:41.067
it's not that we're really stingy.

00:11:41.067 --> 00:11:43.069
We just generally have a
much higher minimum wage

00:11:43.069 --> 00:11:44.570
in the UK than you do in the US,

00:11:44.570 --> 00:11:46.072
so there's less reliance on tips

00:11:46.072 --> 00:11:48.107
to make ends meet for
service-industry staff.

00:11:50.342 --> 00:11:52.111
We thought we'd take a look back over

00:11:52.111 --> 00:11:53.612
the story of MrBeast Burger

00:11:53.612 --> 00:11:55.548
to give you all some context.

00:11:55.548 --> 00:11:58.117
It all started with a
YouTube video back in 2020,

00:11:58.117 --> 00:12:00.986
in which MrBeast opened a
single drive-through restaurant

00:12:00.986 --> 00:12:02.154
where the food is free,

00:12:02.154 --> 00:12:05.491
and customers would even
get free money for visiting.

00:12:05.491 --> 00:12:07.093
Obviously thousands of people showed up,

00:12:07.093 --> 00:12:09.695
and the video got over 100 million views.

00:12:09.695 --> 00:12:12.131
At the end of the video, MrBeast announced

00:12:12.131 --> 00:12:14.867
MrBeast Burger, his chain of burgers,

00:12:14.867 --> 00:12:17.737
which was available across
the US for delivery.

00:12:17.737 --> 00:12:19.438
He partnered with Virtual Dining Concepts,

00:12:19.438 --> 00:12:21.474
a platform which matches brands
with existing restaurants

00:12:21.474 --> 00:12:23.609
and kitchens to prepare and deliver food.

00:12:23.609 --> 00:12:24.777
By using existing kitchens,

00:12:24.777 --> 00:12:26.612
MrBeast Burger was able to expand rapidly,

00:12:26.612 --> 00:12:29.315
opening 300 locations in
the US in the first week,

00:12:29.315 --> 00:12:31.817
followed by more in the UK
and Canada shortly after.

00:12:31.817 --> 00:12:33.686
For context, it took McDonald's six years

00:12:33.686 --> 00:12:35.488
to open 300 US locations.

00:12:35.488 --> 00:12:37.957
You can start to see why
brands love virtual kitchens.

00:12:37.957 --> 00:12:40.359
At the time of filming
this, there is only one

00:12:40.359 --> 00:12:42.561
brick-and-mortar MrBeast Burger location,

00:12:42.561 --> 00:12:45.731
recently opened in New
Jersey's American Dream mall.

00:12:45.731 --> 00:12:48.968
At the grand opening, over
100,000 fans showed up,

00:12:48.968 --> 00:12:50.870
some waiting in line all night.

00:12:50.870 --> 00:12:54.039
It was a massive success,
captured by Colin and Samir,

00:12:54.039 --> 00:12:55.775
who documented the entire day.

00:12:55.775 --> 00:12:57.543
According to the doc,
at the grand opening,

00:12:57.543 --> 00:13:01.380
MrBeast Burger sold 6,212 burgers

00:13:01.380 --> 00:13:03.916
and broke the world record by three times.

00:13:03.916 --> 00:13:05.684
Guinness World Records has asked for proof

00:13:05.684 --> 00:13:07.019
and at the time of this recording

00:13:07.019 --> 00:13:08.454
has not made it official.

00:13:08.454 --> 00:13:10.055
But it hasn't all been sunshine and roses.

00:13:10.055 --> 00:13:11.223
Pretty much anybody can apply

00:13:11.223 --> 00:13:13.292
to become a virtual
kitchen for MrBeast Burger.

00:13:13.292 --> 00:13:15.327
There's a form on the Virtual
Dining Concepts website

00:13:15.327 --> 00:13:16.228
where you can tell them

00:13:16.228 --> 00:13:17.997
which facilities you have in the kitchen.

00:13:17.997 --> 00:13:20.699
So if you have a fryer,
a flattop, and a fridge

00:13:20.699 --> 00:13:23.035
and you normally make fried food,

00:13:23.035 --> 00:13:26.005
even if you just have a single location,

00:13:26.005 --> 00:13:27.373
you can cook MrBeast Burger.

00:13:27.373 --> 00:13:28.507
That's all it takes.

00:13:28.507 --> 00:13:30.242
A fryer, a flattop, and a fridge.

00:13:30.242 --> 00:13:32.978
I mean, you can buy a
deep-fryer for pretty cheap,

00:13:32.978 --> 00:13:34.780
and I feel like you could
install a flattop on

00:13:34.780 --> 00:13:37.650
pretty much any kitchen, and
everyone's got a fridge, so,

00:13:37.650 --> 00:13:38.818
I feel like I could probably cook

00:13:38.818 --> 00:13:40.219
MrBeast Burger if I wanted to.

00:13:40.219 --> 00:13:43.122
A wide variety of restaurants
acting as virtual kitchens

00:13:43.122 --> 00:13:46.225
has led to a slew of quality-control
issues for the chain.

00:13:46.225 --> 00:13:48.394
The food is coming from
all types of restaurants

00:13:48.394 --> 00:13:49.662
independent of each other,

00:13:49.662 --> 00:13:51.931
so what you're getting may
be a bit of a crapshoot.

00:13:51.931 --> 00:13:54.600
So we went ahead and got MrBeast Burger

00:13:54.600 --> 00:13:56.435
from a second location.

00:13:56.435 --> 00:13:58.871
First, the Chandler style. [grunts]

00:13:58.871 --> 00:14:01.073
And I have to say, it
looks pretty good, right?

00:14:01.073 --> 00:14:02.641
Very impressed.

00:14:02.641 --> 00:14:07.479
The Chandler style from restaurant No. 2.

00:14:07.479 --> 00:14:09.315
OK, the first thing I noticed

00:14:09.315 --> 00:14:11.250
is the burger's not wrapped.

00:14:12.985 --> 00:14:14.019
Is that OK?

00:14:14.019 --> 00:14:15.454
It's bigger.

00:14:15.454 --> 00:14:17.690
But, I mean, that's clearly different bun.

00:14:17.690 --> 00:14:19.291
This is more of a smash patty.

00:14:19.291 --> 00:14:21.393
How it's really almost paper-thin,

00:14:21.393 --> 00:14:24.697
where this just looks like tiny burgers.

00:14:24.697 --> 00:14:25.865
Chandler burger, right?

00:14:27.466 --> 00:14:30.035
Mm, the cheese makes this one.

00:14:34.206 --> 00:14:37.443
No. It's a different quality of meat too.

00:14:38.310 --> 00:14:41.013
I think that this actually
is pertinent information.

00:14:41.013 --> 00:14:42.715
This is from a restaurant in Glendale.

00:14:42.715 --> 00:14:45.718
This was from the Buca di
Beppo's at Universal Studios.

00:14:46.585 --> 00:14:47.620
Hot chicken sandwich.

00:14:47.620 --> 00:14:50.055
All right, again, place
No. 1, the place we like.

00:14:50.055 --> 00:14:51.257
It's saying it's Nashville,

00:14:51.257 --> 00:14:52.725
but instead of doing chicken sandwiches,

00:14:52.725 --> 00:14:54.493
they're doing chicken-tender sandwiches.

00:14:54.493 --> 00:14:56.295
Bit of a disparity between A and B.

00:14:59.331 --> 00:15:01.800
Mm-hmm. Not that crispy. Spicy?

00:15:01.800 --> 00:15:04.136
That's disappointing.
There's no spice to that.

00:15:04.136 --> 00:15:05.004
I mean, this one.

00:15:08.107 --> 00:15:09.808
Yeah. Mm!

00:15:09.808 --> 00:15:11.410
That, however, is much better.

00:15:11.410 --> 00:15:13.178
Despite some of these
quality discrepancies,

00:15:13.178 --> 00:15:15.581
MrBeast Burger shows no sign
of slowing down its growth.

00:15:15.581 --> 00:15:17.249
Earlier this year, MrBeast
tweeted that the brand

00:15:17.249 --> 00:15:19.985
has already shared over
$100 million of revenue

00:15:19.985 --> 00:15:21.387
with restaurants across America.

00:15:21.387 --> 00:15:22.988
When he says shared, it
means that not all the money

00:15:22.988 --> 00:15:23.956
is going to MrBeast,

00:15:23.956 --> 00:15:25.858
nor is all the money
going to the restaurants.

00:15:25.858 --> 00:15:27.493
The restaurants will
obviously take a large cut,

00:15:27.493 --> 00:15:28.560
but then some of the money will go

00:15:28.560 --> 00:15:29.795
to Virtual Dining Concepts,

00:15:29.795 --> 00:15:31.630
and I'm sure some of it is
going to MrBeast as well.

00:15:31.630 --> 00:15:33.832
For example, one restaurant
in Dallas, Texas, claimed

00:15:33.832 --> 00:15:37.202
it sold $7,000 worth of MrBeast
Burgers in a single day.

00:15:37.202 --> 00:15:38.537
MrBeast actually once described

00:15:38.537 --> 00:15:40.306
the launch of MrBeast Burger as a gamble,

00:15:40.306 --> 00:15:42.141
but so far it's looking
like that gamble paid off.

00:15:42.141 --> 00:15:43.976
We actually collected
today's order in-store,

00:15:43.976 --> 00:15:45.477
and I had to kind of place the order there

00:15:45.477 --> 00:15:46.545
by showing the guy my phone,

00:15:46.545 --> 00:15:48.080
and he kind of tapped
it all through for me.

00:15:48.080 --> 00:15:49.248
He was actually kind of surprised

00:15:49.248 --> 00:15:50.349
at how much the burgers cost.

00:15:50.349 --> 00:15:51.850
He said they looked quite expensive.

00:15:51.850 --> 00:15:53.585
I guess it just means that he wasn't aware

00:15:53.585 --> 00:15:55.187
of how many fees are being added on

00:15:55.187 --> 00:15:56.989
so that either the delivery platform

00:15:56.989 --> 00:15:59.558
or Virtual Dining Concepts can
get a fair cut of the profit.

00:16:01.794 --> 00:16:04.496
It seems like the nutritional
stats for MrBeast Burger

00:16:04.496 --> 00:16:07.099
are actually the same
in the US and the UK.

00:16:07.099 --> 00:16:10.336
A Beast style with double
patties is 950 calories,

00:16:10.336 --> 00:16:13.539
66 grams of fat, 23
grams of saturated fat,

00:16:13.539 --> 00:16:16.842
43 grams of carbs, 41 grams of protein,

00:16:16.842 --> 00:16:20.245
and 1,840 milligrams of sodium.

00:16:20.245 --> 00:16:22.681
Note that is 80% of your daily sodium.

00:16:22.681 --> 00:16:23.849
Make it a Beast-style triple,

00:16:23.849 --> 00:16:25.985
and the calories go up to 1,160,

00:16:25.985 --> 00:16:27.753
which is over half of
your daily allowance.

00:16:27.753 --> 00:16:29.221
What you really have to look out for here

00:16:29.221 --> 00:16:31.223
is the saturated fat. A Beast-style triple

00:16:31.223 --> 00:16:34.460
contains 150% of your
daily recommended intake.

00:16:34.460 --> 00:16:36.929
Bump it up to a Beast-style
double burger combo

00:16:36.929 --> 00:16:39.498
with unseasoned fries
and a can of Sierra Mist.

00:16:39.498 --> 00:16:43.602
Gives you a grand total of 1,330 calories.

00:16:43.602 --> 00:16:45.270
Bump it up to a triple,

00:16:46.138 --> 00:16:50.442
and you hit 1,540 calories.

00:16:50.442 --> 00:16:52.378
Comparing the Beast-style burger

00:16:52.378 --> 00:16:54.079
to other fast-food-chain burgers,

00:16:54.079 --> 00:16:57.716
MrBeast, calorie-wise, lands about here.

00:16:57.716 --> 00:17:00.552
It's pretty high up there.
But good news for Jimmy:

00:17:00.552 --> 00:17:02.388
No one in America cares.

00:17:02.688 --> 00:17:04.156
Harry: From calorie
count to portion sizes,

00:17:04.156 --> 00:17:06.258
We wanted to find out all the
differences between Red Bull

00:17:06.258 --> 00:17:07.893
in the UK and the US.

00:17:07.893 --> 00:17:09.395
This is Food Wars.

00:17:13.132 --> 00:17:13.966
In the UK,

00:17:13.966 --> 00:17:15.934
Red Bull comes in three portion sizes:

00:17:15.934 --> 00:17:18.437
A 250-milliliter can,

00:17:18.437 --> 00:17:20.706
a 355-milliliter can,

00:17:20.706 --> 00:17:23.509
and a 473-milliliter can.

00:17:23.509 --> 00:17:24.343
In the US,

00:17:24.343 --> 00:17:27.246
our Red Bull cans come in four sizes,

00:17:27.246 --> 00:17:30.916
8.4 fluid ounces, or 250 milliliters,

00:17:30.916 --> 00:17:34.119
12 fluid ounces, or 355 milliliters,

00:17:34.119 --> 00:17:38.290
16 fluid ounces, or 473 milliliters.

00:17:38.290 --> 00:17:39.691
And the biggest one,

00:17:39.691 --> 00:17:44.463
20 fluid ounces — yo!
— or 591 milliliters.

00:17:46.532 --> 00:17:48.700
That means our US largest size

00:17:48.700 --> 00:17:52.004
is 30% bigger than the UK's.

00:17:52.004 --> 00:17:52.938
Harry: Let's see if we're actually getting

00:17:52.938 --> 00:17:55.374
our 473 milliliters' worth.

00:17:57.176 --> 00:18:00.245
Actually, looks slightly more than 473.

00:18:00.245 --> 00:18:02.247
Maybe we're getting
even more for our money.

00:18:02.247 --> 00:18:04.016
The largest single item
by volume in the UK

00:18:04.016 --> 00:18:07.486
is a 24-pack of our 355-milliliter cans.

00:18:07.486 --> 00:18:09.922
That totals 8,520 milliliters,

00:18:09.922 --> 00:18:12.391
which is around 288 fluid ounces.

00:18:12.391 --> 00:18:13.792
While we do have a larger can on offer,

00:18:13.792 --> 00:18:15.327
that only comes as part of a 12-pack,

00:18:15.327 --> 00:18:18.630
meaning that the total is
only 5,664 milliliters,

00:18:18.630 --> 00:18:20.933
which is less than the
24-pack of this one.

00:18:20.933 --> 00:18:24.236
In the US, our largest
Red Bull item is a 24-pack

00:18:24.236 --> 00:18:26.738
of 12-fluid-ounce cans.

00:18:26.738 --> 00:18:29.108
I was unable to get my hands on it,

00:18:29.108 --> 00:18:31.844
but it is the same liquid
amount as the UK's largest.

00:18:31.844 --> 00:18:36.415
Our closest second is a
12-pack of 24-fluid-ounce cans.

00:18:38.350 --> 00:18:40.385
Here are all the Red Bull
products you'll find in the UK,

00:18:40.385 --> 00:18:42.354
some of which you won't find in the US.

00:18:42.354 --> 00:18:44.289
Here are all the Red Bull items in the US

00:18:44.289 --> 00:18:45.657
you won't find in the UK.

00:18:45.657 --> 00:18:47.926
So technically we have eight
Red Bull products in the UK.

00:18:47.926 --> 00:18:48.861
We have the normal one,

00:18:48.861 --> 00:18:49.995
we have the sugar-free one,

00:18:49.995 --> 00:18:51.029
we have the zero one,

00:18:51.029 --> 00:18:53.332
red, green, yellow, orange, and white.

00:18:53.332 --> 00:18:54.199
Some of these are seasonal

00:18:54.199 --> 00:18:55.234
and will rotate in and out,

00:18:55.234 --> 00:18:56.568
so it's a little bit
tricky to keep track of

00:18:56.568 --> 00:18:57.469
exactly what's on offer,

00:18:57.469 --> 00:18:58.704
but this is what we could get today.

00:18:58.704 --> 00:18:59.538
In addition to this,

00:18:59.538 --> 00:19:00.873
we have a couple of sugar-free exclusives,

00:19:00.873 --> 00:19:02.541
which technically adds to the total.

00:19:02.541 --> 00:19:03.542
From what I can tell,

00:19:03.542 --> 00:19:05.677
these three flavors are
exclusive to the US,

00:19:05.677 --> 00:19:07.846
and you can't find them in the UK.

00:19:07.846 --> 00:19:10.749
First, we have the blue edition,

00:19:10.749 --> 00:19:13.051
which is blueberry flavored,

00:19:13.051 --> 00:19:14.419
and we got the peach flavored,

00:19:14.419 --> 00:19:16.688
which I believe is flavored peach,

00:19:16.688 --> 00:19:18.891
and the winter edition,

00:19:18.891 --> 00:19:20.859
which is what flavor?

00:19:20.859 --> 00:19:22.661
Fig apple? Hmm.

00:19:22.661 --> 00:19:24.596
Now both countries have
the coconut flavor,

00:19:24.596 --> 00:19:26.098
but from what I can tell online,

00:19:26.098 --> 00:19:28.967
we also have the coconut
sugar-free flavor.

00:19:28.967 --> 00:19:31.136
I actually couldn't even
find sugar-free versions

00:19:31.136 --> 00:19:32.971
of the red one or the orange one.

00:19:32.971 --> 00:19:35.174
I did find a sugar-free
yellow one, though.

00:19:35.174 --> 00:19:36.041
You can tell it's sugar-free

00:19:36.041 --> 00:19:38.877
because it's got this blue
sugar-free band there,

00:19:38.877 --> 00:19:40.078
blue sugar-free label there,

00:19:40.078 --> 00:19:41.980
and also the tab is blue.

00:19:41.980 --> 00:19:42.915
That's quite fun.

00:19:42.915 --> 00:19:44.650
While it's not technically a UK exclusive,

00:19:44.650 --> 00:19:46.718
I did find this one while
I was hunting for Red Bull,

00:19:46.718 --> 00:19:48.220
I think it's imported from Thailand,

00:19:48.220 --> 00:19:50.589
and it's a
cold-brew-coffee-flavored Red Bull,

00:19:50.589 --> 00:19:52.090
which sounds pretty intense.

00:19:52.090 --> 00:19:54.026
Because there aren't too many exclusives

00:19:54.026 --> 00:19:55.494
between the US and the UK,

00:19:55.494 --> 00:19:56.562
I'm going to do a lightning round

00:19:56.562 --> 00:19:59.898
of every flavor I can get
my hands on here in the US.

00:19:59.898 --> 00:20:01.600
Couldn't find any of
the sugar-free options,

00:20:01.600 --> 00:20:02.701
but I know they are available,

00:20:02.701 --> 00:20:03.702
at least online,

00:20:03.702 --> 00:20:06.238
and also I got Red Bull Zero

00:20:06.238 --> 00:20:08.840
and sugar-free Red Bull.

00:20:08.840 --> 00:20:11.243
So let's do a quick lightning
round of each flavor.

00:20:11.243 --> 00:20:12.077
Ready?

00:20:12.077 --> 00:20:15.247
The issue here is that I
don't drink energy drinks.

00:20:15.247 --> 00:20:17.316
I don't like the taste of Red Bull.

00:20:17.316 --> 00:20:18.617
They make me feel weird.

00:20:18.617 --> 00:20:22.120
I drink tea if I need a bit of
a caffeine hit, and that's it.

00:20:22.120 --> 00:20:24.456
But apparently I have to
taste-test all of these,

00:20:24.456 --> 00:20:26.158
so wish me luck.

00:20:27.259 --> 00:20:29.661
I am not happy about this.

00:20:29.661 --> 00:20:33.398
Regular Red Bull flavors, but sugar-free.

00:20:33.398 --> 00:20:34.900
I don't think I've ever
had a sugar-free one.

00:20:34.900 --> 00:20:35.734
Maybe I should.

00:20:35.734 --> 00:20:37.502
because I did drink an
alarming amount of Red Bull

00:20:37.502 --> 00:20:38.570
when I was younger,

00:20:38.570 --> 00:20:43.242
and maybe a sugar-free option
would've been a good idea.

00:20:44.409 --> 00:20:45.244
You know.

00:20:49.014 --> 00:20:50.983
A little side-by-side action.

