00:29:59.764 --> 00:30:00.932
That's actually kind of a Food Wars first,

00:30:00.932 --> 00:30:02.300
so it doesn't happen often.

00:30:04.669 --> 00:30:05.904
In the UK, our standard Red Bull

00:30:05.904 --> 00:30:07.839
contains the following ingredients:

00:30:07.839 --> 00:30:11.776
water, sucrose, glucose,
acidifier citric acid,

00:30:11.776 --> 00:30:13.545
taurine, sodium carbonates

00:30:13.545 --> 00:30:17.916
and magnesium carbonate, caffeine,
niacin, pantothenic acid,

00:30:17.916 --> 00:30:21.519
vitamin B6, vitamin
B12 flavorings, colors,

00:30:21.519 --> 00:30:24.055
caramel and riboflavin,
and carbon dioxide.

00:30:24.055 --> 00:30:26.257
Our Red Bull in the US
contains pretty much

00:30:26.257 --> 00:30:27.158
the same stuff.

00:30:27.158 --> 00:30:32.030
Carbonated water, sucrose,
glucose, citric acid, taurine,

00:30:32.030 --> 00:30:35.934
sodium bicarbonate, magnesium
carbonate, caffeine.

00:30:37.335 --> 00:30:39.103
Niacinamide.

00:30:39.103 --> 00:30:43.975
Calcium pantothenate.

00:30:43.975 --> 00:30:47.312
Pyridoxine HCI.

00:30:47.312 --> 00:30:49.347
Vitamin B12, natural
and artificial flavors.

00:30:49.347 --> 00:30:50.181
All right.

00:30:50.181 --> 00:30:52.517
The vitamins have different
names, but it's all the same.

00:30:52.517 --> 00:30:54.519
You may notice the ingredient
taurine on that list.

00:30:54.519 --> 00:30:55.887
Now, taurine has been the subject of

00:30:55.887 --> 00:30:58.323
inaccurate rumors on
the internet for years.

00:30:58.323 --> 00:31:00.024
Taurine has an association with bulls,

00:31:00.024 --> 00:31:02.460
drawing its name from the
Latin word for bull, taurus.

00:31:02.460 --> 00:31:03.528
Some people run with this

00:31:03.528 --> 00:31:06.364
and falsely claim that
it's code for bull semen.

00:31:06.364 --> 00:31:07.899
The name actually comes from the fact that

00:31:07.899 --> 00:31:10.568
taurine was first isolated from ox bile.

00:31:10.568 --> 00:31:14.472
OK, the good news is that
there's no ox spit in Red Bull,

00:31:14.472 --> 00:31:17.408
as food producers have used a
synthetic version of taurine

00:31:17.408 --> 00:31:19.944
that isn't derived from animals.

00:31:19.944 --> 00:31:22.313
It also means that Red Bull
is suitable for vegans.

00:31:22.313 --> 00:31:25.016
One study found that exposing
human teeth to energy drinks

00:31:25.016 --> 00:31:26.918
for 15 minutes, four times a day,

00:31:26.918 --> 00:31:28.353
resulted in a significant

00:31:28.353 --> 00:31:30.455
and irreversible loss of tooth enamel.

00:31:30.455 --> 00:31:31.489
The study also noted that

00:31:31.489 --> 00:31:34.058
energy drinks were twice as
harmful as regular soft drinks

00:31:34.058 --> 00:31:34.893
to tooth enamel.

00:31:34.893 --> 00:31:36.227
As the study in rats found,

00:31:36.227 --> 00:31:38.830
chronic intake of Red
Bull may cause a decline

00:31:38.830 --> 00:31:40.031
in kidney function.

00:31:40.031 --> 00:31:42.233
However, these results
have not been replicated

00:31:42.233 --> 00:31:43.501
in human studies.

00:31:43.501 --> 00:31:46.571
But any excuse to see my
boys, the dancing rats.

00:31:51.009 --> 00:31:53.378
Red Bull in the UK contains 110 calories

00:31:53.378 --> 00:31:55.480
per 250-milliliter can.

00:31:55.480 --> 00:31:58.249
One of these cans also
contains 27 grams of sugar.

00:31:58.249 --> 00:31:59.217
According to their website,

00:31:59.217 --> 00:32:00.618
this is actually a similar amount of sugar

00:32:00.618 --> 00:32:02.921
to what you might find
in say, apple juice.

00:32:02.921 --> 00:32:04.956
Both sugar-free Red Bull and Red Bull Zero

00:32:04.956 --> 00:32:09.093
contain 10 calories per
this 8.4-fluid-ounce can.

00:32:09.093 --> 00:32:12.797
Sugar-free replace their sugar with

00:32:13.998 --> 00:32:17.669
acesulfame potassium and aspartame.

00:32:17.669 --> 00:32:19.671
Red Bull Zero replaced sugar with

00:32:20.571 --> 00:32:24.042
acesulfame potassium K and sucralose.

00:32:24.042 --> 00:32:25.877
Acesulfame potassium, or Ace K,

00:32:25.877 --> 00:32:27.845
which is Red Bull's
zero-calorie sweetener,

00:32:27.845 --> 00:32:29.981
has had its share of
controversy over the years.

00:32:29.981 --> 00:32:30.782
Although, to be fair,

00:32:30.782 --> 00:32:33.685
a lot of the studies this came
from were done in the 1970s.

00:32:33.685 --> 00:32:35.820
This has led to the validity
being called into question

00:32:35.820 --> 00:32:36.754
in recent years.

00:32:36.754 --> 00:32:38.523
According to Healthline.com,

00:32:38.523 --> 00:32:41.192
in 1996, the Center for
Science in the Public Interest

00:32:41.192 --> 00:32:43.594
urged the FDA to do more testing on Ace K

00:32:43.594 --> 00:32:45.563
before allowing its
inclusion in soft drinks.

00:32:45.563 --> 00:32:48.666
The CSPI go on to say that there are

00:32:48.666 --> 00:32:50.768
health concerns associated with a Ace K,

00:32:50.768 --> 00:32:53.104
including cancer, hormone disruption,

00:32:53.104 --> 00:32:55.540
and risks to pregnant people.

00:32:55.540 --> 00:32:57.075
There's also a study that determined

00:32:57.075 --> 00:32:59.444
the chronic use of Ace K in male mice

00:32:59.444 --> 00:33:01.913
was linked to possible
changes in brain function

00:33:01.913 --> 00:33:03.348
over a period of 40 weeks.

00:33:03.348 --> 00:33:05.049
Yeah, I believe that it's been 40 minutes,

00:33:05.049 --> 00:33:07.752
and my brain is just.

00:33:07.752 --> 00:33:09.587
One of the perceived
benefits of drinking Red Bull

00:33:09.587 --> 00:33:11.289
is that it's supposed
to give people a boost

00:33:11.289 --> 00:33:12.323
through its caffeine content.

00:33:12.323 --> 00:33:15.760
A 250-milliliter can contains
80 milligrams of caffeine.

00:33:15.760 --> 00:33:16.661
But is that a lot?

00:33:16.661 --> 00:33:17.996
Compared to other soft drinks?

00:33:17.996 --> 00:33:18.830
Yeah.

00:33:18.830 --> 00:33:22.100
A 12-ounce can of Coke contains
34 milligrams of caffeine.

00:33:22.100 --> 00:33:24.035
That's less than half
the amount of caffeine

00:33:24.035 --> 00:33:26.437
and almost double the amount
of fluid as this Red Bull.

00:33:26.437 --> 00:33:27.672
A 12-ounce can of Mountain Dew

00:33:27.672 --> 00:33:30.675
contains slightly more,
with 55 milligrams.

00:33:30.675 --> 00:33:33.211
If we compare Red Bull to
another popular energy drink,

00:33:33.211 --> 00:33:36.814
Monster, you'll find that
they actually have the same

00:33:36.814 --> 00:33:38.750
caffeine content per 100 milliliters,

00:33:38.750 --> 00:33:40.385
which is 32 milligrams.

00:33:40.385 --> 00:33:41.652
Although Monster cans tend to be bigger,

00:33:41.652 --> 00:33:43.454
so you are getting more caffeine in total.

00:33:43.454 --> 00:33:44.589
The caffeine amount, however,

00:33:44.589 --> 00:33:47.792
can be a bit underwhelming when
compared to regular coffee.

00:33:47.792 --> 00:33:50.495
An eight-ounce, 237-milligram

00:33:50.495 --> 00:33:54.866
brewed coffee contains on average
95 milligrams of caffeine,

00:33:54.866 --> 00:33:58.603
and a double shot of espresso
contains 125 milligrams.

00:33:58.603 --> 00:33:59.637
One issue comes from the fact that

00:33:59.637 --> 00:34:01.873
some people will consider Red
Bull to be more like a soda,

00:34:01.873 --> 00:34:03.641
and therefore might drink
higher quantities of it.

00:34:03.641 --> 00:34:05.610
So is it possible to overdose on Red Bull?

00:34:05.610 --> 00:34:08.179
Yeah, although highly unlikely.

00:34:08.179 --> 00:34:10.715
Caffeine-related deaths have
been found in individuals

00:34:10.715 --> 00:34:13.518
that intake somewhere
between 3 and 5 grams —

00:34:13.518 --> 00:34:16.788
not milligrams, grams —
of caffeine in one day.

00:34:16.788 --> 00:34:18.656
That would be 40 of these.

00:34:18.656 --> 00:34:21.092
I feel like your bladder
would explode first.

00:34:21.092 --> 00:34:22.593
Although apparently, that
wasn't enough caffeine

00:34:22.593 --> 00:34:23.461
for some people.

00:34:23.461 --> 00:34:26.397
In 2014, Red Bull was sued
in a class-action lawsuit

00:34:26.397 --> 00:34:27.765
around false advertising.

00:34:27.765 --> 00:34:30.068
Remember the ad campaign
"Red Bull gives you wings"?

00:34:30.068 --> 00:34:31.235
Well, it doesn't.

00:34:31.235 --> 00:34:32.336
False advertising.

00:34:32.336 --> 00:34:35.206
Back then, Red Bull did
say in its marketing

00:34:35.206 --> 00:34:37.275
that this drink could
improve concentration

00:34:37.275 --> 00:34:38.676
and reaction speeds,

00:34:38.676 --> 00:34:40.978
a claim that lacked
any scientific support.

00:34:40.978 --> 00:34:42.547
Furthermore, the suit said that Red Bull

00:34:42.547 --> 00:34:44.749
persistently and pervasively
market their product

00:34:44.749 --> 00:34:47.885
as a superior source of energy,
worthy of a premium price

00:34:47.885 --> 00:34:50.655
over a cup of coffee or
other sources of caffeine.

00:34:50.655 --> 00:34:54.092
Red Bull did agree to a
$13 million settlement,

00:34:54.092 --> 00:34:56.227
which granted anyone
who purchased a Red Bull

00:34:56.227 --> 00:34:58.830
dating back the January 1, 2002,

00:34:58.830 --> 00:35:02.166
was entitled to $10 or
$15 worth of Red Bull.

00:35:02.166 --> 00:35:03.734
Harry: From calorie
count to portion sizes,

00:35:03.734 --> 00:35:05.136
we wanted to find out all the differences

00:35:05.136 --> 00:35:08.005
between movie-theater food at
AMC and Odeon movie theaters

00:35:08.005 --> 00:35:09.607
in the UK and the US.

00:35:09.607 --> 00:35:11.075
This is "Food Wars."

00:35:13.845 --> 00:35:16.280
It might seem like Odeon and
AMC are different chains.

00:35:16.280 --> 00:35:18.015
However, they're actually
owned by the same company,

00:35:18.015 --> 00:35:19.016
so let's compare.

00:35:19.016 --> 00:35:22.019
Popcorn in a UK Odeon
cinema comes in four sizes.

00:35:22.019 --> 00:35:26.390
There's a kids, regular,
medium, and large.

00:35:26.390 --> 00:35:30.094
Classic popcorn at a US
AMC comes in three sizes,

00:35:30.094 --> 00:35:32.697
small, regular, large,

00:35:32.697 --> 00:35:35.800
and of course, if you want
to get a to-go option,

00:35:35.800 --> 00:35:40.805
they have the AMC megabag.

00:35:42.406 --> 00:35:43.808
Boom!

00:35:43.808 --> 00:35:47.211
That's three times the
size of the standard large.

00:35:47.211 --> 00:35:48.579
Harry: Let's weigh a large salted popcorn

00:35:48.579 --> 00:35:51.082
in both countries to see
whose large is bigger.

00:35:51.082 --> 00:35:52.917
So, our large salt popcorn is actually,

00:35:52.917 --> 00:35:54.685
I think comes to 204 grams,

00:35:54.685 --> 00:35:57.221
which is about 30 grams more
than we were supposed to get.

00:35:57.221 --> 00:36:00.291
Joe: 194 grams of popcorn.

00:36:00.291 --> 00:36:02.593
"Avatar." Haven't seen it.

00:36:02.593 --> 00:36:04.462
And for my own morbid curiosity,

00:36:04.462 --> 00:36:06.297
so, I'm going to weigh it in the bag.

00:36:06.297 --> 00:36:09.000
I don't know, just
subtract, like, 2 grams.

00:36:09.000 --> 00:36:10.268
How much could the bag weigh?

00:36:10.268 --> 00:36:11.102
This.

00:36:14.338 --> 00:36:16.174
620 grams.

00:36:16.174 --> 00:36:19.110
Drinks at a US AMC theater
come in three sizes.

00:36:19.110 --> 00:36:21.012
Small, 20 fluid ounces;

00:36:21.012 --> 00:36:23.114
regular, 32 fluid ounces;

00:36:23.114 --> 00:36:26.617
and a large "Avatar," 44 fluid ounces.

00:36:26.617 --> 00:36:28.019
Harry: Now, shockingly,
our drinks in the UK

00:36:28.019 --> 00:36:30.254
are actually just as big
as the US ones for once.

00:36:30.254 --> 00:36:32.290
Cinemas I think are the
only place in the UK

00:36:32.290 --> 00:36:33.925
where you can get a drink of this size.

00:36:33.925 --> 00:36:35.593
The thought of getting one of
these from a fast-food place

00:36:35.593 --> 00:36:37.862
in the UK is absolutely unheard of.

00:36:37.862 --> 00:36:39.463
Let's measure out the
large in both countries

00:36:39.463 --> 00:36:41.666
to see if we're getting as
much as we've been promised.

00:36:41.666 --> 00:36:42.800
Joe: Wow, it's pretty close.

00:36:42.800 --> 00:36:44.502
What was it supposed to be? 44?

00:36:44.502 --> 00:36:45.770
By my calculations,

00:36:45.770 --> 00:36:48.739
they've pretty much nailed
bang on the 40-ounce line,

00:36:48.739 --> 00:36:50.007
so you're maybe not getting quite as much

00:36:50.007 --> 00:36:50.841
as you were promised.

00:36:50.841 --> 00:36:52.410
Admittedly, we did lose
a little bit in transit

00:36:52.410 --> 00:36:54.312
and also a little splash
just on the table there,

00:36:54.312 --> 00:36:57.682
so maybe you could round it up
generously to, like, 41, 42,

00:36:57.682 --> 00:36:59.417
which, honestly, even
if it's slightly less

00:36:59.417 --> 00:37:01.185
than you're being promised,
I think we can forgive them.

00:37:01.185 --> 00:37:04.455
Certainly we can't fault
James Cameron for this.

00:37:04.455 --> 00:37:08.559
Certainly we can't blame
the Na'vi of Pandora.

00:37:08.559 --> 00:37:09.927
We also have ice drinks,

00:37:09.927 --> 00:37:12.029
which are the iconic Tango ice blasts.

00:37:12.029 --> 00:37:13.464
We have them in three sizes,

00:37:13.464 --> 00:37:16.167
a regular, a medium, and a large.

00:37:16.167 --> 00:37:17.602
Tango ice blasts are amazing.

00:37:17.602 --> 00:37:19.270
They have a bit of a
cult following in the UK.

00:37:19.270 --> 00:37:22.039
I think cinemagoers over here
really, really love these.

00:37:22.039 --> 00:37:23.541
You can get them usually in two flavors,

00:37:23.541 --> 00:37:24.775
which are red and blue.

00:37:24.775 --> 00:37:26.544
I don't know exactly what
they're supposed to taste of.

00:37:26.544 --> 00:37:28.679
It's kind of just tangy
food coloring anyway.

00:37:28.679 --> 00:37:29.747
They're not supposed to look like this.

00:37:29.747 --> 00:37:31.616
As you can probably tell,
these have just been sat out

00:37:31.616 --> 00:37:32.817
under the studio lights for a while.

00:37:32.817 --> 00:37:34.018
Here's what they're supposed to look like.

00:37:34.018 --> 00:37:37.688
You can also get ice
beverages at the US AMC,

00:37:37.688 --> 00:37:40.057
primarily in the form of an Icee,

00:37:40.057 --> 00:37:43.060
and they come in three sizes normally,

00:37:43.060 --> 00:37:44.695
but not the AMC we went to.

00:37:44.695 --> 00:37:45.896
They only had regular.

00:37:45.896 --> 00:37:48.199
It should be a small, 20-fluid-ounce.

00:37:48.199 --> 00:37:50.301
The regular "Avatar: Way of the Water"

00:37:50.301 --> 00:37:53.571
Na'vi-colored drink here
is a 32-fluid-ounce,

00:37:53.571 --> 00:37:56.641
and of course the large
is a 44-fluid-ounce.

00:37:56.641 --> 00:37:58.609
I think that's the exact same size

00:37:58.609 --> 00:38:00.144
as the soft drinks we just had.

00:38:00.144 --> 00:38:01.479
I would like to request,

00:38:01.479 --> 00:38:02.613
I don't know how hard this is going to be,

00:38:02.613 --> 00:38:05.449
if Yuelei and the rest of
the postproduction team

00:38:05.449 --> 00:38:09.654
can make it look like I'm
in the underwater "Avatar."

00:38:09.654 --> 00:38:12.990
With me just swimming 
with the Na'vi? Right?

00:38:12.990 --> 00:38:14.292
Whee, I'm in the movie!

00:38:14.292 --> 00:38:15.359
How hard would that be?

00:38:15.359 --> 00:38:16.894
Can you make it 3D as well?

00:38:16.894 --> 00:38:17.862
That's pretty easy, right?

00:38:17.862 --> 00:38:21.465
Can you have that done
by end of day Friday?

00:38:21.465 --> 00:38:24.802
When I'm swimming 
around with Jake Sully.

00:38:28.372 --> 00:38:30.608
Here is everything you'll
find at a UK Odeon cinema

00:38:30.608 --> 00:38:32.376
that you won't find in an AMC.

00:38:32.376 --> 00:38:36.647
Here's everything at a US AMC
you won't find at an Odeon.

00:38:36.647 --> 00:38:38.149
We'll start with the
classic, which is popcorn.

00:38:38.149 --> 00:38:41.285
In the UK, it comes in two
flavors, as salted or sweet.

00:38:41.285 --> 00:38:43.521
You can also ask them to
mix them together for you.

00:38:43.521 --> 00:38:45.890
Salt and sweet, excellent contrast.

00:38:45.890 --> 00:38:47.725
You won't find butter popcorn

00:38:47.725 --> 00:38:49.093
anywhere on the menu in the UK.

00:38:49.093 --> 00:38:51.295
The fact that you guys are
putting melted butter on popcorn,

00:38:51.295 --> 00:38:53.864
extremely weird to us. Stop doing that.

00:38:53.864 --> 00:38:56.534
In the US, our popcorn
obviously comes plain or salted,

00:38:56.534 --> 00:38:59.570
but we also have butter popcorn,

00:38:59.570 --> 00:39:00.404
and yes, Harry,

00:39:00.404 --> 00:39:04.241
we like to put melted
butter all over our popcorn.

00:39:04.241 --> 00:39:05.343
Two things I want to know.

00:39:05.343 --> 00:39:08.379
One, it's almost always referred to as

00:39:08.379 --> 00:39:10.448
"butter-flavored topping,"

00:39:10.448 --> 00:39:13.451
presumably because they
can't legally call it butter,

00:39:13.451 --> 00:39:15.252
or maybe there's just other junk in there

00:39:15.252 --> 00:39:16.854
and it isn't officially butter.

00:39:16.854 --> 00:39:18.823
In America there's just some people

00:39:18.823 --> 00:39:21.926
who are so nuts about the butter.

00:39:21.926 --> 00:39:24.195
AMC now has something -- I
don't know if this is to go

00:39:24.195 --> 00:39:26.130
or you get this in the theater
-- where they give you,

00:39:26.130 --> 00:39:29.633
no joke, this thing of butter on the side

00:39:29.633 --> 00:39:31.535
to take into the theater with you,

00:39:31.535 --> 00:39:32.903
because there's so much

00:39:32.903 --> 00:39:35.706
butter-flavor-topping drama in the US,

00:39:35.706 --> 00:39:39.744
AMC was like, here, just take
this and go do it yourself.

00:39:39.744 --> 00:39:40.578
Oh.

00:39:41.912 --> 00:39:43.781
Wow, look at that. You
see that? You see that?

00:39:43.781 --> 00:39:46.350
Oh, yeah.

00:39:46.350 --> 00:39:47.318
I want you to pay attention.

00:39:47.318 --> 00:39:48.719
Now, imagine I'm eating this in the dark.

00:39:48.719 --> 00:39:50.621
"Ooh, I like my butter so much. Mwah."

00:39:53.724 --> 00:39:56.193
Look at this! Look at my hands!

00:39:56.193 --> 00:39:58.763
This is the messiest snack in the world.

00:40:00.364 --> 00:40:02.900
I never get butter on my
popcorn. This is so gross.

00:40:06.871 --> 00:40:08.706
Yeah, it doesn't actually
taste that much like butter.

00:40:08.706 --> 00:40:10.608
It has a buttery flavor to it.

00:40:10.608 --> 00:40:12.710
Yeah, it's definitely flavored butter.

00:40:12.710 --> 00:40:13.944
That's not melted butter.

00:40:13.944 --> 00:40:14.945
You can also get sweets

00:40:14.945 --> 00:40:16.647
as a topping on your popcorn in the UK.

00:40:16.647 --> 00:40:19.683
This comes in the form of
Cadbury's Dairy Milk buttons,

00:40:19.683 --> 00:40:22.553
as Smarties, Kit Kats, and Rolos.

00:40:22.553 --> 00:40:23.454
Speaking of popcorn,

00:40:23.454 --> 00:40:25.823
you can also get cheddar
popcorn, which is,

00:40:25.823 --> 00:40:27.191
I don't know if this is
just not in your theaters

00:40:27.191 --> 00:40:28.292
or really popular in the UK at all,

00:40:28.292 --> 00:40:31.896
but it's popcorn that is
tossed in cheese dust.

00:40:31.896 --> 00:40:34.632
And also caramel corn, which is popcorn,

00:40:34.632 --> 00:40:35.466
you guessed it,

00:40:35.466 --> 00:40:37.668
encased in caramel.

00:40:38.536 --> 00:40:40.471
[crunching]

00:40:40.471 --> 00:40:42.907
There's a range of hot food
options at a UK Odeon cinema,

00:40:42.907 --> 00:40:43.874
including the following:

00:40:43.874 --> 00:40:45.643
Firstly, we have the
iconic cinema hot dog.

00:40:45.643 --> 00:40:48.345
Now, obviously you guys
have hot dogs in America.

00:40:48.345 --> 00:40:52.917
However, it's an exclusive
because ours is a pork sausage

00:40:52.917 --> 00:40:54.418
while yours, I think, is beef.

00:40:54.418 --> 00:40:57.221
That looks real sad.

00:40:57.221 --> 00:40:59.089
Oh, no.

00:41:04.161 --> 00:41:05.796
Oh, hot dog. Yay!

00:41:05.796 --> 00:41:07.598
That's a pretty good-sized hot dog, right?

00:41:09.533 --> 00:41:12.203
Movie-theater hot dogs for
some reason are really good.

00:41:12.203 --> 00:41:14.872
You ever notice that? Movie
theaters and ball games,

00:41:14.872 --> 00:41:16.540
that's where the hot
dog's the absolute best.

00:41:16.540 --> 00:41:18.976
Next up, we have two pizza
options at UK Odeon cinemas.

00:41:18.976 --> 00:41:21.679
You can get a cheese pizza
or a pepperoni pizza.

00:41:21.679 --> 00:41:23.414
I haven't even opened them
and I'm losing my mind

00:41:23.414 --> 00:41:25.249
because this is how they've been packaged

00:41:25.249 --> 00:41:26.650
and presented to us.

00:41:31.555 --> 00:41:33.724
What is that?

00:41:33.724 --> 00:41:37.094
Um, I'm slightly at a loss for words.

00:41:37.094 --> 00:41:38.596
I might be giving them
too much credit here.

00:41:38.596 --> 00:41:40.831
I think maybe if this were
fresh out of the oven,

00:41:40.831 --> 00:41:43.734
which obviously this is not,
it actually might be OK.

00:41:43.734 --> 00:41:47.671
But there's a reason why pizza
boxes exist, for example.

00:41:47.671 --> 00:41:49.640
Maybe look into that in future.

00:41:49.640 --> 00:41:52.510
I'm just imagining any Italian viewers

00:41:52.510 --> 00:41:54.678
watching this and just crying.

00:41:54.678 --> 00:41:56.113
You can also get flatbread pizzas.

00:41:56.113 --> 00:41:58.415
The AMC I went to did
not currently have them

00:41:58.415 --> 00:41:59.650
because I went there
right when they opened.

00:41:59.650 --> 00:42:00.484
They weren't ready yet.

00:42:00.484 --> 00:42:03.554
But you can get also a
four-cheese, a pepperoni,

00:42:03.554 --> 00:42:05.823
or a supreme flatbread pizza.

00:42:05.823 --> 00:42:07.224
You can also get yourself curly fries.

00:42:07.224 --> 00:42:09.593
Now we're talking. Curly fries, right?

00:42:09.593 --> 00:42:10.594
Mm.

00:42:11.962 --> 00:42:13.864
The Impossible nuggets.

00:42:13.864 --> 00:42:16.200
[thudding]

00:42:16.200 --> 00:42:17.034
Oh, yes.

00:42:17.034 --> 00:42:20.738
For some reason I picked
the marinara. Let's do it.

00:42:20.738 --> 00:42:25.175
Who doesn't want to eat
fake deep-fried meat

00:42:25.175 --> 00:42:29.246
and dip it in a red sauce
in a pitch-dark theater?

00:42:31.749 --> 00:42:33.050
Nope. Oh, wow.

00:42:34.018 --> 00:42:35.052
Those are really bad.

00:42:35.052 --> 00:42:36.787
We have pretzel bites at our AMC.

00:42:36.787 --> 00:42:39.156
You can get them unsalted with cheese;

00:42:39.156 --> 00:42:41.492
salted with cheese, which I got;

00:42:41.492 --> 00:42:43.060
garlic Parmesan with cheese;

00:42:43.060 --> 00:42:44.595
everything bagel with cheese;

00:42:44.595 --> 00:42:47.398
and cinnamon sugar with icing.

00:42:51.168 --> 00:42:53.370
They don't taste bad,
but they're really chewy.

00:42:54.638 --> 00:42:56.106
You're going to want those
right out of the oven.

00:42:56.106 --> 00:42:57.408
Or the microwave.

00:42:57.408 --> 00:43:00.277
You can also get a
Bavarian legend pretzel.

00:43:00.277 --> 00:43:01.745
The theater we went to did not have them

00:43:01.745 --> 00:43:02.980
at the time of filming this.

00:43:02.980 --> 00:43:05.549
At a UK Odeon, you can
get triple-dip nachos,

00:43:05.549 --> 00:43:08.319
which are tortilla chips
which come with guacamole,

00:43:08.319 --> 00:43:10.054
salsa, and I think a cheese sauce.

00:43:10.054 --> 00:43:11.188
This is how it came.

00:43:11.188 --> 00:43:15.926
What we have is just a bag
of plain tortilla chips

00:43:15.926 --> 00:43:18.162
and a box labeled "dips."

00:43:18.162 --> 00:43:19.463
We have the cheese sauce.

00:43:19.463 --> 00:43:23.233
We have some very vibrant guacamole,

00:43:23.233 --> 00:43:25.035
like someone blended up Shrek.

00:43:25.035 --> 00:43:27.805
We have some tomato salsa.

00:43:27.805 --> 00:43:29.306
Jalapeños.

00:43:29.306 --> 00:43:33.143
I think this was onion
and chive dip, maybe.

00:43:33.143 --> 00:43:35.512
I feel like I have to try
and assemble these somehow.

00:43:35.512 --> 00:43:38.115
I want to do it in a way
that hopefully you guys can

00:43:38.115 --> 00:43:40.884
join me along for the ride,
because it could be interesting.

00:43:40.884 --> 00:43:42.653
I want to try and get some layerage going

00:43:42.653 --> 00:43:45.155
on there if possible.

00:43:46.290 --> 00:43:47.124
Oh, God.

00:43:49.360 --> 00:43:51.028
Oh, no! [laughing]

00:43:51.028 --> 00:43:52.796
OK. I thought that all
came out as one brick,

00:43:52.796 --> 00:43:54.932
but there were actually two
pots in there. Thank God.

00:43:54.932 --> 00:43:56.400
Go on.

00:43:56.400 --> 00:44:00.871
Yeah, you go. Look at that queso.

00:44:00.871 --> 00:44:03.841
OK, now we're going to
hit it with some salsa.

00:44:07.544 --> 00:44:11.782
Personally, I think this
has gone sensationally well.

00:44:14.151 --> 00:44:15.519
This is,

00:44:15.519 --> 00:44:17.421
this is nachos right here.

00:44:18.422 --> 00:44:20.424
Some people might say, "Harry,

00:44:20.424 --> 00:44:22.760
do you want to heat these up?"

00:44:22.760 --> 00:44:24.628
I'd say, "No. Doesn't need it.

00:44:24.628 --> 00:44:26.864
Perfect the way they are."

00:44:26.864 --> 00:44:28.732
Oh, man, look at the color on this.

00:44:31.268 --> 00:44:33.337
No. My mum used to like the nachos.

00:44:33.337 --> 00:44:34.171
She's not dead,

00:44:34.171 --> 00:44:35.606
I just haven't been to the
cinema with her in a while.

00:44:35.606 --> 00:44:37.841
[crew laughing]

00:44:39.610 --> 00:44:41.412
Yeah? Yeah?

00:44:41.412 --> 00:44:42.646
Leon: They actually don't look bad.

00:44:42.646 --> 00:44:44.114
They don't look terrible, right?

00:44:47.384 --> 00:44:49.787
Absolutely disgraceful.

00:44:49.787 --> 00:44:52.289
I don't know what's going
on on that island of yours,

00:44:52.289 --> 00:44:54.992
but your nachos, thumbs down.

00:44:54.992 --> 00:44:57.661
I would say pretty
generous with the chips.

00:44:57.661 --> 00:44:58.762
Not bad, right?

00:44:58.762 --> 00:45:00.531
These are UK-level nachos right here.

00:45:00.531 --> 00:45:03.834
I don't know who is
like, "Oh, yeah, perfect.

00:45:03.834 --> 00:45:05.903
This is exactly what I think nachos are."

00:45:05.903 --> 00:45:07.805
Did they make a mistake?
Am I looking at this right?

00:45:07.805 --> 00:45:09.540
They gave us a thing of marinara sauce?

00:45:09.540 --> 00:45:12.242
I'm assuming this marinara
was supposed to be salsa.

00:45:12.242 --> 00:45:13.477
Can you imagine?

00:45:13.477 --> 00:45:14.645
Because you just get this
and go to the theater,

00:45:14.645 --> 00:45:16.914
and you're in the dark, and
you're watching a movie.

00:45:16.914 --> 00:45:19.616
"Oh, man. Man, this salsa sure
isn't very chunky. Oh, well.

00:45:19.616 --> 00:45:21.385
Man, I cannot wait to eat these nachos.

00:45:21.385 --> 00:45:25.222
Oh, I'm so worried about the
tree of life, 'Avatar 2.'"

00:45:25.222 --> 00:45:26.924
Oh, no, f---.

00:45:28.392 --> 00:45:29.493
Like, what the hell?!

00:45:29.493 --> 00:45:31.528
It's so bad it's, like,

00:45:31.528 --> 00:45:32.563
oddly alluring.

00:45:32.563 --> 00:45:33.731
Does that make sense?

00:45:35.432 --> 00:45:36.433
This is terrible. I'm sorry.

00:45:36.433 --> 00:45:37.868
I'm going to do everyone a
favor and throw this out.

00:45:39.236 --> 00:45:40.070
Yuck!

00:45:40.070 --> 00:45:40.938
Then we're on to the sides.

00:45:40.938 --> 00:45:42.506
We have a couple of side options in the UK

00:45:42.506 --> 00:45:43.741
that you won't find in the US.

00:45:43.741 --> 00:45:45.342
Unfortunately, one of them
we couldn't find today,

00:45:45.342 --> 00:45:46.477
which are crisper fries,

00:45:46.477 --> 00:45:48.345
which are kind of like
very thin slices of potato

00:45:48.345 --> 00:45:49.179
which are fried.

00:45:49.179 --> 00:45:52.149
However, we could get our
hands on these chicken strips,

00:45:52.149 --> 00:45:53.450
which are actually pretty good.

00:45:53.450 --> 00:45:56.019
Technically also included on
the sides menu are the dips,

00:45:56.019 --> 00:45:57.588
so that includes basically
everything that you would

00:45:57.588 --> 00:45:58.822
normally find on the nachos,

00:45:58.822 --> 00:46:00.624
including the side of jalapeños,

00:46:00.624 --> 00:46:03.160
the salsa dip, the cheese, the guacamole,

00:46:03.160 --> 00:46:05.629
and this cream cheese,
garlic, and herb dip.

00:46:05.629 --> 00:46:07.231
We have one prepackaged-popcorn option

00:46:07.231 --> 00:46:10.167
if you don't fancy the
fresh stuff, which is this:

00:46:10.167 --> 00:46:11.568
Butterkist toffee popcorn.

00:46:11.568 --> 00:46:13.337
I think this is kind
of more similar to what

00:46:13.337 --> 00:46:15.973
you guys might expect from
caramel corn in the US.

00:46:15.973 --> 00:46:17.007
It's basically popcorn,

00:46:17.007 --> 00:46:20.377
but with an actual coating
of this sugary, syrupy stuff.

00:46:20.377 --> 00:46:23.113
Now, the AMC has a bunch of snack options

00:46:23.113 --> 00:46:24.615
that you won't find in the UK,

00:46:24.615 --> 00:46:27.351
starting with these, known
as "lifestyle snacks."

00:46:27.351 --> 00:46:29.486
I'm assuming they're meant
to be a little bit healthier.

00:46:29.486 --> 00:46:30.420
Starting all the way down here,

00:46:30.420 --> 00:46:35.125
you have the Planters
sweet and salty trail mix.

00:46:35.125 --> 00:46:38.629
Grass-fed beef jerky,
courtesy of Country Archer.

00:46:38.629 --> 00:46:39.463
I don't know about this.

00:46:39.463 --> 00:46:43.534
Rhythm organic white
cheddar cauliflower bites.

00:46:43.534 --> 00:46:45.302
No, thanks.

00:46:45.302 --> 00:46:48.005
Homefree chocolate chip cookies.

00:46:48.005 --> 00:46:49.640
You got only 3 grams of sugar

00:46:49.640 --> 00:46:52.042
for these smart and
sweet watermelon bites.

00:46:52.042 --> 00:46:55.579
Mango sweet and tangy
supersnacks. Dried mangoes.

00:46:55.579 --> 00:46:59.116
And SkinnyDipped dark chocolate almonds.

00:46:59.116 --> 00:47:00.050
In addition to the popcorn,

00:47:00.050 --> 00:47:01.351
we also have some sweets and chocolates,

00:47:01.351 --> 00:47:02.252
which I will go through now.

00:47:02.252 --> 00:47:04.755
Wine gums. Do you guys
have wine gums in the US?

00:47:04.755 --> 00:47:06.990
I really like these. They're
a bit of an old-person sweet.

00:47:06.990 --> 00:47:08.458
I still don't know exactly
why they're called wine gums,

00:47:08.458 --> 00:47:09.927
because I don't think
they have wine in them.

00:47:09.927 --> 00:47:11.528
On top of the gummies themselves,

00:47:11.528 --> 00:47:14.731
they will have the name of
a wine kind of stamped on,

00:47:14.731 --> 00:47:15.766
and they're different colors.

00:47:15.766 --> 00:47:17.367
The flavors change according to the color.

00:47:17.367 --> 00:47:19.236
Red one's always the best, of course.

00:47:19.236 --> 00:47:21.205
Couple of Cadbury Dairy Milk options.

00:47:21.205 --> 00:47:24.508
We have some Cadbury
caramel Dairy Milk nibbles,

00:47:24.508 --> 00:47:25.976
Dairy Milk giant buttons,

00:47:25.976 --> 00:47:27.411
Galaxy minstrels.

00:47:27.411 --> 00:47:30.113
So, in the UK we have Dairy
Milk, which is owned by Cadbury,

00:47:30.113 --> 00:47:32.349
and then the Mars
Corporation has their own

00:47:32.349 --> 00:47:34.551
brand of milk chocolate,
which is called Galaxy.

00:47:34.551 --> 00:47:35.752
And this is basically Galaxy chocolate

00:47:35.752 --> 00:47:37.688
with a hard shell on the outside.

00:47:37.688 --> 00:47:39.356
These honestly are really good.

00:47:39.356 --> 00:47:40.691
Cadbury twirl bites.

00:47:40.691 --> 00:47:42.326
It's Cadbury Dairy Milk
chocolate, and it's kind of got

00:47:42.326 --> 00:47:44.962
this weird swirled texture on the inside,

00:47:44.962 --> 00:47:47.264
so it lends itself to being quite a flaky

00:47:47.264 --> 00:47:49.566
and almost melt-in-your-mouth
chocolate bar.

00:47:49.566 --> 00:47:50.400
They're pretty good.

00:47:50.400 --> 00:47:51.835
Aero peppermint bubbles.

00:47:51.835 --> 00:47:54.304
It's got this weird aerated
texture in the middle,

00:47:54.304 --> 00:47:55.772
which is designed basically

00:47:55.772 --> 00:47:57.241
to melt in your mouth when you eat it.

00:47:57.241 --> 00:48:00.477
Milkybar buttons! I
loved Milkybar as a kid.

00:48:00.477 --> 00:48:01.912
It's basically white chocolate,

00:48:01.912 --> 00:48:03.447
which I used to love when I was younger.

00:48:03.447 --> 00:48:05.215
I think as my palate has kind of evolved

00:48:05.215 --> 00:48:06.483
as I've gotten older,

00:48:06.483 --> 00:48:08.552
I don't really tolerate white
chocolate like I used to,

00:48:08.552 --> 00:48:10.821
but these are great. Bit
of a nostalgia factor.

00:48:10.821 --> 00:48:12.956
And the last one we found
today was Maltesers.

00:48:12.956 --> 00:48:13.790
I love a Malteser.

00:48:13.790 --> 00:48:17.160
I still don't fully understand
what they are, to be honest.

00:48:17.160 --> 00:48:19.196
What is the middle bit?
It's not honeycomb,

00:48:19.196 --> 00:48:21.932
but it's got a crunchy,
almost honeycomb texture.

00:48:21.932 --> 00:48:23.333
Now, it's not a prepackaged option,

00:48:23.333 --> 00:48:24.568
but it is a sweet option.

00:48:24.568 --> 00:48:26.536
We have pick and mix cups in the UK.

00:48:26.536 --> 00:48:29.740
Pick and mix is a really
iconic British thing, I think.

00:48:29.740 --> 00:48:32.809
It's basically this notion
of, you go into a sweet shop,

00:48:32.809 --> 00:48:34.144
or in this case a cinema,

00:48:34.144 --> 00:48:36.847
and they'll have lots of
different pots or tubs

00:48:36.847 --> 00:48:38.215
of individual candies,

00:48:38.215 --> 00:48:40.918
and you can go in with a scoop,
scoop a few, put them in,

00:48:40.918 --> 00:48:42.386
and create your own mixture of them.

00:48:42.386 --> 00:48:44.054
So if there's one particular
one that you love,

00:48:44.054 --> 00:48:45.622
you can just have a cupful of that,

00:48:45.622 --> 00:48:46.757
or you can go for some variety,

00:48:46.757 --> 00:48:48.558
mix it up a little bit,
like we've done today.

00:48:48.558 --> 00:48:50.594
The issue is when you're layering it,

00:48:50.594 --> 00:48:53.363
you end up just going one
layer of thing at a time.

00:48:53.363 --> 00:48:55.165
I haven't assembled this very well.

00:48:55.165 --> 00:48:56.466
Couldn't get everything.

00:48:56.466 --> 00:48:57.467
Just grabbed a bunch of stuff

00:48:57.467 --> 00:48:59.202
that I thought looked pretty good.

00:48:59.202 --> 00:49:00.971
Also I think some classics here.

00:49:00.971 --> 00:49:02.005
Milk Duds.

00:49:02.005 --> 00:49:04.241
Junior Mints, the big box.

00:49:04.241 --> 00:49:05.943
Mini Snickers. Hey.

00:49:07.244 --> 00:49:08.512
Skittles.

00:49:08.512 --> 00:49:09.913
My teeth are already starting to hurt.

00:49:09.913 --> 00:49:12.382
Butterfingers unwrapped minis.

00:49:12.382 --> 00:49:16.153
And Sour Patch Kids.

00:49:16.153 --> 00:49:19.022
And also Airhead extremes.

00:49:19.022 --> 00:49:21.224
This, of course, just
the tip of the iceberg.

00:49:21.224 --> 00:49:25.162
You can get so, so many candies at AMC.

00:49:26.063 --> 00:49:27.331
This many.

00:49:27.331 --> 00:49:28.932
You can also get a Ben
&amp; Jerry's milkshake.

00:49:28.932 --> 00:49:30.100
What they do is they let you choose

00:49:30.100 --> 00:49:32.035
three scoops of ice cream of your choosing

00:49:32.035 --> 00:49:34.237
and then pretty much
just blend them together

00:49:34.237 --> 00:49:35.672
to create a milkshake.

00:49:35.672 --> 00:49:38.008
Also in the US we have ice
cream you can't get in the UK.

00:49:38.008 --> 00:49:39.876
You can get yourself a Dibs Crunch,

00:49:39.876 --> 00:49:41.545
a Häagen-Dazs bar almond,

00:49:41.545 --> 00:49:43.380
a Nestlé Toll House ice cream sandwich,

00:49:43.380 --> 00:49:45.515
and a Nestlé's Drumstick.

00:49:45.515 --> 00:49:47.117
The other soft-drink
exclusives are actually

00:49:47.117 --> 00:49:48.318
aimed more at children.

00:49:48.318 --> 00:49:51.188
We have some Fruit Shoots,
which come either as this one,

00:49:51.188 --> 00:49:54.024
which is apple and black
currant, or as orange.

00:49:54.024 --> 00:49:55.559
It's just kind of a bottle of squash.

00:49:55.559 --> 00:49:58.528
And for the Americans who
might not know what squash is,

00:49:58.528 --> 00:50:00.764
does cordial help at all?

00:50:00.764 --> 00:50:02.966
You get a concentrated juice

00:50:02.966 --> 00:50:05.669
and then dilute it with water
to produce basically this.

00:50:05.669 --> 00:50:06.870
The main event as far as I'm concerned

00:50:06.870 --> 00:50:08.572
when it comes to drinks are these ones,

00:50:08.572 --> 00:50:10.273
which are the alcoholic options.

00:50:10.273 --> 00:50:12.109
You can get alcohol at UK cinemas.

00:50:12.109 --> 00:50:13.577
We got a few of the things on offer today,

00:50:13.577 --> 00:50:16.146
and these include this Rekorderlig

00:50:16.146 --> 00:50:17.180
strawberry and lime cider.

00:50:17.180 --> 00:50:18.882
We have a bottle of Heineken beer.

00:50:18.882 --> 00:50:20.283
We have some wine options.

00:50:20.283 --> 00:50:22.652
Got a little bottle of red
here. It's really cute.

00:50:22.652 --> 00:50:23.653
It's literally just like they've taken

00:50:23.653 --> 00:50:24.554
a full-size bottle of red

00:50:24.554 --> 00:50:26.523
and just squished it and scaled it down.

00:50:26.523 --> 00:50:27.758
You can also get white wine

00:50:27.758 --> 00:50:29.126
and I think rosé wine as well.

00:50:29.126 --> 00:50:31.228
Or, if you're in a celebratory mood,

00:50:31.228 --> 00:50:32.662
you can get a little bottle of prosecco.

00:50:32.662 --> 00:50:34.464
Then we have some
premixed-cocktail options.

00:50:34.464 --> 00:50:36.533
Today we got a classic G and T

00:50:36.533 --> 00:50:39.403
and a Jack and Coke.

00:50:39.403 --> 00:50:40.303
What about the beverages?

00:50:40.303 --> 00:50:43.373
In the US, we have so, so many beverages,

00:50:43.373 --> 00:50:46.176
starting with the Coke
Freestyle, the Freestyle machine.

00:50:46.176 --> 00:50:47.177
You've seen it before.

00:50:47.177 --> 00:50:49.613
It has all of these flavors.

00:50:49.613 --> 00:50:50.981
I wasn't getting one of each.

00:50:50.981 --> 00:50:53.517
You can also get a Gold
Peak unsweetened iced tea,

00:50:53.517 --> 00:50:54.751
which they did not have,

00:50:54.751 --> 00:50:57.721
a Gold Peak sweet tea, which
they also did not have,

00:50:57.721 --> 00:51:00.090
and Minute Maid orange juice

00:51:00.090 --> 00:51:02.692
and Minute Maid apple juice.

00:51:02.692 --> 00:51:07.264
Chocolate milk, Dasani water, Smartwater,

00:51:07.264 --> 00:51:08.832
and a Costa coffee.

00:51:08.832 --> 00:51:11.435
They also didn't have that.

00:51:11.435 --> 00:51:12.803
I could really go for some coffee.

00:51:12.803 --> 00:51:14.304
I've been told that it is interesting

00:51:14.304 --> 00:51:15.872
that we can get Costa coffee here.

00:51:15.872 --> 00:51:17.574
It is actually a British coffee chain,

00:51:17.574 --> 00:51:20.710
but it was bought by Coca-Cola in 2019

00:51:20.710 --> 00:51:24.214
for almost £4 billion

00:51:24.214 --> 00:51:26.516
and has now begun expanding into the US.

00:51:29.352 --> 00:51:31.321
A large salted popcorn at a UK Odeon

00:51:31.321 --> 00:51:32.889
contains the following:

00:51:32.889 --> 00:51:34.257
863 calories;

00:51:34.257 --> 00:51:36.726
48.37 grams of fat,

00:51:36.726 --> 00:51:39.529
of which 37.84 grams are saturated;

00:51:39.529 --> 00:51:41.565
92.18 grams of carbs,

00:51:41.565 --> 00:51:43.867
of which 5.94 grams are sugars;

00:51:43.867 --> 00:51:45.569
and an unknown amount of sodium.

00:51:45.569 --> 00:51:46.470
Unfortunately, the website

00:51:46.470 --> 00:51:47.804
didn't have the sodium information.

00:51:47.804 --> 00:51:49.906
I did reach out via
the live-chat function,

00:51:49.906 --> 00:51:51.475
and the guy said they didn't
know what had gone on.

00:51:51.475 --> 00:51:52.509
He was going to look into it for me,

00:51:52.509 --> 00:51:53.810
but I did not hear back.

00:51:53.810 --> 00:51:56.012
A regular plain popcorn
popped in canola oil

00:51:56.012 --> 00:51:59.116
is 550 calories, 24 grams of fat,

00:51:59.116 --> 00:52:01.618
2 grams of saturated fat, 74 carbs,

00:52:01.618 --> 00:52:04.087
1,380 milligrams of sodium.

00:52:04.087 --> 00:52:08.725
The same size popcorn but this
time cooked in coconut oil,

00:52:08.725 --> 00:52:11.962
540 calories, 24 grams of fat,

00:52:11.962 --> 00:52:13.563
17 grams of saturated fat,

00:52:13.563 --> 00:52:15.465
74 grams of carbs,

00:52:15.465 --> 00:52:18.768
and 1,380 milligrams of sodium.

00:52:18.768 --> 00:52:22.439
Now, there are no stats for
the butter-flavored topping,

00:52:22.439 --> 00:52:23.673
which is a bit concerning,

00:52:23.673 --> 00:52:27.110
but if you add butter and
salt to pretzel bites,

00:52:27.110 --> 00:52:30.046
it adds 100 calories and 12 grams of fat,

00:52:30.046 --> 00:52:33.116
7 grams of saturated fat,
and 300 milligrams of sodium.

00:52:34.618 --> 00:52:36.186
Adding that same amount of butter

00:52:36.186 --> 00:52:39.356
to this large "Avatar:
Way of the Water" popcorn,

00:52:39.356 --> 00:52:40.657
which is cooked in canola oil,

00:52:40.657 --> 00:52:44.728
you get 970 calories, 51 grams of fat,

00:52:44.728 --> 00:52:46.163
10 grams of saturated fat --

00:52:46.163 --> 00:52:47.831
[coughs] popcorn in my throat --

00:52:47.831 --> 00:52:52.068
117 carbs, of which 1 gram is sugars,

00:52:52.068 --> 00:52:56.239
and 2,450 milligrams of sodium.

00:52:56.239 --> 00:52:57.908
Same exact size of popcorn

00:52:57.908 --> 00:53:00.410
but this time cooked in coconut oil

00:53:00.410 --> 00:53:02.212
and the butter topping from before.

00:53:02.212 --> 00:53:05.615
That's 960 calories,
50 grams of total fat,

00:53:05.615 --> 00:53:09.085
35 grams of saturated fat, 117 carbs,

00:53:09.085 --> 00:53:11.488
of which 1 gram of that is sugars,

00:53:11.488 --> 00:53:16.426
and the sodium, 2,450 milligrams.

00:53:16.426 --> 00:53:17.427
People of the internet,

00:53:17.427 --> 00:53:19.996
canola oil has slightly more calories

00:53:19.996 --> 00:53:22.799
but way less saturated fat.

00:53:22.799 --> 00:53:23.633
Huzzah.

00:53:23.633 --> 00:53:26.036
A large sweet popcorn in the
UK contains the following:

00:53:26.036 --> 00:53:30.207
1,790 calories; 73.08 grams of fat,

00:53:30.207 --> 00:53:32.309
of which 55 grams are saturated;

00:53:32.309 --> 00:53:36.613
253 grams of carbs, of which
84.04 grams are sugars;

00:53:36.613 --> 00:53:38.782
and, again, an unknown amount of sodium.

00:53:40.250 --> 00:53:41.151
Mm.

00:53:41.151 --> 00:53:43.153
Gotta watch out for the
caramel corn, Yuelei.

00:53:43.153 --> 00:53:45.889
This caramel corn in this size bucket,

00:53:45.889 --> 00:53:50.260
1,620 calories. 64 grams of fat.

00:53:50.260 --> 00:53:52.462
21 of those are saturated fat.

00:53:52.462 --> 00:53:54.231
510 grams of carbs,

00:53:54.231 --> 00:53:58.034
and of that, 404 of those grams are sugar,

00:53:58.034 --> 00:54:02.072
and 3,190 milligrams of sodium.

00:54:02.072 --> 00:54:05.375
Now, the large cheddar corn, seen here,

00:54:05.375 --> 00:54:08.078
1,620 calories,

00:54:08.078 --> 00:54:11.314
144 total grams of fat.

00:54:11.314 --> 00:54:14.618
21 of those are saturated.
68 grams of carbs,

00:54:14.618 --> 00:54:18.388
and 2,470 milligrams of sodium.

00:54:21.091 --> 00:54:22.092
Yeesh.

00:54:22.092 --> 00:54:24.194
What about the most calorific
thing on the UK menu?

00:54:24.194 --> 00:54:26.963
Well, that would be a large sweet popcorn

00:54:26.963 --> 00:54:29.399
with the topping option of
Dairy Milk giant buttons.

00:54:29.399 --> 00:54:32.936
This combination would come
to a total of 2,004 calories,

00:54:32.936 --> 00:54:37.073
85.08 grams of fat, 62.2
grams of saturated fat,

00:54:37.073 --> 00:54:38.942
275.8 grams of carbs,

00:54:38.942 --> 00:54:42.345
of which 106.44 grams are sugars.

00:54:42.345 --> 00:54:44.948
That is just over 100%
of your daily calories,

00:54:44.948 --> 00:54:47.150
109% of your daily fat,

00:54:47.150 --> 00:54:49.519
311% of your daily saturates,

00:54:49.519 --> 00:54:53.056
and 212% of your daily sugar.

00:54:53.056 --> 00:54:55.058
Jeez.

00:54:55.058 --> 00:54:58.495
In the US, our AMC menus vary.

00:54:58.495 --> 00:55:02.632
I did find a PDF that had a
bunch of stuff listed on here.

00:55:02.632 --> 00:55:05.468
I don't know how common it is at AMCs,

00:55:05.468 --> 00:55:10.106
but it is the Bavarian legend pretzel

00:55:10.106 --> 00:55:12.676
with the cheese cup and mustard.

00:55:12.676 --> 00:55:16.880
That pretzel and mustard
and cheese total is

00:55:16.880 --> 00:55:19.049
1,920 calories.

00:55:19.049 --> 00:55:20.283
One thing I wanted to point out

00:55:20.283 --> 00:55:24.587
is that it has 7,600 milligrams of sodium.

00:55:24.587 --> 00:55:28.325
That is 330.4%

00:55:28.325 --> 00:55:31.161
of your daily sodium intake.

00:55:31.161 --> 00:55:33.363
Hey. Don't eat that pretzel.

00:55:33.730 --> 00:55:35.332
Harry: From calorie
count to portion sizes,

00:55:35.332 --> 00:55:36.733
we wanted to find out all the differences

00:55:36.733 --> 00:55:39.169
between Cinnabon in the US and the UK.

00:55:39.169 --> 00:55:40.470
This is "Food Wars."

00:55:43.940 --> 00:55:45.742
In the UK, Cinnabon's classic rolls come

00:55:45.742 --> 00:55:48.078
in four portion sizes: as a single,

00:55:48.078 --> 00:55:50.947
as a two-pack, as a four-pack,

00:55:50.947 --> 00:55:53.083
and our largest size,

00:55:53.083 --> 00:55:54.150
a six-pack.

00:55:54.150 --> 00:55:56.586
In the US, Cinnabon classic rolls

00:55:56.586 --> 00:55:59.556
come in three sizes: the single —

00:55:59.556 --> 00:56:00.890
oh, my God.

00:56:00.890 --> 00:56:02.726
I want to eat this so bad.

00:56:02.726 --> 00:56:04.427
Then you got the four-pack,

00:56:04.427 --> 00:56:07.397
for you and, let's be honest, just you,

00:56:07.397 --> 00:56:10.200
and then you can get yourself a six-pack.

00:56:10.200 --> 00:56:11.768
This has some weight to it.

00:56:13.837 --> 00:56:16.506
Cinnabon in the US also
offers catering sizes

00:56:16.506 --> 00:56:18.441
that you can't get in the UK.

00:56:18.441 --> 00:56:21.678
That means we can also get
our classic Cinnabon rolls

00:56:21.678 --> 00:56:24.447
in a nine-pack catering tray.

00:56:24.447 --> 00:56:27.150
Put that on the screen! Oh!

00:56:27.150 --> 00:56:31.321
That's 50% larger than
the UK's biggest pack.

00:56:32.756 --> 00:56:34.290
Oh, amazing.

00:56:34.290 --> 00:56:35.392
But is there a difference in the size

00:56:35.392 --> 00:56:36.559
of the rolls themselves?

00:56:36.559 --> 00:56:37.694
We're going to weigh a classic Cinnabon

00:56:37.694 --> 00:56:38.928
in both countries to find out.

00:56:43.700 --> 00:56:45.535
You can get BonBites in
the UK, but unfortunately

00:56:45.535 --> 00:56:47.404
the store I went to didn't
have them this morning.

00:56:47.404 --> 00:56:48.872
If you can get them, then they should come

00:56:48.872 --> 00:56:49.806
in a pack of four.

00:56:49.806 --> 00:56:51.808
In the US, you can get BonBites

00:56:51.808 --> 00:56:55.211
in a pack of four, 16,

00:56:55.211 --> 00:56:57.514
or the catering tray of 36.

00:56:57.514 --> 00:57:02.218
This is nine times bigger
than the UK's four-pack.

00:57:02.218 --> 00:57:04.053
[thunder rumbles]
[laughs maniacally]

00:57:04.053 --> 00:57:05.755
Four? Get a life.

00:57:05.755 --> 00:57:07.724
UK Cinnabons also offer MiniBons.

00:57:07.724 --> 00:57:09.492
These come in three portion sizes:

00:57:09.492 --> 00:57:11.795
as a single, as a six-pack,

00:57:13.363 --> 00:57:16.466
or our largest size, as a 15-pack.

00:57:17.801 --> 00:57:20.970
Use these as, like, a doorstop.
I think they're stale.

00:57:20.970 --> 00:57:21.905
[box thuds]

00:57:21.905 --> 00:57:24.174
Over here, our MiniBons come in portions

00:57:24.174 --> 00:57:28.912
of one, nine, 15,

00:57:28.912 --> 00:57:32.549
and, of course, we have
a catering tray of 20.

00:57:32.549 --> 00:57:33.383
What about the drinks?

00:57:33.383 --> 00:57:35.952
In the UK, we can get
hot drinks in two sizes:

00:57:35.952 --> 00:57:38.221
as a regular, which is 12 fluid ounces,

00:57:38.221 --> 00:57:40.657
or a large, which is 16 fluid ounces.

00:57:40.657 --> 00:57:43.293
In the US, our hot beverages
come in four sizes:

00:57:43.293 --> 00:57:45.995
small, regular, large,

00:57:45.995 --> 00:57:48.598
and this big catering bag.

00:57:48.598 --> 00:57:49.799
Or does it?

00:57:49.799 --> 00:57:51.601
[whooshes]

00:57:51.601 --> 00:57:53.736
Because they forgot those three.

00:57:53.736 --> 00:57:55.872
The more observant among
you would've noticed

00:57:55.872 --> 00:57:58.708
that the UK's large is
only the regular over here.

00:57:58.708 --> 00:58:00.109
We can also get iced drinks in the UK,

00:58:00.109 --> 00:58:01.411
but they just come in the same sizes

00:58:01.411 --> 00:58:03.680
as our hot drinks, 12 and 16 ounces.

00:58:03.680 --> 00:58:05.548
The sizes change a little when you choose

00:58:05.548 --> 00:58:06.816
the iced drinks in the US.

00:58:06.816 --> 00:58:09.285
We got the small and the regular

00:58:09.285 --> 00:58:10.453
and the catering size.

00:58:10.453 --> 00:58:12.689
Again, the more observant
of you would notice

00:58:12.689 --> 00:58:15.091
that there are some beverages
missing from this cup.

00:58:15.091 --> 00:58:16.826
"Joe must've started
drinking them earlier."

00:58:16.826 --> 00:58:20.563
Nuh-uh. Had a major
beverage-spilling mishap

00:58:20.563 --> 00:58:21.865
with the delivery here.

00:58:21.865 --> 00:58:23.366
Ah, more on that later.

00:58:23.366 --> 00:58:25.802
The final things to compare
are the toppings and sauces.

00:58:25.802 --> 00:58:27.437
In the UK, you can get
some additional toppings,

00:58:27.437 --> 00:58:28.805
like the cream cheese and the pecans,

00:58:28.805 --> 00:58:32.141
and they just come in the
one size, these little cups.

00:58:32.141 --> 00:58:34.344
In the US, we can get extra frosting

00:58:34.344 --> 00:58:37.046
as a regular side of the
cream-cheese frosting,

00:58:37.046 --> 00:58:41.551
I mean, a whole pint of the frosting,

00:58:41.551 --> 00:58:43.219
a side of pecans, who cares?

00:58:43.219 --> 00:58:44.721
Let's weigh the largest frosting side

00:58:44.721 --> 00:58:46.155
in each country to find the difference.

00:58:47.824 --> 00:58:50.593
[laughs] That just, like, barely moved.

00:58:50.593 --> 00:58:53.329
So this is eight of their frostings.

00:58:53.329 --> 00:58:55.331
Soon to be seven.

00:58:55.331 --> 00:58:58.401
It's described as "cream cheese ambient."

00:59:00.003 --> 00:59:03.006
Cream cheese ambient.
That sounds like a really

00:59:03.006 --> 00:59:05.008
experimental music genre.

00:59:05.909 --> 00:59:07.544
It's pretty cool, you probably
wouldn't have heard of it,

00:59:07.544 --> 00:59:09.479
but yeah, no, I listen to
mostly cream cheese ambient.

00:59:12.048 --> 00:59:13.783
Here are all the Cinnabon
items from the UK

00:59:13.783 --> 00:59:15.451
that you won't find in the US.

00:59:15.451 --> 00:59:17.053
Here's everything on a Cinnabon menu

00:59:17.053 --> 00:59:19.923
you will not find in the UK.

00:59:19.923 --> 00:59:21.524
To start off with, we
have some Bon varieties

00:59:21.524 --> 00:59:23.159
you actually won't find in the US.

00:59:23.159 --> 00:59:25.495
Let's start down here with ChocoBons.

00:59:25.495 --> 00:59:27.063
So, as far as I can tell, ChocoBons are

00:59:27.063 --> 00:59:28.531
pretty much just the standard rolls,

00:59:28.531 --> 00:59:30.066
maybe with a little
bit of chocolate powder

00:59:30.066 --> 00:59:31.834
sprinkled into the mix, but then also

00:59:31.834 --> 00:59:34.070
they are covered in chocolate sauce.

00:59:34.070 --> 00:59:34.904
Cheers.

00:59:38.942 --> 00:59:42.145
Our next exclusive roll
is a Lotus Biscoff Bon.

00:59:42.145 --> 00:59:44.280
Longtime viewers of
the show will know that

00:59:44.280 --> 00:59:46.716
I don't really like Lotus Biscoff.

00:59:46.716 --> 00:59:48.351
I didn't realize how
passionately the crew felt

00:59:48.351 --> 00:59:51.120
about Lotus Biscoff, because
I'm now taking heat for this.

00:59:51.120 --> 00:59:52.755
Apparently it's because
I don't like coffee

00:59:52.755 --> 00:59:54.123
and they're really good with coffee.

00:59:54.123 --> 00:59:56.125
I just drink tea, so
maybe it's wasted on me.

00:59:56.125 --> 00:59:58.528
Again, look, you do you, it's fine,

00:59:58.528 --> 01:00:00.229
just not for me. Too sweet for me.

01:00:00.229 --> 01:00:01.831
And then finally, because
we're actually shooting this

01:00:01.831 --> 01:00:03.800
on Valentine's Day, we can get

01:00:03.800 --> 01:00:06.636
a limited-edition Valentine's Bon.

01:00:09.539 --> 01:00:11.341
All of our exclusive Bons
can also be purchased

01:00:11.341 --> 01:00:13.576
in all three forms, which
is the regular size,

01:00:13.576 --> 01:00:15.278
the BonBites, and the MiniBons.

01:00:15.278 --> 01:00:18.081
We actually don't have any
exclusive Bons in the US.

01:00:18.081 --> 01:00:21.384
We can only get the classic
and caramel pecan Bons,

01:00:21.384 --> 01:00:24.153
both of which are obviously
available in the UK.

01:00:24.153 --> 01:00:27.256
But we do have some other
exclusives to showcase.

01:00:27.256 --> 01:00:29.826
The first one, the churro swirls.

01:00:29.826 --> 01:00:34.631
♪ They forgot them ♪

01:00:35.798 --> 01:00:37.800
But here's what they look like,

01:00:37.800 --> 01:00:39.335
and I would love to have tried them.

01:00:39.335 --> 01:00:40.370
Now, we don't have churro swirls,

01:00:40.370 --> 01:00:42.005
but we do have something
called Cinnachips,

01:00:42.005 --> 01:00:44.574
which are like small, crunchy
pieces of cinnamon roll.

01:00:44.574 --> 01:00:47.810
I'm not sure if crunchy is what I want

01:00:47.810 --> 01:00:49.646
from my cinnamon roll.

01:00:49.646 --> 01:00:52.682
[crunching]

01:00:52.682 --> 01:00:54.517
They are crunchy. They weren't kidding.

01:00:54.517 --> 01:00:56.052
These aren't doing it for me.

01:00:56.052 --> 01:00:59.856
They're really kind of dry and
a little bit burned, almost,

01:00:59.856 --> 01:01:03.326
so you kind of get that,
like, acrid burn taste,

01:01:03.326 --> 01:01:05.495
which cancels out pretty much any benefits

01:01:05.495 --> 01:01:06.929
that you get from the cinnamon sugar.

01:01:06.929 --> 01:01:07.897
[crunches loudly]

01:01:07.897 --> 01:01:10.533
We also have something
called Center of the Roll,

01:01:10.533 --> 01:01:12.802
which Cinnabon has trademarked in the US.

01:01:12.802 --> 01:01:14.370
Now, here's what I'm assuming this is

01:01:14.370 --> 01:01:15.538
by looking at it.

01:01:15.538 --> 01:01:19.275
What it looks like,
they just took Cinnabons

01:01:19.275 --> 01:01:24.080
and, like, mashed them up
or, like, unraveled them

01:01:24.080 --> 01:01:26.482
and put them in a cup, and this is smart,

01:01:26.482 --> 01:01:28.918
'cause the only thing I
think keeping everyone

01:01:28.918 --> 01:01:30.720
from getting a Cinnabon at the mall

01:01:30.720 --> 01:01:32.555
is it's kind of a pain in the butt to eat,

01:01:32.555 --> 01:01:34.857
and I think Cinnabon noticed this,

01:01:34.857 --> 01:01:36.225
and they responded with this.

01:01:36.225 --> 01:01:38.428
Like, "You're right. We'll just rip it up,

01:01:38.428 --> 01:01:40.697
put it in a cup, and have at it."

01:01:45.401 --> 01:01:46.836
This works.

01:01:46.836 --> 01:01:49.172
Well, you don't want to
mess with the classics.

01:01:49.172 --> 01:01:51.140
If you want to

01:01:52.041 --> 01:01:54.077
sit down, have a Cinnabon
at the food court,

01:01:54.077 --> 01:01:55.344
go for it, but

01:01:56.813 --> 01:01:58.247
if you're not in the mood,
just get one of these.

01:01:58.247 --> 01:01:59.849
Oh, yeah.

01:01:59.849 --> 01:02:01.350
Oh, my God, look at this.

01:02:01.350 --> 01:02:02.752
Are kidding me with this?

01:02:02.752 --> 01:02:03.786
This is so great.

01:02:07.156 --> 01:02:08.357
Oh, yeah.

01:02:09.559 --> 01:02:11.294
Oh, I forgot —

01:02:11.294 --> 01:02:13.362
oh, I forgot I'm shooting
a video right now.

01:02:13.362 --> 01:02:15.264
This is the, that was the regular,

01:02:15.264 --> 01:02:17.433
and this is the caramel pecan Bon.

01:02:17.433 --> 01:02:18.568
We have a near equivalent here,

01:02:18.568 --> 01:02:20.103
but we call it Roll-on-the-Go.

01:02:20.103 --> 01:02:21.971
As far as I can tell, it's
pretty much just the same thing.

01:02:21.971 --> 01:02:23.539
It's a small cup of I think

01:02:23.539 --> 01:02:25.408
just the center pieces of cinnamon rolls.

01:02:25.408 --> 01:02:28.244
Ours come in two flavors,
classic or choco.

01:02:28.244 --> 01:02:30.246
I do think my favorite
part of a cinnamon roll

01:02:30.246 --> 01:02:32.115
is the gooey middle bit.

01:02:32.115 --> 01:02:33.182
See if this holds up.

01:02:34.984 --> 01:02:36.619
This is pretty good.

01:02:36.619 --> 01:02:38.187
Decent amount of frosting.

01:02:38.187 --> 01:02:39.756
They could maybe have given
you slightly more frosting,

01:02:39.756 --> 01:02:42.959
'cause I think there's some
drier bites in the middle. But.

01:02:45.995 --> 01:02:46.896
Pretty good.

01:02:46.896 --> 01:02:49.465
In the US, we also have cookie BonBites.

01:02:50.566 --> 01:02:51.701
These are chocolate chip cookies

01:02:51.701 --> 01:02:53.169
with cinnamon rolls inside of —

01:02:53.169 --> 01:02:55.037
I'm just finding this out right now.

01:02:55.037 --> 01:02:57.373
Chocolate chip cookies with
cinnamon rolls inside of them?

01:02:57.373 --> 01:02:59.142
Yo, straight up when I saw this, I'm like,

01:02:59.142 --> 01:03:01.310
who's getting cookies at Cinnabon?

01:03:01.310 --> 01:03:03.846
This cannot have a cinnamon roll inside.

01:03:03.846 --> 01:03:05.581
Oh, my God, do you see it?

01:03:05.581 --> 01:03:07.450
It actually — what?

01:03:07.450 --> 01:03:09.185
I didn't even know this existed!

01:03:09.185 --> 01:03:11.187
You got that? You got that, yeah?

01:03:12.054 --> 01:03:15.458
Yo, look at that, oh.
Look what's inside of it.

01:03:15.458 --> 01:03:17.260
Oh, my God, that's crazy.

01:03:17.260 --> 01:03:20.029
This cookie's pregnant with a Cinnabon.

01:03:20.029 --> 01:03:21.831
[baby cries]
Now let's get in here.

01:03:23.499 --> 01:03:25.468
Eh, better an idea than execution.

01:03:26.569 --> 01:03:28.871
We also have CinnaSweeties,

01:03:28.871 --> 01:03:33.376
which look like mini
doughnuts that I'm assuming

01:03:33.376 --> 01:03:34.510
are cinnamon — oh, wait,

01:03:34.510 --> 01:03:35.845
I think these have the frosting inside.

01:03:35.845 --> 01:03:37.814
We've done these for ... Taco Bell?

01:03:37.814 --> 01:03:40.049
The Cinnabon Delights. I'm pretty sure

01:03:40.049 --> 01:03:42.051
this is filled with some sort
of, like, cream cheese, right?

01:03:42.051 --> 01:03:44.187
Wait a second!

01:03:44.187 --> 01:03:45.188
There's no --

01:03:47.924 --> 01:03:48.758
[gasping]

01:03:48.758 --> 01:03:50.827
There's no cream cheese
in these! They're blanks!

01:03:50.827 --> 01:03:52.662
The UK Cinnabon website also advertises

01:03:52.662 --> 01:03:53.996
that some of their branches will have

01:03:53.996 --> 01:03:55.631
Carvel brand ice cream as an option,

01:03:55.631 --> 01:03:56.866
but unfortunately, we didn't have that

01:03:56.866 --> 01:03:57.934
at the one we went to.

01:03:57.934 --> 01:04:00.636
Now we're on to the sauces and toppings.

01:04:00.636 --> 01:04:04.073
In the US, we have a side of Oreo pieces

01:04:04.073 --> 01:04:07.243
that you can get on top
of your Bon. There it is.

01:04:07.243 --> 01:04:10.880
We also have the 8 ounces of frosting,

01:04:10.880 --> 01:04:13.282
and we also have — grr, close.

01:04:14.116 --> 01:04:15.218
This right here is,

01:04:15.218 --> 01:04:18.054
you get a side of the caramel frosting.

01:04:21.824 --> 01:04:22.959
That's also really good.

01:04:22.959 --> 01:04:24.627
We only have the one
exclusive topping option here

01:04:24.627 --> 01:04:28.130
in the UK, and it's this
one, the Lotus Biscoff crumb.

01:04:28.130 --> 01:04:30.900
In the interest of fairness,
I'm going to try it again.

01:04:36.205 --> 01:04:39.308
It's just fine. It's just fine.

01:04:39.308 --> 01:04:40.977
Maybe with a coffee, but.

01:04:44.046 --> 01:04:46.616
No, it's still not for me. Sorry, guys.

01:04:46.616 --> 01:04:48.284
Next up, we got drinks.

01:04:48.284 --> 01:04:49.952
Ah, finally. I'm dying of thirst.

01:04:49.952 --> 01:04:51.087
We have coffee, obviously,

01:04:51.087 --> 01:04:53.222
and you can also get
yourself a hot chocolate.

01:04:53.222 --> 01:04:54.790
Let's check out their hot chocolate.

01:04:54.790 --> 01:04:55.992
I mean, it looks like hot chocolate.

01:04:55.992 --> 01:04:57.126
There's nothing to see.

01:04:59.128 --> 01:05:00.496
Wow, actually not that good.

01:05:00.496 --> 01:05:02.331
Blech.

01:05:02.331 --> 01:05:03.699
Skip that.

01:05:03.699 --> 01:05:05.635
We actually have a better
range of hot drinks in the UK,

01:05:05.635 --> 01:05:07.837
including pretty much a full
range of espresso drinks,

01:05:07.837 --> 01:05:09.939
including an Americano, a cappuccino,

01:05:09.939 --> 01:05:11.574
a latte, a mocha, and so on.

01:05:11.574 --> 01:05:13.409
We can also get a tea and a hot chocolate.

01:05:13.409 --> 01:05:14.710
You can also customize the hot drinks

01:05:14.710 --> 01:05:16.946
with a range of syrups,
including cinnamon spice,

01:05:16.946 --> 01:05:19.382
toasted marshmallow,
salted caramel, and more,

01:05:19.382 --> 01:05:21.017
although if you put any
of those in a cup of tea,

01:05:21.017 --> 01:05:22.351
I will fight you. [boxing bell rings]

01:05:22.351 --> 01:05:25.288
In the US, we have way more
cold drink options than hot.

01:05:25.288 --> 01:05:27.924
Here are the following
exclusive cold drink options.

01:05:27.924 --> 01:05:32.695
First up, cinnamon roll
cold brew iced coffee.

01:05:33.796 --> 01:05:36.198
Another victim of the Uber driver.

01:05:36.198 --> 01:05:38.067
Ooh! [laughs]

01:05:39.001 --> 01:05:40.736
I'm falling apart.

01:05:40.736 --> 01:05:42.772
Pretty good. Too sweet.

01:05:42.772 --> 01:05:44.607
Then we got the raspberry lemonade.

01:05:44.607 --> 01:05:48.077
Also missing 2 inches. Ubefied.

01:05:49.011 --> 01:05:51.347
I mean, I don't want to
give the guy a bad rating,

01:05:51.347 --> 01:05:54.450
but, like, look, I have
not sipped any of these.

01:05:58.020 --> 01:06:00.389
Oh, my God, this raspberry,
I love it. It's great.

01:06:00.389 --> 01:06:03.960
Shout-out to Greta Thunberg.
I'm gonna use my straw twice.

01:06:03.960 --> 01:06:05.428
I care about the environment!

01:06:07.730 --> 01:06:08.931
No more single-use plastic.

01:06:08.931 --> 01:06:11.567
This is the frozen raspberry lemonade.

01:06:14.070 --> 01:06:15.204
Whoa!

01:06:15.204 --> 01:06:17.073
That's, like, powerful.

01:06:18.040 --> 01:06:19.175
This is really good.

01:06:19.175 --> 01:06:21.210
Bottle of milk.

01:06:21.210 --> 01:06:22.445
No, thanks.

01:06:22.445 --> 01:06:25.047
And, of course, fountain drinks,

01:06:25.047 --> 01:06:27.149
and I'm the most bummed because

01:06:27.149 --> 01:06:29.885
out of all the drinks that spilled —

01:06:29.885 --> 01:06:32.288
we have so many flavors to choose from.

01:06:32.288 --> 01:06:34.290
Let's get those on the screen.

01:06:34.290 --> 01:06:36.158
But the one I specifically
wanted was this one,

01:06:36.158 --> 01:06:38.160
was the Pibb Xtra.

01:06:40.563 --> 01:06:44.467
Pibb Xtra's perfectly fine.
It's a Dr Pepper wannabe.

01:06:44.467 --> 01:06:47.703
Back in the '90s, '97, '98, or whatever,

01:06:47.703 --> 01:06:50.006
Mr. Pibb changed its formula to Pibb Xtra.

01:06:50.006 --> 01:06:52.842
They're trying to get in on
Dr Pepper's market share.

01:06:52.842 --> 01:06:55.111
It's so annoying. But the problem is,

01:06:55.111 --> 01:06:57.880
is that there's no Mr. Pibb
anymore. [rousing music]

01:06:57.880 --> 01:07:02.218
30 years of no Mr. Pibb. It's ridiculous!

01:07:02.218 --> 01:07:05.187
I am using my platform right now

01:07:05.187 --> 01:07:08.691
to talk to the executives
at Pibb Xtra or Mr. Pibb:

01:07:08.691 --> 01:07:12.028
Release the Mr. Pibb recipe.

01:07:12.028 --> 01:07:13.362
I'm begging you.

01:07:13.362 --> 01:07:14.563
It doesn't have any value for you!

01:07:14.563 --> 01:07:16.165
You're not making it, so
there's no value, right?

01:07:16.165 --> 01:07:17.299
You're just sitting on the recipe,

01:07:17.299 --> 01:07:18.501
you're not even making it?

01:07:18.501 --> 01:07:19.902
It's worthless to you.

01:07:19.902 --> 01:07:21.871
It's priceless to me.

01:07:21.871 --> 01:07:23.105
And I don't want you people watching,

01:07:23.105 --> 01:07:25.074
this happened last time,
people were messaging me like,

01:07:25.074 --> 01:07:27.443
"Oh, yeah, we got Mr.
Pibb here at the Walmart."

01:07:27.443 --> 01:07:29.645
It's like, it's Pibb
Xtra, it's not Mr. Pibb.

01:07:29.645 --> 01:07:31.647
They're different. OK?

01:07:31.647 --> 01:07:36.619
If anyone watching has cans
of Mr. Pibb from the '90s,

01:07:36.619 --> 01:07:38.854
connect with me. I will buy it off of you.

01:07:38.854 --> 01:07:40.222
I will pay for the shipping.

01:07:40.222 --> 01:07:43.092
That stays in the video, or I quit.

01:07:43.092 --> 01:07:45.227
We have a few exclusive cold
drinks over here in the UK,

01:07:45.227 --> 01:07:47.997
including an iced latte,
a strawberry lemonade,

01:07:47.997 --> 01:07:49.098
and a mango lemonade.

01:07:49.098 --> 01:07:51.367
I got the strawberry lemonade today.

01:07:51.367 --> 01:07:52.902
Pretty pleasant. Quite refreshing.

01:07:52.902 --> 01:07:54.870
Also, in the UK, is it true that you guys

01:07:54.870 --> 01:07:56.739
consider lemonade to be more like

01:07:56.739 --> 01:07:59.542
a carbonated lemon beverage, like Sprite?

01:07:59.542 --> 01:08:01.544
That's true, Joe. If you ask
for a lemonade in the UK,

01:08:01.544 --> 01:08:03.846
expect something that's
carbonated and usually clear,

01:08:03.846 --> 01:08:05.114
so more like a Sprite.

01:08:05.114 --> 01:08:06.816
Although I will say,
Cinnabon seems to be doing it

01:08:06.816 --> 01:08:07.683
kind of the American way,

01:08:07.683 --> 01:08:09.218
so maybe you'd approve of that one.

01:08:09.218 --> 01:08:11.487
Now, you can also get
something called a Chillatta

01:08:11.487 --> 01:08:13.022
in the US and the UK.

01:08:13.022 --> 01:08:15.524
However, over here, they come in flavors

01:08:15.524 --> 01:08:18.227
of Oreo cookies and cream,
strawberries and cream,

01:08:18.227 --> 01:08:20.996
which I got, and the
double chocolate mocha.

01:08:23.999 --> 01:08:25.468
That's just OK.

01:08:26.969 --> 01:08:27.803
Don't bother.

01:08:27.803 --> 01:08:29.738
In the UK, Chillattas
come in five flavors:

01:08:29.738 --> 01:08:31.941
cinnamon roll, strawberry, mango,

01:08:31.941 --> 01:08:33.742
caramel latte, and chocolate mocha.

01:08:33.742 --> 01:08:36.745
I got the cinnamon roll one today.

01:08:36.745 --> 01:08:39.148
Actually looks pretty good.

01:08:39.148 --> 01:08:40.716
It also looked even more impressive

01:08:40.716 --> 01:08:43.085
when the whipped cream was
kind of in a nice swirl.

01:08:44.053 --> 01:08:45.554
It's just, like, a,

01:08:45.554 --> 01:08:47.389
again, quite sweet

01:08:47.389 --> 01:08:51.460
but pretty, like, luxurious
cinnamony milkshake.

01:08:53.629 --> 01:08:54.997
It certainly seems like it.

01:08:54.997 --> 01:08:57.099
I cannot remember a time
when there wasn't one

01:08:57.099 --> 01:08:58.767
in any mall I've gone to.

01:08:58.767 --> 01:09:00.736
You can always smell it before you see it.

01:09:00.736 --> 01:09:05.007
It's impossible to separate
the scent of Cinnabon

01:09:05.007 --> 01:09:07.810
from the mall and vice versa.

01:09:07.810 --> 01:09:11.413
It's like a soundtrack to the memory,

01:09:11.413 --> 01:09:13.048
but how it smells,

01:09:13.048 --> 01:09:16.619
so Cinnabon is like the
smell-track to malls.

01:09:16.619 --> 01:09:17.920
Does that make sense?

01:09:17.920 --> 01:09:19.655
And that's by design.

01:09:19.655 --> 01:09:22.024
Cinnabon purposely put their locations

01:09:22.024 --> 01:09:24.527
away from food courts
and other food stalls

01:09:24.527 --> 01:09:27.163
so the Cinnabon odor would waft

01:09:27.163 --> 01:09:29.465
and not interfere with any other smells.

01:09:29.465 --> 01:09:31.400
So if you're in the
mall, you smell Cinnabon

01:09:31.400 --> 01:09:36.372
and only Cinnabon, and that's
almost like nose marketing?

01:09:36.372 --> 01:09:38.641
I don't know how you would describe it,

01:09:38.641 --> 01:09:39.842
and it's really smart, right?

01:09:39.842 --> 01:09:41.443
'Cause when you smell
it, man, you smell it,

01:09:41.443 --> 01:09:44.046
and you're like, there it
is, I gotta have one. So.

01:09:44.046 --> 01:09:45.981
Is Cinnabon a meal, a snack, a dessert?

01:09:45.981 --> 01:09:48.083
I'm gonna go with snack.

01:09:48.083 --> 01:09:49.818
I feel like one of
those regular Cinnabons,

01:09:49.818 --> 01:09:52.188
I could just eat one of those
easily. Maybe one and a half.

01:09:52.188 --> 01:09:53.856
I don't really know my Cinnabon limit.

01:09:53.856 --> 01:09:55.291
I just kind of found out
about these little guys,

01:09:55.291 --> 01:09:58.093
and I feel like I could easily
knock out half this tray.

01:09:59.295 --> 01:10:01.030
I don't think it should be a meal,

01:10:01.030 --> 01:10:02.998
'cause that could do
some damage to your body.

01:10:02.998 --> 01:10:06.602
As far as a dessert, it seems weird to me

01:10:06.602 --> 01:10:09.572
to eat a full meal and
then get a Cinnabon.

01:10:09.572 --> 01:10:11.974
Like, it just kind of exists on its own.

01:10:11.974 --> 01:10:15.411
So, yeah, it's weird
to consider it a snack,

01:10:15.411 --> 01:10:17.746
but you're definitely
not having it for lunch,

01:10:17.746 --> 01:10:19.915
and you're definitely not
having it after a meal, so.

01:10:19.915 --> 01:10:21.850
By default, snack.

01:10:24.353 --> 01:10:26.422
In the UK, a single Cinnabon classic roll

01:10:26.422 --> 01:10:28.524
will cost you £2.99,

01:10:28.524 --> 01:10:31.193
which at the time of
recording this was $3.65.

01:10:31.193 --> 01:10:34.230
In the US, a single Cinnabon classic roll

01:10:34.230 --> 01:10:37.132
will cost you $7.19.

01:10:37.132 --> 01:10:39.635
That makes this single US roll

01:10:39.635 --> 01:10:42.371
97% more expensive.

01:10:42.371 --> 01:10:43.806
That is hilarious.

01:10:43.806 --> 01:10:45.574
But does the price change if you bulk-buy?

01:10:45.574 --> 01:10:47.276
A six-pack of classic rolls in the UK

01:10:47.276 --> 01:10:48.877
will cost you £10.49,

01:10:48.877 --> 01:10:51.981
which at the time of recording was $12.80.

01:10:51.981 --> 01:10:53.882
So by spending three and a
half times the amount of money,

01:10:53.882 --> 01:10:55.784
you're getting six times
the amount of Cinnabon,

01:10:55.784 --> 01:10:56.785
which is a pretty good deal.

01:10:56.785 --> 01:10:59.888
In the US, a six-pack of
Cinnabon classic rolls

01:10:59.888 --> 01:11:02.791
will cost you $24.99,

01:11:02.791 --> 01:11:05.227
so even when you are bulk-buying,

01:11:05.227 --> 01:11:08.931
it's 95% more expensive to buy in the US.

01:11:08.931 --> 01:11:12.601
For that same 500% increase in food,

01:11:12.601 --> 01:11:15.938
we pay 247% more money.

01:11:15.938 --> 01:11:17.873
It's not often on "Food
Wars" that it's much cheaper

01:11:17.873 --> 01:11:20.142
in the UK than it is in
the US to buy fast food.

01:11:20.142 --> 01:11:20.976
How's that feel, Joe?

01:11:20.976 --> 01:11:24.613
Well, it's Cinnabon, and I
will pay whatever it takes.

01:11:24.613 --> 01:11:26.048
This stuff is amazing.

01:11:26.048 --> 01:11:28.083
They could double the
price. I'm still eating it.

01:11:30.452 --> 01:11:32.054
The UK Cinnabon website doesn't give

01:11:32.054 --> 01:11:34.123
a full nutritional
breakdown including things

01:11:34.123 --> 01:11:36.191
like the fat and the
sugar content of Cinnabon.

01:11:36.191 --> 01:11:38.994
However, when we got this CinnaPack,

01:11:38.994 --> 01:11:40.195
I noticed that they actually have

01:11:40.195 --> 01:11:41.930
a full breakdown on the box.

01:11:41.930 --> 01:11:43.265
Here, we're given the information

01:11:43.265 --> 01:11:46.435
for 100 grams' worth of
classic Cinnabon rolls.

01:11:46.435 --> 01:11:47.503
So you might remember from earlier,

01:11:47.503 --> 01:11:48.570
when we weighed one roll,

01:11:48.570 --> 01:11:50.939
we found that it was pretty
much exactly 200 grams,

01:11:50.939 --> 01:11:52.941
so doubling those numbers
gives us the stats

01:11:52.941 --> 01:11:54.710
for a full roll in the UK.

01:11:54.710 --> 01:11:56.745
Here's everything that's
in a classic Cinnabon roll

01:11:56.745 --> 01:11:58.314
in the UK.

01:11:58.314 --> 01:12:01.183
So that's almost 40% of your
daily recommended calories,

01:12:01.183 --> 01:12:02.985
80% of your daily saturated fat,

01:12:02.985 --> 01:12:05.387
and over 110% of your daily sugar.

01:12:05.387 --> 01:12:06.789
To put the calories into context,

01:12:06.789 --> 01:12:08.324
one of these rolls is like eating

01:12:08.324 --> 01:12:09.992
three McDonald's hamburgers.

01:12:09.992 --> 01:12:12.961
Here's everything in a classic
Cinnabon roll in the US.

01:12:14.430 --> 01:12:15.698
You are reading that right,

01:12:15.698 --> 01:12:18.167
61 grams of sugar.

01:12:18.167 --> 01:12:19.468
And for some reason,

01:12:19.468 --> 01:12:22.738
1,150 milligrams of sodium?

01:12:22.738 --> 01:12:25.374
That puts us slightly ahead of the UK

01:12:25.374 --> 01:12:27.076
in every single category.

01:12:27.076 --> 01:12:28.277
I mean, look at that sodium.

01:12:28.277 --> 01:12:31.380
That is way higher, for some reason.

01:12:31.380 --> 01:12:35.918
That's exactly 50% of your
daily sodium in one roll.

01:12:35.918 --> 01:12:38.354
What about some other even
more unhealthy menu items?

01:12:38.354 --> 01:12:39.955
The most-calorific roll in the UK

01:12:39.955 --> 01:12:41.190
is the Lotus Biscoff roll,

01:12:41.190 --> 01:12:43.992
which clocks in at 1,019 calories.

01:12:43.992 --> 01:12:45.694
That's a hefty increase
on the standard roll

01:12:45.694 --> 01:12:48.364
as well as being over half of
your daily caloric allowance,

01:12:48.364 --> 01:12:49.932
or, as we now use to quantify things,

01:12:49.932 --> 01:12:51.467
four McDonald's hamburgers.

01:12:51.467 --> 01:12:53.068
The least-healthy roll in the US

01:12:53.068 --> 01:12:57.172
is the caramel pecan Bon,
which is 1,090 calories.

01:12:57.172 --> 01:12:58.974
This is also the most calorific thing

01:12:58.974 --> 01:13:01.744
on the entire US menu, sort of.

01:13:01.744 --> 01:13:04.279
A single caramel pecan Bon roll

01:13:04.279 --> 01:13:07.649
is 1,090 calories, but
according to Cinnabon,

01:13:07.649 --> 01:13:09.752
if you get them in a pack of four or six,

01:13:09.752 --> 01:13:11.520
the calories of each individual roll

01:13:11.520 --> 01:13:14.523
increases to 1,160.

01:13:14.523 --> 01:13:16.792
It is unclear why that is the case,

01:13:16.792 --> 01:13:18.494
but I'm going to go ahead and guess

01:13:18.494 --> 01:13:21.430
because they dump way more frosting on it.

01:13:21.430 --> 01:13:23.098
The most-calorific thing on the UK menu

01:13:23.098 --> 01:13:24.700
actually isn't a roll, it's this,

01:13:24.700 --> 01:13:26.969
a 16-ounce cinnamon roll Chillatta.

01:13:26.969 --> 01:13:30.906
One of these contains a
whopping 1,231 calories.

01:13:30.906 --> 01:13:33.308
That means that one of these
large cinnamon roll Chillattas

01:13:33.308 --> 01:13:36.078
combined with one of our
classic cinnamon rolls in the UK

01:13:36.078 --> 01:13:37.546
would put you pretty much exactly

01:13:37.546 --> 01:13:39.782
at your 2,000-calorie daily limit.

01:13:42.518 --> 01:13:45.421
Cinnabon does not disclose
a full ingredients list

01:13:45.421 --> 01:13:47.389
in the US, only allergens.

01:13:47.389 --> 01:13:49.158
The website in the UK also didn't contain

01:13:49.158 --> 01:13:51.660
ingredients information, but once again,

01:13:51.660 --> 01:13:53.762
the box provided us with
all of the ingredients

01:13:53.762 --> 01:13:56.965
of a classic cinnamon
roll, and it is a lot.

01:13:56.965 --> 01:13:58.033
But are there any ingredients which

01:13:58.033 --> 01:13:59.101
you need to look out for?

01:13:59.101 --> 01:14:00.602
The bun itself is pretty much fine,

01:14:00.602 --> 01:14:02.504
despite the sheer number of ingredients.

01:14:02.504 --> 01:14:04.940
The things to watch out
for are actually found

01:14:04.940 --> 01:14:06.542
in the frosting.

01:14:06.542 --> 01:14:08.710
The frosting contains an
imitation vanilla extract,

01:14:08.710 --> 01:14:10.846
which in turn contains E1520.

01:14:10.846 --> 01:14:12.881
This is also known as propylene glycol.

01:14:12.881 --> 01:14:14.016
It's fairly common in foods

01:14:14.016 --> 01:14:15.984
and in small doses is used as a carrier

01:14:15.984 --> 01:14:17.953
for ingredients which
aren't soluble in water.

01:14:17.953 --> 01:14:20.222
However, it can be toxic in large doses.

01:14:20.222 --> 01:14:22.157
It's one of the main
ingredients in antifreeze,

01:14:22.157 --> 01:14:24.026
as it lowers the freezing point of water.

01:14:24.026 --> 01:14:26.462
Too much propylene glycol could lead

01:14:26.462 --> 01:14:29.531
to internal bleeding and kidney failure.

01:14:29.531 --> 01:14:31.500
Mm. The good news is that you're unlikely

01:14:31.500 --> 01:14:33.469
to ever hit these levels from food.

01:14:33.469 --> 01:14:35.037
Just don't go drinking antifreeze.

01:14:35.037 --> 01:14:38.407
The lemon extract in the
frosting also contains E102,

01:14:38.407 --> 01:14:40.742
sometimes known as yellow 5 or tartrazine.

01:14:40.742 --> 01:14:42.811
It's a somewhat controversial
yellow food dye.

01:14:42.811 --> 01:14:45.180
It was part of a panic in
the UK about food colorings

01:14:45.180 --> 01:14:46.949
causing hyperactivity in children,

01:14:46.949 --> 01:14:47.983
although eventually it was shown

01:14:47.983 --> 01:14:49.852
that there was limited evidence for this.

01:14:49.852 --> 01:14:53.322
A 2015 study also found that yellow No. 5

01:14:53.322 --> 01:14:56.959
can damage your white
blood cells, which, mm,

01:14:56.959 --> 01:14:59.661
means you're likely to
develop tumors and cancer.

01:15:00.963 --> 01:15:02.698
See us out, dancing rats.

01:15:06.768 --> 01:15:08.170
Harry: From calorie
count to portion sizes,

01:15:08.170 --> 01:15:09.538
we wanted to find out all the differences

01:15:09.538 --> 01:15:12.140
between Little Caesars
in the US and the UK.

01:15:12.140 --> 01:15:13.809
This is "Food Wars."

01:15:17.279 --> 01:15:19.481
Little Caesars in the US
sells Hot-N-Ready pizzas

01:15:19.481 --> 01:15:22.317
in one size, 14 inches.

01:15:22.317 --> 01:15:24.753
Closer to 13 ½. I'll let it slide, though.

01:15:24.753 --> 01:15:26.788
In the UK, Little Caesars
Hot-N-Ready pizzas

01:15:26.788 --> 01:15:29.191
only come in one size, 12 inches.

01:15:29.191 --> 01:15:30.392
That means that the surface area

01:15:30.392 --> 01:15:34.162
of a UK Little Caesars pizza
is 113.1 square inches.

01:15:34.162 --> 01:15:36.598
The surface area of a
US Little Caesars pizza

01:15:36.598 --> 01:15:40.035
is 153.94 square inches.

01:15:40.035 --> 01:15:44.373
That makes the pizza 36%
larger than the UK's.

01:15:44.373 --> 01:15:45.941
Now, we can get Crazy Bread in the UK,

01:15:45.941 --> 01:15:47.409
and we ordered it from our Little Caesars,

01:15:47.409 --> 01:15:48.944
but unfortunately they forgot it.

01:15:48.944 --> 01:15:50.045
If they remember your Crazy Bread,

01:15:50.045 --> 01:15:51.747
it looks like you get
four pieces with an order,

01:15:51.747 --> 01:15:52.748
according to the website.

01:15:52.748 --> 01:15:54.349
Too bad for the UK, but the US,

01:15:54.349 --> 01:15:55.684
we did get our Crazy Bread,

01:15:55.684 --> 01:15:59.855
and an order of Crazy Bread
comes with eight sticks.

01:15:59.855 --> 01:16:01.790
Eight crazy sticks.

01:16:01.790 --> 01:16:04.893
It wouldn't, of course,
be a order of Crazy Bread

01:16:04.893 --> 01:16:06.929
without the Crazy Sauce.

01:16:06.929 --> 01:16:07.896
To add insult to injury,

01:16:07.896 --> 01:16:10.265
they gave us just the Crazy
Sauce, but without the bread.

01:16:10.265 --> 01:16:11.967
Let's weight it anyway
to see how much we get.

01:16:11.967 --> 01:16:14.870
A side of Crazy Sauce in
the UK weighs 7 grams.

01:16:14.870 --> 01:16:16.572
Joe: It's 159 grams.

01:16:17.773 --> 01:16:19.841
Whoa, it's so crazy!

01:16:19.841 --> 01:16:21.276
No. It's not, of course. It's fine.

01:16:21.276 --> 01:16:22.578
I wouldn't call the sauce crazy.

01:16:22.578 --> 01:16:25.047
Misunderstood, maybe, but it feels like

01:16:25.047 --> 01:16:26.348
the sauce kind of has it under control.

01:16:26.348 --> 01:16:29.418
This is a very mild-mannered,

01:16:29.418 --> 01:16:32.321
well-thought-out, well-measured sauce.

01:16:32.321 --> 01:16:34.823
Another item available in both
countries is cheese bread.

01:16:34.823 --> 01:16:37.225
I'll say on the
medium-rare side of cooked.

01:16:37.225 --> 01:16:40.729
7.5 inches across, and 5.5 inches wide.

01:16:40.729 --> 01:16:42.631
I would like to note that in the US,

01:16:42.631 --> 01:16:45.734
our cheese bread is called
Italian cheese bread.

01:16:45.734 --> 01:16:47.903
Ooh, that's almost exactly 9 inches.

01:16:47.903 --> 01:16:48.971
7 inches.

01:16:48.971 --> 01:16:51.006
If you want to get a small
pizza at a Little Caesars,

01:16:51.006 --> 01:16:54.109
just get the Italian cheese
bread and a side of sauce.

01:16:54.109 --> 01:16:56.078
Some assembly required.

01:16:58.113 --> 01:17:00.282
Here are all the Little
Caesars menu items in the UK

01:17:00.282 --> 01:17:01.750
that you won't find in the US.

01:17:01.750 --> 01:17:04.853
Here is all of the
Little Caesars menu items

01:17:04.853 --> 01:17:07.389
you can get in the US that
you won't find in the UK.

01:17:07.389 --> 01:17:09.358
Before we talk about some of
the default pizza options,

01:17:09.358 --> 01:17:11.159
we'll talk about some of
the customization options

01:17:11.159 --> 01:17:13.562
you get in the UK that you
guys can't change in the US.

01:17:13.562 --> 01:17:16.331
For example, over here we can
sub out the tomato sauce base

01:17:16.331 --> 01:17:18.767
for barbecue sauce or peri-peri sauce.

01:17:18.767 --> 01:17:20.435
I think the peri-peri
sauce is kind of a nod

01:17:20.435 --> 01:17:22.204
to the UK's obsession with peri-peri.

01:17:22.204 --> 01:17:23.772
You guys know how much
we love our Nando's.

01:17:23.772 --> 01:17:25.607
I think Little Caesars are
trying to get in on that as well.

01:17:25.607 --> 01:17:28.076
Nando's just dropped to
their knees in Tesco,

01:17:28.076 --> 01:17:29.711
just like, oh, my God, no.

01:17:29.711 --> 01:17:31.113
The peri-peri option doesn't stop there,

01:17:31.113 --> 01:17:32.681
because you can also
add peri-peri seasoning

01:17:32.681 --> 01:17:34.549
to the crust of your
pizza at Little Caesars.

01:17:34.549 --> 01:17:35.851
The US customizations.

01:17:35.851 --> 01:17:37.686
For the crust, round,
which I guess is regular.

01:17:37.686 --> 01:17:40.188
But we also have thin
crust, stuffed crust,

01:17:40.188 --> 01:17:41.823
Detroit-style deep dish,

01:17:41.823 --> 01:17:43.659
and stuffed-crust deep dish.

01:17:43.659 --> 01:17:46.061
For bake, we also do a well done.

01:17:46.061 --> 01:17:47.763
Cheese, you can get,
obviously regular cheese,

01:17:47.763 --> 01:17:49.164
but no cheese or light cheese.

01:17:49.164 --> 01:17:52.701
Sauce, same thing, light,
normal, extra, no sauce.

01:17:52.701 --> 01:17:54.536
Now let's talk about some of
the pizza options in the UK

01:17:54.536 --> 01:17:56.204
you won't find on the menu in the US.

01:17:56.204 --> 01:17:59.307
Here we have the barbecue chicken pizza.

01:17:59.307 --> 01:18:01.209
If you stare at this thing for too long,

01:18:01.209 --> 01:18:04.546
you will be lured into a hypnotic trance.

01:18:06.214 --> 01:18:08.016
The barbecue sauce is very sweet

01:18:08.016 --> 01:18:10.185
and kind of becomes the main
thing that you can taste.

01:18:10.185 --> 01:18:11.920
If that's your thing,
do it. Not really mine.

01:18:11.920 --> 01:18:14.356
Over this way, we have
the spicy peri-peri.

01:18:15.590 --> 01:18:17.192
The peri-peri is quite gentle.

01:18:17.192 --> 01:18:18.760
Just, like, a little bit of heat, maybe.

01:18:18.760 --> 01:18:20.996
But to call that a spicy peri-peri,

01:18:20.996 --> 01:18:22.397
I think they've oversold the spicy,

01:18:22.397 --> 01:18:24.199
and they've also kind of
oversold the peri-peri.

01:18:24.199 --> 01:18:25.567
Our next pizza is this one.

01:18:25.567 --> 01:18:27.202
It's called the quattro.

01:18:27.202 --> 01:18:28.403
What they've done is take a pizza

01:18:28.403 --> 01:18:30.772
and divide it into fours and
then top those individually.

01:18:30.772 --> 01:18:32.240
So you have two slices of Margherita,

01:18:32.240 --> 01:18:34.776
two slices of pepperoni, two
slices chicken and mushroom,

01:18:34.776 --> 01:18:38.013
and two slices of peppers,
tomatoes, and sweet corn.

01:18:38.013 --> 01:18:40.182
All right, this says "SC pepperoni,"

01:18:40.182 --> 01:18:42.184
stuffed-crust pepperoni.

01:18:42.184 --> 01:18:43.218
I mean, this looks, like,

01:18:43.218 --> 01:18:44.453
I mean, pretty generous
with the pepperoni.

01:18:44.453 --> 01:18:47.422
It's a bit more
neon-colored than I'd like.

01:18:47.422 --> 01:18:49.758
The crust, of course, is
stuffed with mozzarella cheese.

01:18:49.758 --> 01:18:51.760
Eh, yeah, not bad.

01:18:51.760 --> 01:18:52.794
Let's just try.

01:18:56.164 --> 01:18:56.965
Sorry, stuffed crust.

01:18:56.965 --> 01:18:58.133
People just kind of don't care about it.

01:18:58.133 --> 01:19:01.236
Something newer to the Little
Caesars menu here in the US,

01:19:01.236 --> 01:19:02.938
there's something called Slice-N-Stix,

01:19:02.938 --> 01:19:05.674
which is half pizza, half breadsticks.

01:19:05.674 --> 01:19:07.275
For the consumer who
wants a little variety,

01:19:07.275 --> 01:19:09.044
just them by themselves don't
want to get a whole pizza

01:19:09.044 --> 01:19:10.112
and a whole thing of sticks.

01:19:10.112 --> 01:19:11.580
I want to point out that Slice-N-Stix

01:19:11.580 --> 01:19:13.882
come in what I think is
this, aka the classic.

01:19:13.882 --> 01:19:15.917
But you also get bacon Slice-N-Stix

01:19:15.917 --> 01:19:17.719
and jalapeño Slice-N-Stix.

01:19:17.719 --> 01:19:20.555
Throw on your grass skirts,
ladies and gentlemen.

01:19:20.555 --> 01:19:22.357
We're going to Hawaii.

01:19:22.357 --> 01:19:24.359
This is the Hula Hawaiian,

01:19:24.359 --> 01:19:28.363
which of course is bacon and pineapple.

01:19:29.464 --> 01:19:31.533
I think pineapple on
pizza's perfectly fine.

01:19:31.533 --> 01:19:33.301
This Hawaiian's not very good, but.

01:19:33.301 --> 01:19:34.636
The before-mentioned thin crust.

01:19:34.636 --> 01:19:36.304
Thin-crust pepperoni.

01:19:36.304 --> 01:19:38.106
It's pretty good, if you want
to pay the exact same price

01:19:38.106 --> 01:19:39.474
for literally half the pizza.

01:19:39.474 --> 01:19:40.542
So far for Little Caesars,

01:19:40.542 --> 01:19:42.244
the pepperoni's winning across the board.

01:19:42.244 --> 01:19:44.646
Little Caesars got me through
some financial rough patches,

01:19:44.646 --> 01:19:45.747
so I don't want to be too hard on them.

01:19:45.747 --> 01:19:47.115
But, I mean, I'm eating it, I'm like,

01:19:47.115 --> 01:19:49.985
oh, yeah, my early 20s. Great.

01:19:49.985 --> 01:19:53.755
5 Meat Feast. Count with me here.

01:19:53.755 --> 01:19:57.092
Pepperoni, ham, sausage, hamburger?

01:19:57.092 --> 01:19:59.661
Bacon, and, yeah, I think
it's, like, a seasoned beef.

01:19:59.661 --> 01:20:01.396
I don't like when they go ham and pork

01:20:01.396 --> 01:20:02.798
are two different meats. I
know they're two different,

01:20:02.798 --> 01:20:04.666
but it's kind of like,
they're pretty close.

01:20:04.666 --> 01:20:07.435
Or it should be five meats, two animals.

01:20:07.435 --> 01:20:09.905
The seasoned ground beef or sausage

01:20:09.905 --> 01:20:12.340
looks a lot like mouse turds,

01:20:12.340 --> 01:20:14.509
making this incredibly unappetizing.

01:20:14.509 --> 01:20:16.745
[mouse squeaks]

01:20:16.745 --> 01:20:18.013
You're trying too hard with this one.

01:20:18.013 --> 01:20:19.648
Then we have a few
deluxe options in the UK,

01:20:19.648 --> 01:20:21.483
starting with a pepperoni deluxe.

01:20:21.483 --> 01:20:22.684
If you're wondering what makes this deluxe

01:20:22.684 --> 01:20:24.052
when compared to a standard pepperoni,

01:20:24.052 --> 01:20:26.621
they just take some extra
pepperoni and add it to the pizza

01:20:26.621 --> 01:20:29.124
and then sprinkle it
with Grana Padano cheese.

01:20:29.124 --> 01:20:30.725
I will say, like, it does look

01:20:30.725 --> 01:20:32.427
slightly more deluxe than the rest.

01:20:32.427 --> 01:20:33.995
Let's see if it tastes deluxe.

01:20:35.163 --> 01:20:36.464
It might just be a placebo effect,

01:20:36.464 --> 01:20:39.100
but it does kind of taste like
the best one I've had so far.

01:20:39.100 --> 01:20:41.269
I don't know if I'd stretch
to deluxe as an adjective,

01:20:41.269 --> 01:20:42.838
but slightly better for sure.

01:20:42.838 --> 01:20:45.006
Maybe just rename it the
slightly better pepperoni.

01:20:45.006 --> 01:20:47.275
Something that here in the
US our Little Caesars has --

01:20:47.275 --> 01:20:48.376
I've never heard of this before,

01:20:48.376 --> 01:20:50.612
and I don't know exactly
what they're doing --

01:20:50.612 --> 01:20:52.614
a series of pizzas, two pizzas,

01:20:52.614 --> 01:20:54.282
called, and this is all one word,

01:20:54.282 --> 01:20:56.117
Extramostbestest.

01:20:56.117 --> 01:20:58.820
The Extramostbestest cheese and pepperoni.

01:20:58.820 --> 01:21:01.623
Is this just rebranding the
plain cheese and the plain?

01:21:01.623 --> 01:21:03.892
What makes this Extramostbestest?

01:21:03.892 --> 01:21:05.493
All right, let's find out together.

01:21:05.493 --> 01:21:07.796
It's an upgrade take on
their classic pepperoni pizza

01:21:07.796 --> 01:21:11.633
that offers 80% more pepperoni,
uses 25% more cheese.

01:21:11.633 --> 01:21:13.335
OK, so more cheese and more pepperoni.

01:21:13.335 --> 01:21:16.438
Wait a second, wait a
second, wait a second.

01:21:16.438 --> 01:21:18.740
Can someone grab a screenshot of that?

01:21:18.740 --> 01:21:20.475
We'll compare this to,

01:21:20.475 --> 01:21:21.810
there's a pepperoni that's coming up

01:21:21.810 --> 01:21:23.845
that has a lot more on here, so.

01:21:23.845 --> 01:21:25.413
Next up is another deluxe option.

01:21:25.413 --> 01:21:26.648
The Margherita deluxe.

01:21:26.648 --> 01:21:28.316
Just as a linguistic note, in the UK,

01:21:28.316 --> 01:21:30.151
if you see a cheese-and-tomato
pizza on the menu,

01:21:30.151 --> 01:21:32.020
it's almost always referred
to as a Margherita.

01:21:32.020 --> 01:21:33.388
Everyone knows what that means.

01:21:33.388 --> 01:21:35.123
It's a slightly more
traditional Italian way

01:21:35.123 --> 01:21:36.391
of saying cheese and tomato.

01:21:36.391 --> 01:21:37.692
Whereas in America, it seems like you guys

01:21:37.692 --> 01:21:39.327
all just have to say cheese pizza

01:21:39.327 --> 01:21:40.662
or you don't really understand
what you're getting.

01:21:40.662 --> 01:21:42.364
To turn this Margherita
into a deluxe version,

01:21:42.364 --> 01:21:43.398
it seems like all they've really done

01:21:43.398 --> 01:21:45.000
is added, I think, some herbs

01:21:45.000 --> 01:21:47.269
and then some chopped-up
pieces of actual tomato.

01:21:48.803 --> 01:21:50.372
All I really have to
say about most of these

01:21:50.372 --> 01:21:51.640
is that they're fine.

01:21:51.640 --> 01:21:54.509
Our final deluxe pizza exclusive
is the mushroom deluxe.

01:21:54.509 --> 01:21:56.611
Again, it looks like a fairly
standard mushroom pizza,

01:21:56.611 --> 01:21:57.913
with, I think, the herbs again

01:21:57.913 --> 01:21:59.814
and the Grana Padano
sprinkled around the edge.

01:21:59.814 --> 01:22:01.149
It's also funny that they call this one

01:22:01.149 --> 01:22:03.151
a mushroom deluxe pizza,
because there isn't actually

01:22:03.151 --> 01:22:04.519
a standard mushroom on the menu.

01:22:04.519 --> 01:22:06.922
So I guess if you like
mushrooms on your pizza,

01:22:06.922 --> 01:22:09.324
you're being forced into having
the deluxe, fancy version.

01:22:09.324 --> 01:22:11.159
This [drumroll]

01:22:11.159 --> 01:22:15.063
is the Old World Fanceroni Pepperoni.

01:22:15.063 --> 01:22:16.298
Guh-roan.

01:22:16.298 --> 01:22:19.434
Now that's pepperoni! Let's go!

01:22:19.434 --> 01:22:22.103
The cups? Oh, yeah!

01:22:22.103 --> 01:22:23.805
Now, remember that one a
minute ago that we just saw

01:22:23.805 --> 01:22:25.507
that was the Extrabestmostest

01:22:25.507 --> 01:22:26.508
or whatever the hell it's called?

01:22:26.508 --> 01:22:28.643
Yes. Yes!

01:22:30.378 --> 01:22:31.513
Oh, they're crispy!

01:22:31.513 --> 01:22:32.447
This is pretty good.

01:22:32.447 --> 01:22:34.582
I will say, the dough on all these pizzas

01:22:34.582 --> 01:22:36.184
are a lot spongier.

01:22:36.184 --> 01:22:38.853
I'm hoping that that is a
choice to make it spongier

01:22:38.853 --> 01:22:41.022
and not that they just
didn't cook these through.

01:22:41.022 --> 01:22:42.657
I'll find out in a couple hours.

01:22:42.657 --> 01:22:43.858
Of the regular round pizzas,

01:22:43.858 --> 01:22:47.195
last and certainly least, veggie.

01:22:47.195 --> 01:22:48.096
As before mentioned,

01:22:48.096 --> 01:22:50.065
a version of pizza you
can get here in the US,

01:22:50.065 --> 01:22:54.636
we have a Detroit-style deep-dish
pizza at Little Caesars.

01:22:54.636 --> 01:22:57.639
You can get the ultimate
supreme, the veggie,

01:22:57.639 --> 01:22:59.808
the pepperoni, the 3 Meat,

01:22:59.808 --> 01:23:01.710
Hawaiian, and just regular cheese.

01:23:01.710 --> 01:23:03.345
I went with the pepperoni
because I feel that's

01:23:03.345 --> 01:23:04.646
classic Detroit style.

01:23:04.646 --> 01:23:05.780
Hm.

01:23:05.780 --> 01:23:08.416
Detroit, let us know in
the comments how they did.

01:23:08.416 --> 01:23:09.851
True Detroit style puts the sauce,

01:23:09.851 --> 01:23:11.786
or a little bit of sauce
on top. They did not.

01:23:11.786 --> 01:23:14.389
So it just looks like
a really thick pizza.

01:23:14.389 --> 01:23:15.657
We love our bread in this country.

01:23:16.758 --> 01:23:20.128
I would suggest against
selling this in Detroit.

01:23:20.128 --> 01:23:23.064
So, what we have here
is the UK-only pizza.

01:23:23.064 --> 01:23:25.000
What we've done is take all
of the customization options

01:23:25.000 --> 01:23:26.368
you can only find in the UK

01:23:26.368 --> 01:23:28.203
and combine them onto one pizza.

01:23:28.203 --> 01:23:30.572
So what this pizza has is
the peri-peri sauce base,

01:23:30.572 --> 01:23:32.674
a barbecue sauce drizzle,
peri-peri chicken,

01:23:32.674 --> 01:23:36.177
regular chicken, red onions,
sweet corn, and tomatoes.

01:23:38.079 --> 01:23:40.081
Honestly, that's not terrible.

01:23:40.081 --> 01:23:42.784
Far from the worst UK-only
creation that we've ever made.

01:23:42.784 --> 01:23:45.687
The peri sauce base seems
to just be tomato sauce

01:23:45.687 --> 01:23:48.023
with a bit of peri seasoning
kind of mixed into it.

01:23:48.023 --> 01:23:49.891
So you still get a bit of
the sweetness from the tomato

01:23:49.891 --> 01:23:51.993
and a very gentle warmth from that.

01:23:51.993 --> 01:23:54.529
The barbecue sauce is kind
of the dominant flavor again,

01:23:54.529 --> 01:23:57.532
but as far as UK-only
pizzas go, it's not bad.

01:23:57.532 --> 01:23:59.100
A segment that, Yuelei,

01:23:59.100 --> 01:24:01.469
we haven't done this in
forever, it feels like!

01:24:01.469 --> 01:24:03.471
A USA-only! That's right!

01:24:03.471 --> 01:24:05.240
This is a pizza you can only get

01:24:05.240 --> 01:24:08.143
in the United States of
America at a Little Caesars.

01:24:08.143 --> 01:24:09.744
Of all the many USA-only options,

01:24:09.744 --> 01:24:12.447
we went with a well-done
pizza with a stuffed crust,

01:24:12.447 --> 01:24:14.115
extra sauce, light cheese,

01:24:14.115 --> 01:24:16.951
Old World pepperoni,
pineapple, and black olives.

01:24:16.951 --> 01:24:19.988
Oh, man. Wah-wah.

01:24:19.988 --> 01:24:22.857
The extra sauce I think
is what really -- oh, God.

01:24:22.857 --> 01:24:24.492
The extra sauce is what
really ruined this,

01:24:24.492 --> 01:24:26.461
'cause now it's just all sliding off.

01:24:26.461 --> 01:24:27.262
Ah.

01:24:30.331 --> 01:24:31.232
It's really bad.

01:24:31.232 --> 01:24:33.034
And it's really bad
because it's falling apart.

01:24:33.034 --> 01:24:34.369
And also we got this separately,

01:24:34.369 --> 01:24:36.371
so this actually just
came out of the oven.

01:24:36.371 --> 01:24:37.472
It's really hot.

01:24:37.472 --> 01:24:38.406
Then we're on to the sides.

01:24:38.406 --> 01:24:39.974
We have two exclusives in the UK.

01:24:39.974 --> 01:24:41.409
Now, while we didn't get
any of the Crazy Bread,

01:24:41.409 --> 01:24:42.544
at least we got the Crazy Puffs.

01:24:42.544 --> 01:24:43.411
They take the dough,

01:24:43.411 --> 01:24:45.914
they form it into a kind
of cupcake, muffin shape,

01:24:45.914 --> 01:24:47.682
which is then filled
with some tomato sauce

01:24:47.682 --> 01:24:48.983
and cheese and pepperoni.

01:24:50.218 --> 01:24:51.719
You can see the grease,
like, dripping out of that

01:24:51.719 --> 01:24:52.587
as soon as I bit in.

01:24:52.587 --> 01:24:53.421
They're not bad.

01:24:53.421 --> 01:24:55.023
They're on a mid-level of the crazy scale.

01:24:55.023 --> 01:24:56.691
And we can also get veggie Crazy Puff.

01:24:56.691 --> 01:24:58.126
It's the same cheese and sauce base,

01:24:58.126 --> 01:24:59.727
but then instead of the pepperoni,

01:24:59.727 --> 01:25:01.629
they've added corn, peppers, and onion.

01:25:01.629 --> 01:25:04.332
We also have stuffed Crazy Bread.

01:25:04.332 --> 01:25:06.201
Remember that Crazy Bread from earlier?

01:25:06.201 --> 01:25:07.402
Now it's stuffed.

01:25:07.402 --> 01:25:08.803
What the?

01:25:09.637 --> 01:25:12.273
This is like a giant mozzarella stick.

01:25:12.273 --> 01:25:13.108
Isn't really melted.

01:25:15.143 --> 01:25:17.212
Oh, man, remarkably bland. Avoid.

01:25:17.212 --> 01:25:18.513
Caesars' got wings.

01:25:18.513 --> 01:25:20.882
Oven-roasted, barbecue, and Buffalo.

01:25:20.882 --> 01:25:21.916
I'm starting to get a headache.

01:25:21.916 --> 01:25:23.318
I can't for the life of me

01:25:23.318 --> 01:25:25.653
pinpoint what is making
me suddenly so nauseous.

01:25:25.653 --> 01:25:27.322
We have a couple of
exclusive sauces in the UK,

01:25:27.322 --> 01:25:28.590
which means it's time for:

01:25:28.590 --> 01:25:30.325
Sauce Talk.

01:25:30.325 --> 01:25:31.459
We have three sauces in the UK

01:25:31.459 --> 01:25:33.161
that you won't find on an American menu,

01:25:33.161 --> 01:25:34.696
which is garlic and herb.

01:25:34.696 --> 01:25:36.498
When you order at Domino's,
it comes by default

01:25:36.498 --> 01:25:38.032
with a garlic and herb dip in the UK.

01:25:38.032 --> 01:25:40.602
People go crazy for that
dip. People really love it.

01:25:40.602 --> 01:25:42.070
So a few other places
have tried to kind of

01:25:42.070 --> 01:25:44.072
jump on that bandwagon,
and this is their version.

01:25:44.072 --> 01:25:45.840
We then have a peri-peri sauce,

01:25:45.840 --> 01:25:47.942
and finally we have a ketchup on the menu.

01:25:47.942 --> 01:25:50.578
I'm questioning anybody who
eats pizza with ketchup.

01:25:50.578 --> 01:25:51.446
I'm gonna be honest.

01:25:51.446 --> 01:25:52.914
And we don't really even have any sides

01:25:52.914 --> 01:25:54.682
on the menu that go with ketchup, so.

01:25:54.682 --> 01:25:56.551
The garlic and herb is defeating me.

01:25:56.551 --> 01:25:58.052
Leon, help.

01:25:58.052 --> 01:25:58.887
[glass breaks]

01:26:01.089 --> 01:26:02.924
It's got quite a harsh taste, actually.

01:26:02.924 --> 01:26:03.992
Surprisingly harsh.

01:26:03.992 --> 01:26:05.760
Try the peri-peri.

01:26:05.760 --> 01:26:08.296
So, the thing is, peri-peri
has a very distinct flavor.

01:26:08.296 --> 01:26:09.931
It's a specific type of chili.

01:26:09.931 --> 01:26:11.299
All I'm really getting
from this is just, like,

01:26:11.299 --> 01:26:12.767
chili-pepper heat. No.

01:26:12.767 --> 01:26:13.735
You have ketchup.

01:26:13.735 --> 01:26:15.036
Can't quite put my finger on it.

01:26:15.036 --> 01:26:16.905
I'm going to literally
put my finger on it.

01:26:18.039 --> 01:26:20.708
It's got almost more of, like,
a tomato-soup flavor to it,

01:26:20.708 --> 01:26:21.643
which I don't hate.

01:26:21.643 --> 01:26:24.179
After my preamble about
how much I do not think

01:26:24.179 --> 01:26:26.080
ketchup should go with any
of these pizzas, it actually

01:26:26.080 --> 01:26:28.283
ended up being my favorite
of these three sauces.

01:26:28.283 --> 01:26:29.384
I think that's more of a comment

01:26:29.384 --> 01:26:31.119
on the other two not being very nice

01:26:31.119 --> 01:26:32.687
rather than the ketchup being good.

01:26:32.687 --> 01:26:34.756
You have a variety of four exclusive

01:26:34.756 --> 01:26:36.391
delicious dipping sauces.

01:26:36.391 --> 01:26:38.193
Butter garlic flavor,

01:26:38.193 --> 01:26:39.694
Buffalo ranch,

01:26:39.694 --> 01:26:41.629
cheezy jalapeño,

01:26:41.629 --> 01:26:42.664
and just regular ranch.

01:26:42.664 --> 01:26:44.766
Little Caesars in the UK
also has one dessert option

01:26:44.766 --> 01:26:47.435
you won't find in the US,
chocolate chip cookies.

01:26:47.435 --> 01:26:49.170
So, we got desserts.

01:26:49.170 --> 01:26:50.872
Cookie dough brownies.

01:26:50.872 --> 01:26:53.508
One has Twix pieces,
the other has M&amp;M minis.

01:26:55.076 --> 01:26:56.110
Very, very sweet.

01:26:56.110 --> 01:26:57.212
Kind of weird, actually.

01:26:57.212 --> 01:26:58.379
Finally, let's talk about drinks.

01:26:58.379 --> 01:27:00.949
In the UK, Little Caesars
carries Coca-Cola branded drinks,

01:27:00.949 --> 01:27:02.617
including, obviously, Coca-Cola,

01:27:02.617 --> 01:27:05.620
but then also things like
Monster Energy and Oasis,

01:27:05.620 --> 01:27:07.455
which is a bit of a British classic.

01:27:07.455 --> 01:27:09.724
Comes in either citrus
punch or summer fruits.

01:27:09.724 --> 01:27:13.228
It's kind of like a diluted
fruit juice. Refreshing.

01:27:13.228 --> 01:27:14.696
Finally, I can have something to drink.

01:27:14.696 --> 01:27:16.965
They had Coke products.
We got Pepsi products.

01:27:16.965 --> 01:27:18.866
Oh, you know, the classic Pepsi.

01:27:18.866 --> 01:27:20.735
Mug root beer, Mountain Dew,

01:27:20.735 --> 01:27:21.903
and Starry!

01:27:21.903 --> 01:27:24.138
It's the new one. It's
what replaced Sierra Mist.

01:27:24.138 --> 01:27:26.274
RIP Sierra Mist, thank God.

01:27:27.775 --> 01:27:29.777
Yeah, that's, like, exactly
what 7Up tastes like.

01:27:29.777 --> 01:27:31.779
They invented 7Up. Great job, guys.

01:27:33.948 --> 01:27:35.483
Unfortunately, Little Caesars in the UK

01:27:35.483 --> 01:27:37.986
doesn't give us a full nutritional
breakdown, only calories.

01:27:37.986 --> 01:27:41.856
A Hot-N-Ready cheese pizza
in the UK is 1,700 calories.

01:27:41.856 --> 01:27:44.592
That's 85% of your
recommended daily allowance.

01:27:44.592 --> 01:27:48.396
A Hot-N-Ready US cheese
pizza is 1,950 calories.

01:27:48.396 --> 01:27:52.700
That's 97.5% of your
recommended daily intake.

01:27:52.700 --> 01:27:54.269
Also, the sodium.

01:27:54.269 --> 01:27:55.136
Good Lord.

01:27:55.136 --> 01:27:59.173
160% of your recommended daily intake.

01:27:59.173 --> 01:28:02.110
The most calorific pizza in
the UK is this, 3 Meat Treat.

01:28:02.110 --> 01:28:05.246
A whole one of these
contains 1,910 calories,

01:28:05.246 --> 01:28:07.949
or 95.5% of your daily allowance.

01:28:07.949 --> 01:28:09.250
We also have the 3 Meat Treat,

01:28:09.250 --> 01:28:12.453
but ours is 2,870 calories.

01:28:12.453 --> 01:28:15.423
That's 960 calories more
than the UK version.

01:28:15.423 --> 01:28:20.361
And ours is 143.5% of your daily calories.

01:28:20.361 --> 01:28:21.829
You're not going to believe this.

01:28:21.829 --> 01:28:25.566
The 3 Meat Treat isn't
our biggest-caloried pie.

01:28:25.566 --> 01:28:28.269
That award goes to, oddly enough, this:

01:28:28.269 --> 01:28:31.572
the pepperoni and cheese
stuffed-crust pizza.

01:28:31.572 --> 01:28:34.642
This whole thing, 3,340 calories.

01:28:34.642 --> 01:28:39.280
That's 167% of your daily calorie intake.

01:28:39.280 --> 01:28:40.548
And, of course, the sodium.

01:28:40.548 --> 01:28:41.683
The sodium!

01:28:41.683 --> 01:28:46.387
380% your recommended daily sodium intake.

01:28:46.387 --> 01:28:48.389
So, the pizza's cut in eight slices.

01:28:48.389 --> 01:28:52.727
So one slice contains
1,094 milligrams of sodium,

01:28:52.727 --> 01:28:55.763
which is almost half of your daily amount

01:28:55.763 --> 01:28:58.366
in just one slice.

01:28:58.366 --> 01:29:00.335
RIP my kidneys.

01:29:02.470 --> 01:29:04.739
A Hot-N-Ready Margherita
or pepperoni in the UK

01:29:04.739 --> 01:29:06.107
will cost you £5,

01:29:06.107 --> 01:29:08.843
which at the time of
recording this is $6.04.

01:29:08.843 --> 01:29:10.278
A Little Caesars Hot-N-Ready pizza

01:29:10.278 --> 01:29:14.115
has become a contentious topic
in the US in recent years.

01:29:14.115 --> 01:29:16.851
Forever, this was just $5.

01:29:16.851 --> 01:29:19.187
But in 2022, they raised the price

01:29:19.187 --> 01:29:22.557
for the first time in nearly 25 years.

01:29:22.557 --> 01:29:24.192
Price can vary depending on your location,

01:29:24.192 --> 01:29:26.561
but where I am here in
Southern California,

01:29:26.561 --> 01:29:29.931
a Hot-N-Ready cheese pizza is now $6.49,

01:29:29.931 --> 01:29:31.999
or £5.40.

01:29:31.999 --> 01:29:34.502
Our most expensive pizzas
are the ultimate supreme,

01:29:34.502 --> 01:29:37.438
spicy peri-peri, barbecue
chicken, and 3 Meat Treat,

01:29:37.438 --> 01:29:39.207
which will all cost you £10.

01:29:39.207 --> 01:29:41.209
This was my first time
trying Little Caesars pizza,

01:29:41.209 --> 01:29:43.644
because currently there is only
one of them in the whole UK.

01:29:43.644 --> 01:29:45.313
It's in Chellaston, just near Derby.

01:29:45.313 --> 01:29:47.648
Having now tried it, and also
with the context of the price,

01:29:47.648 --> 01:29:48.950
I think I'm fairly confident in saying

01:29:48.950 --> 01:29:51.052
this is a pretty low-rung pizza.

01:29:51.052 --> 01:29:53.521
It is very rare to find
anything of this size

01:29:53.521 --> 01:29:56.124
for £5 in the UK when you come to pizzas.

01:29:56.124 --> 01:29:57.692
But in kind of return for that,

01:29:57.692 --> 01:29:59.026
you're not getting the best quality.

01:29:59.026 --> 01:30:01.362
I think in terms of my taste
of pizza power rankings

01:30:01.362 --> 01:30:03.531
for the UK, this would
be sitting fairly low.

01:30:03.531 --> 01:30:06.033
But for £5, it's kind of hard to complain,

01:30:06.033 --> 01:30:07.368
because that is quite cheap.

01:30:07.368 --> 01:30:08.803
I don't know. How do
you feel about it, Joe?

01:30:08.803 --> 01:30:10.505
When researching for this video,

01:30:10.505 --> 01:30:13.608
I looked it up, and I was
surprised to find out,

01:30:13.608 --> 01:30:15.977
and you might be surprised
as well to learn this,

01:30:15.977 --> 01:30:19.914
Little Caesars is the third-biggest
pizza chain in America.

01:30:19.914 --> 01:30:20.882
Totally surprised.

01:30:20.882 --> 01:30:22.917
Little Caesars recently became

01:30:22.917 --> 01:30:24.886
the official pizza of the NFL.

01:30:24.886 --> 01:30:25.720
What?

01:30:25.720 --> 01:30:27.422
I always thought, this
is just me talking here,

01:30:27.422 --> 01:30:30.825
Little Caesars was always
the cheapest option.

01:30:30.825 --> 01:30:33.694
Also the quality was never that good.

01:30:33.694 --> 01:30:35.563
So I was surprised to learn

01:30:35.563 --> 01:30:37.865
that this pizza is, A, still around,

01:30:37.865 --> 01:30:39.400
B, very popular,

01:30:39.400 --> 01:30:42.236
and, C, after this video, not that bad.

01:30:42.236 --> 01:30:43.638
I dogged on Little Caesars for a while,

01:30:43.638 --> 01:30:45.139
but, I mean, I've had worse.

01:30:45.740 --> 01:30:47.208
Harry: From calorie
count to portion sizes,

01:30:47.208 --> 01:30:48.609
we wanted to find out all the differences

01:30:48.609 --> 01:30:51.345
between Tim Hortons in the US and the UK.

01:30:51.345 --> 01:30:53.014
This is "Food Wars."

01:30:56.517 --> 01:30:59.587
Coffees at a UK Tim Hortons
come in three portion sizes:

01:30:59.587 --> 01:31:01.489
a small, which is 12 ounces;

01:31:01.489 --> 01:31:03.424
a regular, which is 16 ounces;

01:31:03.424 --> 01:31:05.593
and a large, which is 20 ounces.

01:31:05.593 --> 01:31:07.695
The hot coffee from a US Tim Hortons

01:31:07.695 --> 01:31:09.664
comes in four sizes:

01:31:09.664 --> 01:31:11.566
small, 10 ounces;

01:31:11.566 --> 01:31:13.601
medium, 15 ounces;

01:31:13.601 --> 01:31:15.269
large, 20 ounces;

01:31:15.269 --> 01:31:18.539
and extra large, 24 ounces.

01:31:18.539 --> 01:31:20.341
Harry: Let's measure the
largest coffee in both countries

01:31:20.341 --> 01:31:22.443
to see if we're getting as
much as we've been promised.

01:31:22.443 --> 01:31:25.146
Irene: It's supposed to be
24 ounces. It's 22 ounces.

01:31:25.146 --> 01:31:26.747
So we're missing 2 ounces.

01:31:26.747 --> 01:31:27.815
I don't know where they went.

01:31:27.815 --> 01:31:30.218
I personally don't care if
there's 2 ounces missing,

01:31:30.218 --> 01:31:31.052
but I feel like there are people

01:31:31.052 --> 01:31:32.820
who would take this very seriously.

01:31:32.820 --> 01:31:34.956
I assume if you're getting an extra large,

01:31:34.956 --> 01:31:37.225
you want all 24 ounces.

01:31:37.225 --> 01:31:39.594
They've actually only given us 18 ounces.

01:31:39.594 --> 01:31:41.162
2 whole ounces missing.

01:31:41.162 --> 01:31:43.130
And it doesn't stop there.

01:31:43.130 --> 01:31:46.767
This is the Take 12 coffee traveler,

01:31:46.767 --> 01:31:49.670
which is the size of a
small child, I feel like,

01:31:49.670 --> 01:31:52.573
for when you need 12 cups
of coffee for yourself

01:31:52.573 --> 01:31:53.674
or I assume friends,

01:31:53.674 --> 01:31:55.776
but probably yourself, honestly.

01:31:57.411 --> 01:31:58.446
I don't drink coffee,

01:31:58.446 --> 01:31:59.447
so if I drank this whole thing,

01:31:59.447 --> 01:32:00.548
I think I would die.

01:32:00.548 --> 01:32:01.382
You know how people are like,

01:32:01.382 --> 01:32:03.451
"Oh, this is how you'd
kill a Victorian child"?

01:32:03.451 --> 01:32:05.386
Like, this is how you would kill me.

01:32:05.386 --> 01:32:07.922
I feel like this is what
Joe drinks every morning

01:32:07.922 --> 01:32:09.524
if we're being honest.

01:32:09.524 --> 01:32:11.125
Tim Hortons' signature Iced Capps

01:32:11.125 --> 01:32:12.693
also come in three sizes in the UK,

01:32:12.693 --> 01:32:14.128
and they're supposed to be the same sizes

01:32:14.128 --> 01:32:15.162
as our hot coffees,

01:32:15.162 --> 01:32:17.732
12, 16, and 20 ounces.

01:32:17.732 --> 01:32:19.100
When we got these, I was shocked.

01:32:19.100 --> 01:32:19.934
I'd never seen one before,

01:32:19.934 --> 01:32:21.135
and they kind of look like slushies.

01:32:21.135 --> 01:32:23.137
They've sort of melted a little bit

01:32:23.137 --> 01:32:24.839
and gone a little bit sad.

01:32:24.839 --> 01:32:27.208
Our Iced Capps only come in three sizes:

01:32:27.208 --> 01:32:29.043
small, 12 ounces;

01:32:29.043 --> 01:32:30.545
medium, 16 ounces;

01:32:30.545 --> 01:32:32.747
and large, 20 ounces.

01:32:32.747 --> 01:32:34.515
So the same as the UK.

01:32:36.951 --> 01:32:39.186
OK, actually really similar to a Coolatta.

01:32:39.186 --> 01:32:40.888
Like, very, very similar.

01:32:40.888 --> 01:32:41.923
Harry: Again, let's check the biggest one

01:32:41.923 --> 01:32:44.158
to see if we're getting as
much as we've been promised.

01:32:45.026 --> 01:32:46.160
Oh, there's a big lump.

01:32:46.160 --> 01:32:48.429
Oh, no. Oh, no. Oh, no.

01:32:48.429 --> 01:32:49.297
Ah!

01:32:49.297 --> 01:32:51.032
Ah.

01:32:51.032 --> 01:32:53.968
It's just under 16 ounces.

01:32:53.968 --> 01:32:56.837
And it's supposed to be 20,
so we're missing 4 ounces.

01:32:56.837 --> 01:32:59.240
Maybe they gave us 4 ounces of
whipped cream. I don't know.

01:32:59.240 --> 01:33:01.709
The liquid line is only
actually coming up to,

01:33:01.709 --> 01:33:03.811
like, 13 fluid ounces.

01:33:03.811 --> 01:33:06.380
There is another line
of, like, foamy stuff,

01:33:06.380 --> 01:33:09.750
which takes you closer to 17.

01:33:09.750 --> 01:33:11.285
I don't know how much
you can count the foam,

01:33:11.285 --> 01:33:13.354
because I feel like
that's not proper liquid.

01:33:13.354 --> 01:33:15.623
I don't know enough about fluid dynamics

01:33:15.623 --> 01:33:18.125
to know if that's
actually true or not, but

01:33:18.125 --> 01:33:20.361
in my mind we've been shortchanged here

01:33:20.361 --> 01:33:23.598
13 ounces of actual liquid plus
maybe 3 or 4 ounces of foam.

01:33:25.299 --> 01:33:26.767
That's actually really tasty.

01:33:26.767 --> 01:33:28.703
This is, like, dangerously good.

01:33:28.703 --> 01:33:30.605
I don't want to stop drinking this.

01:33:30.605 --> 01:33:31.939
Got a long shoot ahead of us. Let's go.

01:33:31.939 --> 01:33:32.940
They're already pretty sweet,

01:33:32.940 --> 01:33:35.109
but apparently you can get
these made with chocolate milk,

01:33:35.109 --> 01:33:37.111
so you can get it even sweeter.

01:33:37.111 --> 01:33:38.980
It's their secret-menu item.

01:33:38.980 --> 01:33:42.116
Doughnuts from a UK Tim Hortons
come in three portion sizes:

01:33:42.116 --> 01:33:45.152
as a single doughnut, as a box of six,

01:33:45.152 --> 01:33:47.989
or as a dozen doughnuts.

01:33:47.989 --> 01:33:49.457
These look really good.

01:33:49.457 --> 01:33:51.926
In the US, we also get
Tim Hortons doughnuts

01:33:51.926 --> 01:33:55.162
in serving sizes of one,

01:33:55.162 --> 01:33:58.065
six,

01:33:58.065 --> 01:33:59.200
and 12.

01:33:59.200 --> 01:34:00.801
Are the doughnuts
themselves a different size

01:34:00.801 --> 01:34:01.836
in the US or the UK?

01:34:01.836 --> 01:34:03.771
We're going to weigh a
glazed old-fashioned doughnut

01:34:03.771 --> 01:34:05.373
to find out.

01:34:05.373 --> 01:34:08.175
So close. 68 grams.

01:34:08.175 --> 01:34:09.477
God, grow up, Harry.

01:34:11.012 --> 01:34:12.046
Whoa.

01:34:12.046 --> 01:34:13.814
We're 58 grams.

01:34:13.814 --> 01:34:15.850
So we're missing 10 grams?!

01:34:15.850 --> 01:34:18.586
It's suspicious. Is your flour heavier?

01:34:18.586 --> 01:34:20.554
I feel like you rigged
your scale. I don't know.

01:34:20.554 --> 01:34:23.591
I'm going to put out
some conspiracy theories.

01:34:23.591 --> 01:34:26.894
Tim Hortons' Timbits come
in three sizes in the UK,

01:34:26.894 --> 01:34:28.729
as a box of 10,

01:34:28.729 --> 01:34:30.464
as a box of 20,

01:34:31.332 --> 01:34:33.134
or our largest size,

01:34:34.001 --> 01:34:35.302
[grunts]

01:34:36.804 --> 01:34:38.139
as a box of 50.

01:34:38.139 --> 01:34:41.542
US Timbits come in four portion sizes:

01:34:41.542 --> 01:34:43.010
one,

01:34:43.010 --> 01:34:44.378
10,

01:34:44.378 --> 01:34:45.613
20,

01:34:45.613 --> 01:34:47.348
and 40.

01:34:47.348 --> 01:34:49.350
This one is so funny.

01:34:49.350 --> 01:34:51.819
I don't think there's Munchkins
with sprinkles on them.

01:34:51.819 --> 01:34:54.255
Tim Hortons is kind of gourmet.

01:34:54.255 --> 01:34:55.523
Oh, my God.

01:34:56.457 --> 01:34:57.992
It's so dense.

01:34:57.992 --> 01:34:59.026
This is really good.

01:34:59.026 --> 01:35:01.462
These are not like
Munchkins. I take that back.

01:35:01.462 --> 01:35:03.798
I'm so sorry, Dunkin'
Donuts, I still love you.

01:35:03.798 --> 01:35:06.000
In the Dunkin' Donuts episode,

01:35:06.000 --> 01:35:07.735
I tried to fit as many doughnut holes

01:35:07.735 --> 01:35:10.571
in my mouth at once as I could.

01:35:10.571 --> 01:35:11.972
So you know what this means.

01:35:14.842 --> 01:35:16.410
Well, I think it's stupid that

01:35:16.410 --> 01:35:18.913
he makes us do this every
time. Such a guy thing.

01:35:18.913 --> 01:35:20.715
But yeah, let's beat Harry.

01:35:48.175 --> 01:35:49.043
Irene: Mm-mm.

01:35:57.752 --> 01:36:00.020
I thought I could fit 10 in my mouth.

01:36:00.020 --> 01:36:00.955
They're really dense.

01:36:00.955 --> 01:36:03.257
I think if they weren't as
dense, I could put more.

01:36:03.257 --> 01:36:06.560
[sighs] I don't want to admit Harry won.

01:36:06.560 --> 01:36:07.995
This was rigged!

01:36:09.163 --> 01:36:12.166
I don't know how, but it
was definitely rigged.

01:36:12.166 --> 01:36:13.334
I don't know, man.

01:36:13.334 --> 01:36:15.136
Yeah, OK, Harry, you won.

01:36:16.403 --> 01:36:18.973
Whatever. We still won the
Revolutionary War, huh?

01:36:22.543 --> 01:36:24.411
Here are the Tim Hortons
menu items from the UK

01:36:24.411 --> 01:36:26.247
that you won't find in the US.

01:36:26.247 --> 01:36:28.282
And here's everything at a US Tim Hortons

01:36:28.282 --> 01:36:30.384
you won't find in the UK.

01:36:30.384 --> 01:36:31.919
Harry: We'll start down
this end with the doughnuts.

01:36:31.919 --> 01:36:33.988
This is the Canadian maple doughnut.

01:36:33.988 --> 01:36:35.656
This is the maple caramel doughnut.

01:36:35.656 --> 01:36:37.091
The rainbow doughnut,

01:36:37.091 --> 01:36:38.692
the strawberry and vanilla doughnut,

01:36:38.692 --> 01:36:40.027
a banoffee pie,

01:36:40.027 --> 01:36:41.462
chocolate brownie doughnut,

01:36:41.462 --> 01:36:43.097
a caramel apple fritter,

01:36:43.097 --> 01:36:45.299
and a red velvet cheesecake doughnut.

01:36:45.299 --> 01:36:48.903
These are almost too much
for me, a lot of these ones.

01:36:48.903 --> 01:36:50.304
I like a slightly more simple taste

01:36:50.304 --> 01:36:52.106
when it comes to doughnuts.
I like just a classic jam.

01:36:52.106 --> 01:36:53.274
I think it's the chocolate brownie one

01:36:53.274 --> 01:36:54.842
that's calling my name the most.

01:36:54.842 --> 01:36:56.043
It's not bad.

01:36:56.043 --> 01:36:59.113
The doughnut itself is slightly dry,

01:36:59.113 --> 01:37:01.482
as are the brownie chunks on top.

01:37:01.482 --> 01:37:03.717
So I think the two of those combined

01:37:03.717 --> 01:37:07.421
give a fairly dry doughnut experience.

01:37:07.421 --> 01:37:09.356
Maybe a little more sauce in the middle.

01:37:09.356 --> 01:37:11.559
Or just wash it down with an Iced Capp,

01:37:11.559 --> 01:37:13.093
and then you'll be fine.

01:37:13.093 --> 01:37:15.095
We also have some exclusive doughnuts.

01:37:15.095 --> 01:37:17.298
Not as many, but, you know, we have four.

01:37:17.298 --> 01:37:19.667
This is the honey dip.

01:37:19.667 --> 01:37:21.335
Sour cream glazed.

01:37:21.335 --> 01:37:23.270
This one does look cool.

01:37:23.270 --> 01:37:25.005
Chocolate dip, which,

01:37:25.005 --> 01:37:26.907
this does just look like
a chocolate doughnut,

01:37:26.907 --> 01:37:30.778
so I don't really understand
how this is exclusive.

01:37:30.778 --> 01:37:33.547
And this is the honey,

01:37:33.547 --> 01:37:35.382
honey crueler, cruh-ler.

01:37:35.382 --> 01:37:36.717
I don't know how to pronounce this.

01:37:36.717 --> 01:37:39.453
Actually, we're going to
check that real quick.

01:37:39.453 --> 01:37:42.790
Phone: We are looking at
how to pronounce this word

01:37:42.790 --> 01:37:46.994
as well as how to say more
interesting and related word.

01:37:46.994 --> 01:37:51.765
Crawler. Crawler. Pretty
straightforward once you know.

01:37:51.765 --> 01:37:55.970
Crawler. Not crueler, but rather crawler.

01:37:55.970 --> 01:37:57.872
And now you know.

01:37:57.872 --> 01:37:59.673
I'm probably not saying
it completely right,

01:37:59.673 --> 01:38:01.375
but I think we're going to live with it,

01:38:01.375 --> 01:38:03.344
because I think if we try
to say it completely right,

01:38:03.344 --> 01:38:05.145
it's just going to be worse for all of us.

01:38:05.145 --> 01:38:06.614
The honey cruller.

01:38:09.316 --> 01:38:11.986
Hm. I didn't taste the honey
at first, but it's good.

01:38:11.986 --> 01:38:13.420
I do want to try the sour cream one.

01:38:15.956 --> 01:38:19.226
I don't know if I like the sour cream.

01:38:19.226 --> 01:38:20.794
You taste the sour cream.

01:38:20.794 --> 01:38:23.864
You taste and smell it
right away, I think.

01:38:23.864 --> 01:38:25.466
Take a bite?

01:38:25.466 --> 01:38:27.635
Take a little bite.

01:38:27.635 --> 01:38:30.838
We also have a couple of
exclusive Timbit varieties.

01:38:30.838 --> 01:38:32.806
Sour cream glazed Timbit

01:38:32.806 --> 01:38:35.175
and the sour cream
blueberry glazed Timbit.

01:38:35.175 --> 01:38:37.044
They really like sour cream, huh?

01:38:37.044 --> 01:38:38.512
Or do they think we like sour cream

01:38:38.512 --> 01:38:40.014
so they're adding it to everything?

01:38:40.014 --> 01:38:42.483
It's like when you go
to the "American aisle"

01:38:42.483 --> 01:38:44.852
of a grocery store in another country

01:38:44.852 --> 01:38:48.322
and it's just all, like,
containers of sour cream.

01:38:48.322 --> 01:38:49.657
We also have a load of breakfast options

01:38:49.657 --> 01:38:50.891
that you won't find in the US.

01:38:50.891 --> 01:38:51.725
We'll start with this one.

01:38:51.725 --> 01:38:53.594
It's a veggie sausage and egg muffin.

01:38:53.594 --> 01:38:55.396
I gotta say, this looks pretty good.

01:38:55.396 --> 01:38:57.331
This is a vegetarian sausage patty

01:38:57.331 --> 01:38:59.600
with cheese and egg, as you might imagine.

01:38:59.600 --> 01:39:01.669
This is good! Like, the
texture looks there.

01:39:01.669 --> 01:39:02.503
It's kind of got those, like,

01:39:02.503 --> 01:39:04.004
fibers that you're used to for meat.

01:39:04.004 --> 01:39:05.839
Honestly, that's not bad at all.

01:39:05.839 --> 01:39:09.643
There is a chance that
you could give this to me

01:39:09.643 --> 01:39:11.946
and I would not know that it wasn't meat,

01:39:11.946 --> 01:39:13.080
which, for a meat eater, is pretty much

01:39:13.080 --> 01:39:14.481
the highest praise that I can give that.

01:39:14.481 --> 01:39:16.417
Next up we have an
option called the stack.

01:39:16.417 --> 01:39:18.986
So for both the sausage
and the bacon muffins,

01:39:18.986 --> 01:39:21.055
you have the option to
turn it into a stack.

01:39:21.055 --> 01:39:24.224
What this means is adding a
hash brown into your muffin.

01:39:24.224 --> 01:39:25.626
I don't really understand
where the stack thing

01:39:25.626 --> 01:39:27.328
came from in the UK, because Tim Hortons

01:39:27.328 --> 01:39:28.295
aren't the only ones doing it.

01:39:28.295 --> 01:39:30.397
I think Subway also
have, like, sub stacks,

01:39:30.397 --> 01:39:32.466
where you can just add
hash browns to anything,

01:39:32.466 --> 01:39:33.968
and apparently that makes it a stack.

01:39:33.968 --> 01:39:37.137
In the US, we have avocado-toast options.

01:39:37.137 --> 01:39:38.739
I was going to hold it up like
the "Animal Crossing" style.

01:39:38.739 --> 01:39:39.940
It's kind of flimsy.

01:39:39.940 --> 01:39:41.775
You know when they hold up,
like, the fish and they're like,

01:39:41.775 --> 01:39:43.744
"This is what I caught."

01:39:43.744 --> 01:39:44.945
The bread's just really thin.

01:39:44.945 --> 01:39:46.347
I feel like avocado toast usually comes

01:39:46.347 --> 01:39:49.116
with a really crusty piece
of bread, like really thick.

01:39:49.116 --> 01:39:51.118
Then we're on to breakfast sandwiches,

01:39:51.118 --> 01:39:54.088
both in the form of
English muffins and bagels.

01:39:54.088 --> 01:39:56.323
There's the double stacked
breakfast sandwich,

01:39:56.323 --> 01:39:57.891
which we weren't able to get.

01:39:57.891 --> 01:40:01.595
We have the sausage
bagel breakfast sandwich,

01:40:01.595 --> 01:40:03.731
bacon bagel breakfast sandwich,

01:40:03.731 --> 01:40:06.066
the egg and cheese bagel
breakfast sandwich,

01:40:06.066 --> 01:40:09.603
and the bagel BELT,

01:40:09.603 --> 01:40:12.039
bacon, egg, lettuce, and tomato.

01:40:12.039 --> 01:40:13.040
That's interesting.

01:40:13.040 --> 01:40:14.675
I don't think I've ever
heard of that before.

01:40:14.675 --> 01:40:16.643
It doesn't look like a bad bagel,

01:40:16.643 --> 01:40:18.946
but this isn't the bagel I
would want to go and get.

01:40:18.946 --> 01:40:20.948
It doesn't feel right.

01:40:20.948 --> 01:40:21.915
Katya: Rubbery?

01:40:21.915 --> 01:40:23.617
Yeah, it does feel ...

01:40:23.617 --> 01:40:25.486
I don't know if it feels
rubbery, but it's, like,

01:40:25.486 --> 01:40:28.522
actually, the inside's a little ...

01:40:28.522 --> 01:40:29.356
I don't know about that.

01:40:29.356 --> 01:40:30.457
You know, we're filming this in New York.

01:40:30.457 --> 01:40:32.126
We have high standards for bagels.

01:40:32.126 --> 01:40:34.561
The UK has one breakfast wrap option,

01:40:34.561 --> 01:40:37.965
the big breakfast wrap, which
contains a hash brown, egg,

01:40:37.965 --> 01:40:40.167
bacon, cheese, and sausage.

01:40:40.167 --> 01:40:42.803
That looks like the equivalent of our

01:40:42.803 --> 01:40:44.772
loaded farmers breakfast wrap.

01:40:45.906 --> 01:40:47.307
It's really stuck in here.

01:40:50.177 --> 01:40:51.879
OK, we got it out.

01:40:51.879 --> 01:40:53.180
This is hefty.

01:40:53.180 --> 01:40:56.216
I wonder why they call ours
the loaded farmers breakfast

01:40:56.216 --> 01:40:58.285
but theirs the big breakfast.

01:40:58.285 --> 01:41:01.288
Do they think this is
what American farmers eat?

01:41:01.288 --> 01:41:03.824
And they're like, "Oh,
that's a big breakfast.

01:41:03.824 --> 01:41:05.092
That's what I want today."

01:41:05.092 --> 01:41:07.928
I don't think this is
what would keep me going

01:41:07.928 --> 01:41:10.564
if I needed to go out
on the farm for a day.

01:41:10.564 --> 01:41:13.300
But we can also get the
loaded breakfast wrap

01:41:13.300 --> 01:41:15.969
and then the breakfast wrap snacker.

01:41:15.969 --> 01:41:17.237
This is so little and cute.

01:41:17.237 --> 01:41:20.174
Snack Wrap dupe. Sorry, McDonald's.

01:41:20.174 --> 01:41:21.575
Bring it back!

01:41:24.078 --> 01:41:26.113
You know, snack size.
That's the right size.

01:41:26.113 --> 01:41:28.115
Next up, the UK has bagels on the menu.

01:41:28.115 --> 01:41:31.218
You can get these either as
plain or with cream cheese.

01:41:31.218 --> 01:41:32.586
I think I did ask for cream cheese

01:41:32.586 --> 01:41:33.821
and they might have forgotten it,

01:41:33.821 --> 01:41:35.489
and now I just have a very dry bagel,

01:41:35.489 --> 01:41:37.191
which I will probably not be eating.

01:41:37.191 --> 01:41:38.792
Over here we love our bagels,

01:41:38.792 --> 01:41:42.162
and Tim Hortons reflects that
by providing lots of options.

01:41:42.162 --> 01:41:44.598
We have the everything bagel,

01:41:44.598 --> 01:41:46.400
cinnamon raisin bagel,

01:41:46.400 --> 01:41:48.469
the 12-grain bagel,

01:41:48.469 --> 01:41:50.237
and a pretzel bagel,

01:41:50.237 --> 01:41:51.805
which I don't know if I've seen before.

01:41:51.805 --> 01:41:56.777
It's a cool flavor in theory,
and I appreciate the options.

01:41:56.777 --> 01:41:58.145
I think it's cool that
they're trying to provide

01:41:58.145 --> 01:41:59.613
a good variety for us.

01:41:59.613 --> 01:42:01.615
They have more bagel options
than I thought they would have.

01:42:01.615 --> 01:42:02.583
If bagels aren't for you

01:42:02.583 --> 01:42:04.151
but you want another kind of bread thing,

01:42:04.151 --> 01:42:05.953
we also have toast on the menu at a UK,

01:42:05.953 --> 01:42:07.287
although they wouldn't
actually give it to me today

01:42:07.287 --> 01:42:08.489
because they've run out of the jam

01:42:08.489 --> 01:42:09.523
that it's usually served with.

01:42:09.523 --> 01:42:11.125
So unfortunately I couldn't get it.

01:42:11.125 --> 01:42:12.826
The next one is a classic
British breakfast item,

01:42:12.826 --> 01:42:13.927
the bacon roll.

01:42:13.927 --> 01:42:17.531
As the name suggests, it's
a bread roll with bacon.

01:42:17.531 --> 01:42:18.799
You can get them with a range of sauces.

01:42:18.799 --> 01:42:19.967
This one has ketchup,

01:42:19.967 --> 01:42:21.435
but I think you can also get brown sauce.

01:42:21.435 --> 01:42:23.003
Compared to the standard

01:42:23.003 --> 01:42:25.472
fast-food bacon quality
that I'm used to seeing,

01:42:25.472 --> 01:42:29.676
this is a pretty thick
piece of back British bacon.

01:42:29.676 --> 01:42:31.812
Compared to, like, McDonald's bacon,

01:42:31.812 --> 01:42:33.514
this has way more flavor.

01:42:33.514 --> 01:42:35.716
Actually tastes of pork,
which is always nice.

01:42:35.716 --> 01:42:38.685
We can also get breakfast biscuit options.

01:42:38.685 --> 01:42:41.688
We have the simply sausage biscuit,

01:42:41.688 --> 01:42:44.625
and then we have the simply bacon biscuit.

01:42:44.625 --> 01:42:46.293
I know this is controversial.

01:42:46.293 --> 01:42:48.395
Biscuits and scones aren't
the same thing, I'm sorry.

01:42:48.395 --> 01:42:49.997
The scones are definitely denser.

01:42:49.997 --> 01:42:51.665
I get that they might look similar,

01:42:51.665 --> 01:42:54.268
so maybe putting biscuits
with savory things

01:42:54.268 --> 01:42:57.538
seems weird, but it's not.

01:42:57.538 --> 01:42:59.940
I think you just need to try,
like, a good Southern biscuit.

01:42:59.940 --> 01:43:02.209
I say as a girl from New Jersey,

01:43:02.209 --> 01:43:04.444
because I clearly know
what I'm talking about.

01:43:04.444 --> 01:43:06.446
This isn't a scone.

01:43:06.446 --> 01:43:07.514
They're not similar at all.

01:43:07.514 --> 01:43:09.883
I'm annoying, so I've
gone to afternoon tea,

01:43:09.883 --> 01:43:12.619
here in the US and in London,
so I know the difference.

01:43:12.619 --> 01:43:13.820
It's not the same thing.

01:43:13.820 --> 01:43:16.023
UK Tim Hortons also sells pancakes.

01:43:16.023 --> 01:43:18.091
Now, these are American-style pancakes,

01:43:18.091 --> 01:43:22.229
so they are small, round, and
thicker than British pancakes,

01:43:22.229 --> 01:43:24.164
which tend to be more like crepes.

01:43:24.164 --> 01:43:25.599
They come in portions of two.

01:43:25.599 --> 01:43:28.468
This one comes with some Nutella.

01:43:28.468 --> 01:43:30.604
You can also get maple syrup pancakes,

01:43:30.604 --> 01:43:32.839
which are just the same
but with a little thing

01:43:32.839 --> 01:43:35.809
of maple syrup, or
"maple-flavored golden syrup,"

01:43:35.809 --> 01:43:37.644
because apparently that's
what we have in the UK.

01:43:37.644 --> 01:43:41.014
Or you can get bacon maple
pancakes, which are two pancakes

01:43:41.014 --> 01:43:43.250
with bacon and also the syrup.

01:43:44.451 --> 01:43:45.786
[laughs]

01:43:46.653 --> 01:43:48.922
The bacon pancakes.

01:43:48.922 --> 01:43:50.290
Oh, there is more. OK, there's more.

01:43:50.290 --> 01:43:54.895
I thought that this was
the only bacon that we had

01:43:54.895 --> 01:43:57.397
on our maple bacon
pancakes, but thankfully

01:43:57.397 --> 01:44:01.034
they've actually layered it
with some more underneath.

01:44:01.034 --> 01:44:02.703
The bacon that you're
getting on the pancakes

01:44:02.703 --> 01:44:05.305
isn't the same bacon as you're
getting in your bacon roll.

01:44:05.305 --> 01:44:07.040
This is, like, streaky bacon.

01:44:07.040 --> 01:44:08.442
That's what we call it in the UK.

01:44:08.442 --> 01:44:11.411
Whereas this is what we
would call back bacon,

01:44:11.411 --> 01:44:13.413
which has the kind of medallion

01:44:13.413 --> 01:44:15.282
and then the little fatty bit on the end.

01:44:15.282 --> 01:44:17.718
I'm not sure why they haven't just used

01:44:17.718 --> 01:44:20.053
one uniform type of
bacon for the whole menu.

01:44:20.053 --> 01:44:21.922
To British people, bacon and pancakes is

01:44:21.922 --> 01:44:23.991
kind of a weird combination as it is,

01:44:23.991 --> 01:44:26.727
so I don't think it would've
been made significantly weirder

01:44:26.727 --> 01:44:28.929
by putting British bacon on these.

01:44:28.929 --> 01:44:31.231
We go to the store and get
Canadian bacon, which is ham,

01:44:31.231 --> 01:44:33.000
which is I guess this British bacon,

01:44:33.000 --> 01:44:35.836
which is, like, what do
they call it? Back bacon?

01:44:35.836 --> 01:44:37.371
This is getting overly complicated.

01:44:37.371 --> 01:44:39.706
There's bacon, and then there's ham.

01:44:39.706 --> 01:44:40.807
That is ham.

01:44:40.807 --> 01:44:44.044
Our last breakfast items
are these omelet bites,

01:44:44.044 --> 01:44:47.180
which come in spinach and egg whites

01:44:47.180 --> 01:44:49.182
and bacon and cheese.

01:44:49.182 --> 01:44:52.152
These are basically like
Starbucks' egg bites,

01:44:52.152 --> 01:44:54.254
which are good. I love them. But.

01:44:54.254 --> 01:44:55.622
Yeah, I feel like the spinach chunks

01:44:55.622 --> 01:44:56.990
are kind of big. I don't know.

01:44:56.990 --> 01:44:59.960
And then we have the croissant, which,

01:44:59.960 --> 01:45:02.195
I don't know if they all look like this,

01:45:02.195 --> 01:45:03.664
but it's kind of making me uncomfortable

01:45:03.664 --> 01:45:05.465
that the ends are touching.

01:45:05.465 --> 01:45:07.000
I feel like they shouldn't do that.

01:45:07.000 --> 01:45:08.068
I don't know. It's like when you walk in

01:45:08.068 --> 01:45:09.836
on your toothbrushes touching.

01:45:09.836 --> 01:45:10.671
Then we have some

01:45:10.671 --> 01:45:13.940
sort of breakfast, sort
of snack exclusives.

01:45:13.940 --> 01:45:16.043
The chocolate chip muffin.

01:45:16.043 --> 01:45:18.412
The fruit explosion muffin.

01:45:18.412 --> 01:45:20.681
What fruits are going to be exploding?

01:45:20.681 --> 01:45:24.051
It'd be cool if it was
like a Gusher situation.

01:45:24.051 --> 01:45:25.319
If you're going to put
"explosion" in the name,

01:45:25.319 --> 01:45:26.553
I feel like it should be doing something.

01:45:26.553 --> 01:45:29.056
And the wild blueberry muffin.

01:45:29.056 --> 01:45:31.825
We also get two cookies
you can't get in the UK,

01:45:31.825 --> 01:45:35.295
chocolate chunk cookie
and oatmeal raisin cookie,

01:45:35.295 --> 01:45:36.363
which, I still don't know

01:45:36.363 --> 01:45:38.799
who would willingly eat
a oatmeal raisin cookie.

01:45:38.799 --> 01:45:40.334
Do you eat oatmeal raisin?!

01:45:42.002 --> 01:45:42.969
Both of you?!

01:45:45.472 --> 01:45:46.740
Well, yeah, that's, like,

01:45:46.740 --> 01:45:49.776
no one actually likes
oatmeal raisin cookies.

01:45:49.776 --> 01:45:52.346
When someone brings in
oatmeal raisin cookies,

01:45:52.346 --> 01:45:53.447
you're hoping it's chocolate chip,

01:45:53.447 --> 01:45:54.981
and then when you find
out it's oatmeal raisin,

01:45:54.981 --> 01:45:55.949
you're like, what the f---?

01:45:55.949 --> 01:45:58.385
I don't get why you would
want raisins in a cookie.

01:45:58.385 --> 01:45:59.519
I'm sorry, Katya.

01:46:02.222 --> 01:46:03.890
Now, later in the day
you can get lunch options

01:46:03.890 --> 01:46:04.925
from a UK Tim Hortons.

01:46:04.925 --> 01:46:06.626
Unfortunately, we went
there slightly too early

01:46:06.626 --> 01:46:08.795
to actually get these,
but if you arrive later,

01:46:08.795 --> 01:46:10.063
here are the exclusive options.

01:46:10.063 --> 01:46:12.899
Tims crispy chicken stack,
with or without bacon,

01:46:12.899 --> 01:46:14.501
Tims crispy chicken sandwich,

01:46:14.501 --> 01:46:16.770
crispy meatless chicken sandwich,

01:46:16.770 --> 01:46:19.039
grilled chicken wrap or
a crispy chicken wrap,

01:46:19.039 --> 01:46:21.074
a tuna wrap, or a vegan wrap.

01:46:21.074 --> 01:46:24.111
Chicken tenders, chicken
and mozzarella panini,

01:46:24.111 --> 01:46:26.380
tuna and cheese melt, ham and cheese melt,

01:46:26.380 --> 01:46:29.383
tomato and basil soup, or potato wedges.

01:46:29.383 --> 01:46:32.285
The lunch options
exclusive to the US include

01:46:32.285 --> 01:46:35.522
a tuna salad sandwich,
chicken salad sandwich,

01:46:35.522 --> 01:46:38.625
turkey bacon club, ham and Swiss sandwich,

01:46:38.625 --> 01:46:41.228
BLT, chipotle steak wrap,

01:46:41.228 --> 01:46:44.798
chipotle chicken bacon
wrap, chipotle chicken wrap,

01:46:44.798 --> 01:46:47.033
and chili, because, you know,

01:46:47.033 --> 01:46:49.703
that's what we really want, I guess.

01:46:49.703 --> 01:46:51.972
I do like chili, but that's interesting.

01:46:51.972 --> 01:46:53.573
Now let's look at some
drinks you can only find

01:46:53.573 --> 01:46:54.875
at a UK Tim Hortons.

01:46:54.875 --> 01:46:56.443
'Cause I've only looked at the US menu,

01:46:56.443 --> 01:46:58.078
so I'm going to say "only find in the UK."

01:46:58.078 --> 01:47:00.213
I bet some of these will
be available in Canada

01:47:00.213 --> 01:47:02.682
and there's going to be angry
Canadians in the comments.

01:47:02.682 --> 01:47:04.251
How angry can Canadians really get?

01:47:04.251 --> 01:47:06.086
I feel like they're
pretty polite in general.

01:47:06.086 --> 01:47:07.587
Let's start with some cold beverages.

01:47:07.587 --> 01:47:10.190
Over here we have an Iced Capp supreme.

01:47:10.190 --> 01:47:12.325
So, a supreme basically means
that they've added some extra

01:47:12.325 --> 01:47:15.061
whipped cream and then some
topping pieces to an Iced Capp.

01:47:15.061 --> 01:47:16.963
You can get these in a couple
of flavor and topping options.

01:47:16.963 --> 01:47:18.665
There was one that was
coconut, for example.

01:47:18.665 --> 01:47:19.766
This one is Oreo.

01:47:19.766 --> 01:47:21.234
So you get the extra whipped cream

01:47:21.234 --> 01:47:23.103
with some little crushed Oreo pieces.

01:47:23.103 --> 01:47:25.705
The standard Iced Capp
was already really sweet,

01:47:25.705 --> 01:47:29.042
so I'm not sure it needs
Oreo, but, eh, you do you.

01:47:29.042 --> 01:47:31.511
We can also get milkshakes
at a Tim Hortons in the UK.

01:47:31.511 --> 01:47:33.346
These come in a range of
options, including vanilla,

01:47:33.346 --> 01:47:35.115
strawberry, chocolate, maple,

01:47:35.115 --> 01:47:37.284
or a dairy-free mango and coconut.

01:47:39.719 --> 01:47:41.955
[coughing]

01:47:43.657 --> 01:47:44.658
That went down the wrong hole.

01:47:44.658 --> 01:47:47.694
That wasn't the shake's fault.

01:47:49.396 --> 01:47:50.664
It's, like, banana-y, you know?

01:47:50.664 --> 01:47:52.265
Oh, it's banoffee.

01:47:52.265 --> 01:47:54.100
Took me a minute, but, hey.

01:47:54.100 --> 01:47:55.569
Banoffee shake as well.

01:47:55.569 --> 01:47:57.404
Then we have some hot
drink options as well.

01:47:57.404 --> 01:47:59.673
Here we have a caramel macchiato.

01:47:59.673 --> 01:48:01.575
You can, of course, get
an English breakfast tea.

01:48:01.575 --> 01:48:03.410
We're in the UK. You
can't really open a place

01:48:03.410 --> 01:48:05.412
and not put this on the menu.

01:48:05.412 --> 01:48:07.747
We're continuing the
banoffee-menu-item theme

01:48:07.747 --> 01:48:10.617
with a banoffee latte,
which I'm less convinced by.

01:48:12.185 --> 01:48:14.087
Yeah, banana coffee

01:48:14.087 --> 01:48:16.923
isn't really one that I have tried before.

01:48:17.757 --> 01:48:19.092
I guess technically

01:48:19.092 --> 01:48:21.328
you could have "banoffee"
to mean "banana coffee,"

01:48:21.328 --> 01:48:23.997
but I think if you've got
banana and toffee right there,

01:48:23.997 --> 01:48:25.365
just stick with the classic.

01:48:25.365 --> 01:48:27.267
We can also get a flat white in the UK.

01:48:27.267 --> 01:48:28.869
We can also get a chai latte

01:48:28.869 --> 01:48:30.837
and a red velvet hot chocolate.

01:48:30.837 --> 01:48:33.373
Sandwich van with "Match
of the Day" music.

01:48:33.373 --> 01:48:36.676
[distant music]
Ba ba ba ba, ba da ba ba ba.

01:48:42.849 --> 01:48:45.452
Here are our US-exclusive cold drinks.

01:48:45.452 --> 01:48:47.754
Cinnamon sugar oat milk cold brew,

01:48:47.754 --> 01:48:49.456
vanilla-flavored cream cold brew

01:48:49.456 --> 01:48:51.291
with chocolate cold foam,

01:48:51.291 --> 01:48:53.994
caramel cream cold brew with cold foam,

01:48:53.994 --> 01:48:56.196
mocha cream cold brew with cold foam,

01:48:56.196 --> 01:48:59.165
Sunrise Sunset TimsBoost with Red Bull,

01:48:59.165 --> 01:49:02.235
Sky's the Limit TimsBoost with Red Bull,

01:49:02.235 --> 01:49:04.204
orange tangerine refresher,

01:49:04.204 --> 01:49:06.673
fruit smoothie (mixed berry),

01:49:06.673 --> 01:49:08.308
and frozen lemonade.

01:49:08.308 --> 01:49:11.011
Here are the US-exclusive hot drinks.

01:49:11.011 --> 01:49:13.914
The Take 12, which,
coffee's not exclusive,

01:49:13.914 --> 01:49:17.450
but you can only get this
giant size in the US,

01:49:17.450 --> 01:49:20.153
French vanilla, and steeped tea.

01:49:20.153 --> 01:49:23.189
And that's interesting that
the UK doesn't get steeped tea,

01:49:23.189 --> 01:49:25.125
'cause, you know, UK.

01:49:25.125 --> 01:49:27.160
Apparently this is
really popular in Canada,

01:49:27.160 --> 01:49:30.497
and it's just tea that's
made by, instead of brewing,

01:49:30.497 --> 01:49:33.700
you leave the leaves in
either cold or hot water,

01:49:33.700 --> 01:49:35.502
and eventually the flavor comes through.

01:49:35.502 --> 01:49:37.938
But my friend said that this
is really, really popular,

01:49:37.938 --> 01:49:39.472
and they have different flavors, so.

01:49:39.472 --> 01:49:41.575
I'm going to make a double double.

01:49:41.575 --> 01:49:45.946
This is apparently a big thing
in Canada for Tim Hortons,

01:49:45.946 --> 01:49:49.382
and it's literally just coffee
with two creams, two sugars.

01:49:49.382 --> 01:49:51.851
But it's, like, a thing.

01:49:51.851 --> 01:49:54.588
Unless I'm being set up by my friend.

01:49:54.588 --> 01:49:56.623
April, don't do this to me.

01:49:58.291 --> 01:49:59.793
I'm not strong enough.

01:50:02.495 --> 01:50:04.197
Is half and half the same thing as cream?

01:50:04.197 --> 01:50:05.165
I think they are, right?

01:50:05.165 --> 01:50:08.134
I used to drink half and
half when I was a kid.

01:50:08.134 --> 01:50:09.336
I feel like some people
think that's gross,

01:50:09.336 --> 01:50:10.570
but it tastes really good.

01:50:10.570 --> 01:50:11.771
When I was little, we would go to Denny's,

01:50:11.771 --> 01:50:13.406
and it's on the table,
and you're just like ...

01:50:16.443 --> 01:50:17.277
It tastes good.

01:50:17.277 --> 01:50:19.079
Two sugars.

01:50:19.079 --> 01:50:20.246
The few times I do drink coffee,

01:50:20.246 --> 01:50:22.382
I usually put six to
eight packets, if that,

01:50:22.382 --> 01:50:24.618
but I line them up at once and rip them

01:50:24.618 --> 01:50:26.186
so no one can tell how
much sugar I'm putting in,

01:50:26.186 --> 01:50:27.487
so they can't judge me.

01:50:31.124 --> 01:50:33.460
Maybe it tastes better
when they make it for you.

01:50:33.460 --> 01:50:35.362
It just tastes like coffee,

01:50:35.362 --> 01:50:38.465
and I don't like coffee that
much, so maybe that's why.

01:50:38.465 --> 01:50:40.133
Can I have my diet Coke now?

01:50:43.570 --> 01:50:46.940
A large Iced Capp from a
UK Tim Hortons costs £4.39,

01:50:46.940 --> 01:50:48.942
which is $5.30.

01:50:48.942 --> 01:50:52.512
In the US, a large Iced Capp is $4.89,

01:50:52.512 --> 01:50:54.981
or £4.01.

01:50:54.981 --> 01:50:58.451
That makes a US large
Iced Capp 7.7% cheaper

01:50:58.451 --> 01:51:00.286
in the US than the UK.

01:51:00.286 --> 01:51:02.822
Six doughnuts at a UK
Tim Hortons cost £8.99,

01:51:02.822 --> 01:51:04.357
which is $10.85.

01:51:04.357 --> 01:51:07.961
In the US, six doughnuts cost $8.99,

01:51:07.961 --> 01:51:10.864
or £7.38.

01:51:10.864 --> 01:51:14.234
20 Timbits from a UK
Tim Hortons cost £7.49,

01:51:14.234 --> 01:51:16.436
which is around $9.04.

01:51:16.436 --> 01:51:20.040
In the US, 20 Timbits cost $6.29,

01:51:20.040 --> 01:51:21.875
or £5.16.

01:51:21.875 --> 01:51:23.777
Overall, it honestly seems
like pretty good value

01:51:23.777 --> 01:51:25.512
compared to some of the
other fast-food chains

01:51:25.512 --> 01:51:26.813
that are comparable, I suppose.

01:51:26.813 --> 01:51:29.049
I feel like the breakfast deal
particularly was quite good.

01:51:29.049 --> 01:51:31.685
They had a £3.49-ish deal

01:51:31.685 --> 01:51:34.154
for a breakfast meal including the muffin,

01:51:34.154 --> 01:51:36.423
a hash brown, and a drink,
which is really good.

01:51:36.423 --> 01:51:38.358
Probably even better value
than McDonald's, for example.

01:51:38.358 --> 01:51:39.192
I really love doughnuts.

01:51:39.192 --> 01:51:41.494
I kind of wish doughnuts were
more commonplace in the UK,

01:51:41.494 --> 01:51:42.829
because they're not that big a thing.

01:51:42.829 --> 01:51:45.065
I feel like from what I've
seen from Tim Hortons today,

01:51:45.065 --> 01:51:45.899
they've got what it takes.

01:51:45.899 --> 01:51:48.068
They should be pushing really
hard into the UK market.

01:51:48.068 --> 01:51:49.469
I do think there's demand for this.

01:51:52.005 --> 01:51:53.773
A large Iced Capp from a UK Tim Hortons

01:51:53.773 --> 01:51:56.543
contains the following: 399 calories,

01:51:56.543 --> 01:51:58.011
23 grams of total fat,

01:51:58.011 --> 01:52:00.013
of which 15 grams are saturated,

01:52:00.013 --> 01:52:01.448
and 44 grams of carbs,

01:52:01.448 --> 01:52:03.516
of which 42 grams are sugars.

01:52:03.516 --> 01:52:05.318
That's 20% of your daily calories,

01:52:05.318 --> 01:52:07.554
75% of your daily saturates,

01:52:07.554 --> 01:52:09.723
and 84% of your daily sugar,

01:52:09.723 --> 01:52:12.459
which is alarming,
because it's really good.

01:52:13.927 --> 01:52:16.863
A large Iced Capp in the
US contains the following:

01:52:16.863 --> 01:52:18.665
393 calories,

01:52:18.665 --> 01:52:21.134
23.4 grams total fat,

01:52:21.134 --> 01:52:23.670
12.5 grams of saturated fat,

01:52:23.670 --> 01:52:26.106
42.7 grams of carbs,

01:52:26.106 --> 01:52:28.742
38.2 of which are sugars.

01:52:28.742 --> 01:52:30.944
That means that apart
from total fat content,

01:52:30.944 --> 01:52:33.546
the US Iced Capp is actually
healthier than the UK's

01:52:33.546 --> 01:52:35.215
in every other metric.

01:52:39.285 --> 01:52:42.756
Although it's still 62.5%
of your daily saturated fat

01:52:42.756 --> 01:52:46.693
and 76.4% of your daily sugar. So.

01:52:46.693 --> 01:52:48.495
You win some, you lose some.

01:52:48.495 --> 01:52:51.030
Milk.fandom.com.

01:52:51.865 --> 01:52:55.001
If you're a huge fan of
milk, that's the place to go.

01:52:55.001 --> 01:52:57.303
Oh, here you go. Here's a
table. Thank you, ah, milk.

01:52:57.303 --> 01:52:59.572
The milk Wiki is educational.

01:52:59.572 --> 01:53:01.474
This is a good opportunity
to explain the differences

01:53:01.474 --> 01:53:03.176
between the standard dairy products used

01:53:03.176 --> 01:53:05.111
in beverages in the US and the UK.

01:53:05.111 --> 01:53:07.447
To me, this is an alarming
amount of saturated fat

01:53:07.447 --> 01:53:09.482
because usually when you're
making a beverage like this

01:53:09.482 --> 01:53:11.718
in the UK, you'll be using
either semi-skimmed milk

01:53:11.718 --> 01:53:12.986
or maybe whole milk.

01:53:12.986 --> 01:53:14.788
In the UK, semi-skimmed milk contains

01:53:14.788 --> 01:53:17.056
somewhere between 1% to 2% fat content.

01:53:17.056 --> 01:53:17.891
And then we have whole milk,

01:53:17.891 --> 01:53:20.860
which contains closer to 3.5% to 4% fat.

01:53:20.860 --> 01:53:22.829
These are pretty comparable
to the American equivalent.

01:53:22.829 --> 01:53:24.097
So you guys have semi-skimmed milk,

01:53:24.097 --> 01:53:26.866
but that's, I think, 1.5% to 1.8% fat.

01:53:26.866 --> 01:53:30.003
And then you have whole
milk, which is around 3.25%.

01:53:30.003 --> 01:53:32.038
What's interesting about
Tim Hortons in the UK

01:53:32.038 --> 01:53:33.973
is that they've adopted a
slightly more American approach

01:53:33.973 --> 01:53:34.874
to their beverages.

01:53:34.874 --> 01:53:36.276
So what they've done is actually made this

01:53:36.276 --> 01:53:38.444
with single cream instead of with milk.

01:53:38.444 --> 01:53:41.614
The fat content of single
cream in the UK is around 18%,

01:53:41.614 --> 01:53:44.651
which I think is around what
half and half is in the US.

01:53:44.651 --> 01:53:46.419
But here that is very much the exception

01:53:46.419 --> 01:53:48.154
rather than the norm. This is very rare.

01:53:48.154 --> 01:53:49.656
You will not see this in many places.

01:53:49.656 --> 01:53:51.825
If you're making your beverages
with coffee cream in the US,

01:53:51.825 --> 01:53:54.928
that can even range from
18% to 30% fat content.

01:53:54.928 --> 01:53:57.864
That's crazy. Honestly, it's tasty,

01:53:57.864 --> 01:53:59.332
but I would not want to
drink these every day,

01:53:59.332 --> 01:54:01.100
because that is not good for you.

01:54:01.100 --> 01:54:02.569
The most calorific Timbit in the UK

01:54:02.569 --> 01:54:04.304
is the white chocolate
birthday cake Timbit,

01:54:04.304 --> 01:54:06.940
coming in at 94 calories per bit.

01:54:06.940 --> 01:54:09.776
One of these also contains
8.5 grams of sugar,

01:54:09.776 --> 01:54:12.011
which means that just one of
those and a large Iced Capp

01:54:12.011 --> 01:54:14.247
contains your entire
daily sugar allowance.

01:54:14.247 --> 01:54:16.749
Also means that I was able
to fit almost 1,000 calories

01:54:16.749 --> 01:54:18.418
in my mouth at once. Who knew?

01:54:18.551 --> 01:54:20.119
Harry: From calorie
count to portion sizes,

01:54:20.119 --> 01:54:22.255
we wanted to find out all the
differences between Denny's

01:54:22.255 --> 01:54:23.890
in the US and the UK.

01:54:23.890 --> 01:54:25.725
This is "Food Wars."

01:54:27.861 --> 01:54:30.697
This is an All-American Slam
breakfast at a UK Denny's.

01:54:30.697 --> 01:54:32.999
It consists of two
scrambled eggs with cheddar,

01:54:32.999 --> 01:54:34.868
two sausages, two pieces of bacon,

01:54:34.868 --> 01:54:38.338
some American-style hash brown,
and two triangles of toast.

01:54:38.338 --> 01:54:39.839
This bacon looks a little sad.

01:54:39.839 --> 01:54:42.275
I know you guys like
crispy bacon in the US.

01:54:42.275 --> 01:54:44.077
An All-American Slam breakfast in the US

01:54:44.077 --> 01:54:45.845
comes with the following by default.

01:54:45.845 --> 01:54:48.514
Three scrambled eggs with
cheese, two bacon strips,

01:54:48.514 --> 01:54:50.817
two sausage links, hash
browns, and a choice

01:54:50.817 --> 01:54:54.220
of either four triangles
of toast or two pancakes.

01:54:54.220 --> 01:54:55.655
We went with pancakes.

01:54:55.655 --> 01:54:57.423
The largest breakfast in the UK is this,

01:54:57.423 --> 01:54:58.825
the Grand Slam Slugger.

01:54:58.825 --> 01:55:00.627
It's the same as the All-American Slam,

01:55:00.627 --> 01:55:02.829
but instead of the toast,
you get two pancakes.

01:55:02.829 --> 01:55:04.130
Now, when I saw this on the menu,

01:55:04.130 --> 01:55:05.832
I didn't think changing
the toast for pancakes

01:55:05.832 --> 01:55:07.367
would actually add that much size to it,

01:55:07.367 --> 01:55:09.202
but these things are huge.

01:55:09.202 --> 01:55:11.938
I think two of these plus the rest,

01:55:11.938 --> 01:55:14.007
and that is a substantial breakfast.

01:55:14.007 --> 01:55:16.542
Our largest slam is the Lumberjack Slam.

01:55:16.542 --> 01:55:19.012
It comes with two pancakes,

01:55:19.012 --> 01:55:21.080
two or three eggs, I can't tell,

01:55:21.080 --> 01:55:23.650
grilled ham, you have a
choice of two sausages links

01:55:23.650 --> 01:55:25.818
and two bacon strips or four of either,

01:55:25.818 --> 01:55:27.420
so I went with four bacon strips,

01:55:27.420 --> 01:55:31.257
hash browns, and four triangles of toast.

01:55:31.257 --> 01:55:32.091
Look at this.

01:55:32.091 --> 01:55:33.860
Now here is a guy who's ready

01:55:33.860 --> 01:55:37.797
for a full day of lumberjacking.

01:55:37.797 --> 01:55:39.933
You can get some of Denny's
iconic sandwiches in the UK,

01:55:39.933 --> 01:55:42.735
including the Grand Slamwich.

01:55:42.735 --> 01:55:43.803
We're going to weigh a Grand Slamwich

01:55:43.803 --> 01:55:45.638
in both countries to see whose is bigger.

01:55:50.376 --> 01:55:53.479
Now, we all know the Moons
Over My Hammy in plate version.

01:55:53.479 --> 01:55:54.314
I didn't know this,

01:55:54.314 --> 01:55:55.815
but apparently now it's
in sandwich version.

01:55:55.815 --> 01:55:56.649
Here it is.

01:55:56.649 --> 01:55:59.719
You got the eggs, you got the ham, right?

01:55:59.719 --> 01:56:02.355
This is a UK Moons Over My Hammy.

01:56:02.355 --> 01:56:03.890
I don't get that pun.
I'm really sorry, guys.

01:56:07.827 --> 01:56:08.761
No diner would be complete

01:56:08.761 --> 01:56:11.564
without American-style
pancakes in the United States.

01:56:11.564 --> 01:56:15.368
An order of pancakes comes
by default as a two-piece.

01:56:15.368 --> 01:56:18.471
One, two. One, two.

01:56:18.471 --> 01:56:22.175
An order of pancakes in the
UK also means two pancakes.

01:56:22.175 --> 01:56:23.810
However, when I went to
order them on the website,

01:56:23.810 --> 01:56:25.311
it also gave me the option to add

01:56:25.311 --> 01:56:28.081
a single additional
extra pancake for £1.99,

01:56:28.081 --> 01:56:30.416
and it let me do that up to 99 times.

01:56:30.416 --> 01:56:32.285
So if you do really, really love pancakes,

01:56:32.285 --> 01:56:34.921
you can order 101
pancakes from a UK Denny's

01:56:34.921 --> 01:56:38.424
for a small, small price of £203.80.

01:56:38.424 --> 01:56:40.093
But how big are the pancakes themselves?

01:56:40.093 --> 01:56:41.694
We're going to measure them to find out.

01:56:41.694 --> 01:56:45.965
So, our pancake, I'm going
to say 16 centimeters across.

01:56:45.965 --> 01:56:50.103
And our pancake weighs around 147 grams.

01:56:50.103 --> 01:56:51.004
6 inches?

01:56:51.938 --> 01:56:54.774
I once caught a pancake this big.

01:56:54.774 --> 01:56:56.943
Yeah, again, the Tinder profile, like.

01:56:57.944 --> 01:57:00.213
The weight of the same pancake.

01:57:00.213 --> 01:57:04.384
This specific 6-inch pancake

01:57:04.384 --> 01:57:06.786
at Denny's weighs

01:57:06.786 --> 01:57:09.055
148 grams.

01:57:11.891 --> 01:57:13.926
Here are all the items
you'll find at a UK Denny's

01:57:13.926 --> 01:57:15.661
that you won't find in the US.

01:57:15.661 --> 01:57:17.030
And here's everything you'll find

01:57:17.030 --> 01:57:19.699
at a US Denny's you
will not find in the UK.

01:57:19.699 --> 01:57:21.200
Let's start with the breakfast items.

01:57:21.200 --> 01:57:23.102
Our largest slam breakfast,

01:57:23.102 --> 01:57:26.439
the Grand Slam Slugger,
is in fact an exclusive.

01:57:26.439 --> 01:57:29.275
We have a couple exclusive
slam breakfasts in the US.

01:57:29.275 --> 01:57:31.677
The before-mentioned Lumberjack.

01:57:31.677 --> 01:57:35.214
I mean, I'm curious about
this fried ham steak.

01:57:35.214 --> 01:57:38.484
If you want to eat something at Denny's

01:57:38.484 --> 01:57:40.620
that doesn't go straight
for your arteries,

01:57:40.620 --> 01:57:42.288
you can get the Fit Slam.

01:57:42.288 --> 01:57:44.424
It is two English muffins,

01:57:44.424 --> 01:57:49.228
I see spinach, egg whites, tomatoes,

01:57:49.228 --> 01:57:50.797
looks like feta cheese. Let's get in here.

01:57:50.797 --> 01:57:52.098
I bet that's great when it's hot,

01:57:52.098 --> 01:57:54.200
but it is not hot and
therefore it is not great.

01:57:54.200 --> 01:57:56.202
Next up we have the veggie breakfast.

01:57:56.202 --> 01:57:59.038
In here, we have what
seems to be an omelet

01:57:59.038 --> 01:58:02.041
made with peppers, some spinach,

01:58:02.041 --> 01:58:03.409
and maybe some onion as well.

01:58:03.409 --> 01:58:07.180
There are these little
cubes, almost cubes,

01:58:07.180 --> 01:58:09.649
little square things of potato.

01:58:09.649 --> 01:58:11.017
And then just a couple of bits of

01:58:11.017 --> 01:58:13.119
either boiled or steamed broccoli.

01:58:13.119 --> 01:58:15.955
And if you're not eating
eggs, we have a vegan version.

01:58:15.955 --> 01:58:17.356
It looks like all they've really done is

01:58:17.356 --> 01:58:19.592
just replace the eggs with more potato.

01:58:19.592 --> 01:58:22.995
Benny, which is of course
short for eggs Benedict.

01:58:22.995 --> 01:58:25.098
Everything needs a fun name in America.

01:58:25.098 --> 01:58:29.268
With a poached egg,
ham, hollandaise sauce,

01:58:29.268 --> 01:58:31.170
not to be confused with holiday sauce.

01:58:34.107 --> 01:58:35.108
That's pretty good.

01:58:35.108 --> 01:58:36.909
Of course, we also have a Southwest Benny.

01:58:36.909 --> 01:58:37.910
Southwest?

01:58:37.910 --> 01:58:39.846
Oh, wait, no, this is, like,

01:58:39.846 --> 01:58:41.647
it has, like, chorizo and stuff.

01:58:41.647 --> 01:58:42.615
That actually kind of rules.

01:58:42.615 --> 01:58:44.117
I'm surprised. That's
actually pretty good.

01:58:44.117 --> 01:58:47.854
Something that may mystify the UK viewers,

01:58:47.854 --> 01:58:50.389
as you will see various
versions throughout this video

01:58:50.389 --> 01:58:52.992
of what I'm about to show
you, biscuits and gravy,

01:58:52.992 --> 01:58:54.794
chicken biscuits and gravy.

01:58:54.794 --> 01:58:57.330
It's going to be some sort of combination

01:58:57.330 --> 01:59:00.399
of fried chicken, or some cases steak,

01:59:00.399 --> 01:59:02.702
smothered in the white gravy we have,

01:59:02.702 --> 01:59:04.837
a gravy that is filled with sausage

01:59:04.837 --> 01:59:07.340
and also on our biscuits.

01:59:07.340 --> 01:59:10.877
Deep-fried chicken covered
in our white sauce.

01:59:10.877 --> 01:59:13.279
It's a gravy that's sausage-flavored.

01:59:13.279 --> 01:59:14.947
Cheese. Not a scone.

01:59:16.716 --> 01:59:17.783
Damn it, it's really good.

01:59:17.783 --> 01:59:19.185
Next to that is a Santa Fe bowl.

01:59:19.185 --> 01:59:21.988
Again, does Santa Fe just
mean, like, salsa and chorizo?

01:59:21.988 --> 01:59:25.191
Get these type of potatoes,
these sliced-up seasoned ones.

01:59:25.191 --> 01:59:27.326
Also mushrooms and veggies.

01:59:27.326 --> 01:59:28.628
Another fried gravy thing.

01:59:28.628 --> 01:59:30.963
This is a country-fried steak.

01:59:30.963 --> 01:59:34.033
Yes, a steak that has been fried

01:59:34.033 --> 01:59:38.137
and put our white gravy on it!

01:59:38.137 --> 01:59:41.040
And it also comes with eggs.

01:59:41.040 --> 01:59:42.241
Kind of like a big McNugget

01:59:42.241 --> 01:59:44.177
that's kind of more beef-flavored.

01:59:44.177 --> 01:59:48.447
And speaking of steaks, you can
get a T-bone steak and eggs.

01:59:48.447 --> 01:59:52.351
Denny's, what's with the
onions and mushrooms, guys?

01:59:52.351 --> 01:59:53.586
I want a steak. Like ...

01:59:53.586 --> 01:59:57.590
I assure you there is a
steak underneath this.

01:59:57.590 --> 02:00:00.793
Yeah, there it is. There it is. T-bone.

02:00:00.793 --> 02:00:02.295
Doorstop of a steak.

02:00:02.295 --> 02:00:04.096
Look at the size of this thing.

02:00:04.096 --> 02:00:05.064
I mean, this is ...

02:00:10.002 --> 02:00:12.038
Man, they destroyed this piece of meat.

02:00:12.038 --> 02:00:13.539
This thing is, like,

02:00:13.539 --> 02:00:15.241
the most well-done thing
I've ever bit into.

02:00:15.241 --> 02:00:17.476
It's like biting into a wallet.

02:00:17.476 --> 02:00:19.645
Skip the steak at Denny's.

02:00:19.645 --> 02:00:21.347
We have a few omelet options in the UK,

02:00:21.347 --> 02:00:23.149
but only one of them is exclusive.

02:00:23.149 --> 02:00:25.251
It's the ham and cheese omelet.

02:00:25.251 --> 02:00:26.886
I'm surprised you guys
don't have these in America

02:00:26.886 --> 02:00:28.421
because I'd say ham and cheese is probably

02:00:28.421 --> 02:00:30.890
the most commonly eaten omelet in the UK.

02:00:30.890 --> 02:00:33.559
So, we have exclusive omelets of our own,

02:00:33.559 --> 02:00:35.361
and they are way more elaborate

02:00:35.361 --> 02:00:38.130
than the UK's simple ham and cheese.

02:00:38.130 --> 02:00:41.400
Here we have the Mile High Denver omelet,

02:00:41.400 --> 02:00:45.705
the Ultimate omelet, and the
Philly cheesesteak omelet.

02:00:45.705 --> 02:00:47.440
Now, you watching right now are thinking,

02:00:47.440 --> 02:00:49.475
"Hey, Joe, which is which?"

02:00:49.475 --> 02:00:50.610
I have no idea.

02:00:50.610 --> 02:00:52.445
So another game we're going to play

02:00:52.445 --> 02:00:55.848
in this episode is Omelet Roulette.

02:00:55.848 --> 02:00:57.717
♪ What's in the omelet? ♪

02:00:57.717 --> 02:00:59.418
♪ What's in the omelet? ♪

02:00:59.418 --> 02:01:00.620
So I'm going to take a bite of each one

02:01:00.620 --> 02:01:03.289
and see if I can guess which omelet it is.

02:01:03.289 --> 02:01:04.123
All right.

02:01:06.626 --> 02:01:08.094
Denver.

02:01:08.094 --> 02:01:11.030
Ham, peppers, onions, cheese.

02:01:11.030 --> 02:01:12.198
The next omelet.

02:01:13.099 --> 02:01:15.901
I'm seeing sausage.

02:01:16.869 --> 02:01:20.239
The question is, does the
viewer want it to be tilted?

02:01:20.239 --> 02:01:23.009
I think, if we could put
a poll on the screen.

02:01:23.009 --> 02:01:23.876
Should he tilt it?

02:01:23.876 --> 02:01:26.078
I think a lot of people
would be like, please don't.

02:01:26.078 --> 02:01:27.513
Yeah, this is the Ultimate one.

02:01:27.513 --> 02:01:29.615
Sausage, obviously.
Bacon, peppers, onions,

02:01:29.615 --> 02:01:31.284
mushrooms, tomato, cheese.

02:01:32.285 --> 02:01:33.119
Eh, not bad.

02:01:33.119 --> 02:01:35.187
Everything's so wet.

02:01:35.187 --> 02:01:36.455
It's dripping with water.

02:01:36.455 --> 02:01:38.524
And this one must be therefore
the Philly cheesesteak.

02:01:38.524 --> 02:01:41.827
Grilled prime rib, peppers,
onions, mushroom, Swiss cheese.

02:01:41.827 --> 02:01:43.429
Ooh, prime.

02:01:43.429 --> 02:01:46.699
You will not find the following
pancake options in the UK.

02:01:46.699 --> 02:01:47.967
Starting down here,

02:01:47.967 --> 02:01:52.571
they got the choconana, which
is chocolate and banana.

02:01:52.571 --> 02:01:54.774
Every one of these comes
with, like, eggs and,

02:01:54.774 --> 02:01:55.908
again, you just don't get pancakes.

02:01:55.908 --> 02:01:57.410
I feel like I want to point this out.

02:01:57.410 --> 02:01:59.779
Are you aware, UK? Because I
haven't seen Harry's footage.

02:01:59.779 --> 02:02:01.314
Every pancake order comes

02:02:01.314 --> 02:02:04.784
with eggs and hash browns and meats.

02:02:04.784 --> 02:02:07.286
Look at this. It's
ridiculous. It's so much food.

02:02:07.286 --> 02:02:09.588
Next to that is the double berry.

02:02:09.588 --> 02:02:11.223
I mean, I see strawberries.

02:02:11.223 --> 02:02:14.327
Oh. Because it's a berry pancake.

02:02:14.327 --> 02:02:16.462
Ugh. Actually, it's not very good.

02:02:16.462 --> 02:02:17.797
The strawberries are weird.

02:02:17.797 --> 02:02:19.699
Hearty nine-grain pancakes.

02:02:20.566 --> 02:02:22.201
I can't tell how many
grains are in this pancake.

02:02:22.201 --> 02:02:23.469
Can you at home?

02:02:23.469 --> 02:02:24.303
I have no idea.

02:02:24.303 --> 02:02:27.907
And the cinnamon roll pancakes.

02:02:27.907 --> 02:02:30.443
I'm sure at this point the
Cinnabon episode is out.

02:02:30.443 --> 02:02:31.544
Oh, my God.

02:02:33.446 --> 02:02:34.780
Ooh, that's trouble.

02:02:34.780 --> 02:02:35.781
That's really good.

02:02:35.781 --> 02:02:37.550
And at the end, this is really funny.

02:02:37.550 --> 02:02:39.985
It's a crepe. A berry vanilla crepe.

02:02:39.985 --> 02:02:41.721
There's something weird
with their strawberries.

02:02:41.721 --> 02:02:44.090
We have some exclusive
pancake options of our own.

02:02:44.090 --> 02:02:45.925
One thing to point out is that Americans

02:02:45.925 --> 02:02:47.860
have this kind of
pancakes-for-breakfast culture,

02:02:47.860 --> 02:02:49.795
and that really does not exist in the UK.

02:02:49.795 --> 02:02:51.697
Over here, pancake generally means crepe,

02:02:51.697 --> 02:02:53.065
so like a thin pancake,

02:02:53.065 --> 02:02:54.800
and they're traditionally
more eaten for dessert.

02:02:54.800 --> 02:02:55.968
Denny's pancakes in the UK

02:02:55.968 --> 02:02:57.803
are the kind of thick American-style ones.

02:02:57.803 --> 02:02:59.872
However, the toppings and the sauces

02:02:59.872 --> 02:03:02.575
tend to reflect our
dessert-pancake culture a bit more.

02:03:02.575 --> 02:03:04.176
We'll start with a
classic pancake topping,

02:03:04.176 --> 02:03:05.778
which is Nutella.

02:03:05.778 --> 02:03:06.712
I pronounce it "nut-ell-uh."

02:03:06.712 --> 02:03:08.981
Some people say "new-tell-uh."

02:03:08.981 --> 02:03:10.383
Leon: Who says "new-tell-uh"?

02:03:10.383 --> 02:03:13.452
I've definitely — do
Americans say "new-tell-uh"?

02:03:13.452 --> 02:03:14.720
Do you guys say "new-tell-uh"?

02:03:14.720 --> 02:03:16.555
That's horrible. Please don't do that.

02:03:16.555 --> 02:03:17.423
It's "nut-ell-uh."

02:03:17.423 --> 02:03:20.292
Over here we have the
double chocolate pancakes.

02:03:20.292 --> 02:03:22.561
I think the double chocolate refers to

02:03:22.561 --> 02:03:24.730
the chocolate chips in
the pancakes themselves

02:03:24.730 --> 02:03:26.832
and also this rather large amount

02:03:26.832 --> 02:03:28.434
of chocolate drizzle on top.

02:03:28.434 --> 02:03:31.637
Next up, we have some
strawberry dream pancakes,

02:03:31.637 --> 02:03:34.340
which have not held up
super well in transit,

02:03:34.340 --> 02:03:35.341
I'll be honest.

02:03:35.341 --> 02:03:37.610
These are looking less like
strawberry dream pancakes

02:03:37.610 --> 02:03:40.012
and more like strawberry
nightmare pancakes.

02:03:40.012 --> 02:03:42.014
What is this sauce that's just, like,

02:03:42.014 --> 02:03:42.848
fallen off the pancake?

02:03:45.985 --> 02:03:47.486
Like, a very sweet

02:03:47.486 --> 02:03:50.890
maybe white-chocolate-vanillary-type
cream thing.

02:03:50.890 --> 02:03:53.692
Over here, we have the
Oreo cookie pancakes.

02:03:53.692 --> 02:03:55.294
I think there are chocolate pieces

02:03:55.294 --> 02:03:58.330
or maybe the cookie pieces
in the pancake as well.

02:03:58.330 --> 02:03:59.899
Then it's topped with some more

02:03:59.899 --> 02:04:02.368
of this kind of sweet
cream stuff they have.

02:04:02.368 --> 02:04:04.537
Next up, we have a Kinder Bueno pancake.

02:04:04.537 --> 02:04:06.405
Do Americans know what Kinder Bueno is?

02:04:06.405 --> 02:04:07.573
It's a chocolate bar.

02:04:07.573 --> 02:04:09.942
Very popular in Europe and the UK.

02:04:09.942 --> 02:04:12.344
I don't know what the cream
stuff inside of it is,

02:04:12.344 --> 02:04:16.515
but one of the best-tasting
things in the world.

02:04:16.515 --> 02:04:18.350
And then, finally, because
it's near Valentine's Day

02:04:18.350 --> 02:04:20.186
here in the UK while we're filming this,

02:04:20.186 --> 02:04:22.054
we can get some Valentine's pancakes.

02:04:22.054 --> 02:04:24.290
These red velvet ones.

02:04:24.290 --> 02:04:27.126
These are the exact colors that you see

02:04:27.126 --> 02:04:29.595
on snakes that you are
supposed to run away from

02:04:29.595 --> 02:04:30.796
if you see them in the wild.

02:04:30.796 --> 02:04:32.565
We don't have any crepes
on the menu in the UK,

02:04:32.565 --> 02:04:33.799
but we do have waffles.

02:04:33.799 --> 02:04:35.601
These are also generally
desserts in the UK,

02:04:35.601 --> 02:04:37.436
and Denny's serves them
in the following flavors.

02:04:37.436 --> 02:04:39.572
Here we have a fresh fruit waffle.

02:04:39.572 --> 02:04:42.608
Each one seems to be one
whole circular waffle

02:04:42.608 --> 02:04:44.410
cut into quarters and then topped

02:04:44.410 --> 02:04:47.079
with powdered sugar and
some other toppings.

02:04:47.079 --> 02:04:48.714
With the fresh fruit one you're getting

02:04:48.714 --> 02:04:50.349
some banana and some strawberry.

02:04:50.349 --> 02:04:52.151
Here we have a golden waffle.

02:04:52.151 --> 02:04:54.019
That's a waffle with golden syrup,

02:04:54.019 --> 02:04:57.022
which is kind of like a
British version of maple syrup.

02:04:57.022 --> 02:04:58.123
Some of the waffles on the menu

02:04:58.123 --> 02:05:00.793
also come as Liège-style waffles.

02:05:00.793 --> 02:05:03.496
Liège is a place in
Belgium. Belgian waffles.

02:05:03.496 --> 02:05:06.932
They're a little bit more dense
than the American waffles.

02:05:06.932 --> 02:05:10.402
Next up, we have a Nutella
waffle, not "new-tell-uh."

02:05:10.402 --> 02:05:12.004
Then we have a Kinder Bueno waffle.

02:05:12.004 --> 02:05:13.639
The sauce stuff really does capture

02:05:13.639 --> 02:05:14.907
the flavor of Kinder Bueno.

02:05:14.907 --> 02:05:16.342
You can just get a plain waffle

02:05:16.342 --> 02:05:17.743
with just some of the whipped butter

02:05:17.743 --> 02:05:19.144
that you get with the pancakes.

02:05:19.144 --> 02:05:20.846
And then finally, another Liège option

02:05:20.846 --> 02:05:23.415
is the banana and salted caramel waffle.

02:05:23.415 --> 02:05:24.683
Great flavor combination.

02:05:24.683 --> 02:05:25.718
Big fan of that.

02:05:25.718 --> 02:05:27.152
Now that we've reset
the table, let's move on

02:05:27.152 --> 02:05:29.321
to some other options,
starting with sandwiches.

02:05:29.321 --> 02:05:31.824
Start here with the New York melt.

02:05:31.824 --> 02:05:34.026
We're more American than the Americans.

02:05:34.026 --> 02:05:35.160
Let's try the pastrami.

02:05:36.128 --> 02:05:38.831
We're not very good at deli
meats in the UK on average.

02:05:42.201 --> 02:05:44.270
Up next, we have the three-cheese melt.

02:05:44.270 --> 02:05:46.372
Pretty much just a grilled cheese

02:05:46.372 --> 02:05:48.240
with three types of cheese in here.

02:05:48.240 --> 02:05:49.942
Here we have the Mac and Me.

02:05:49.942 --> 02:05:52.645
This is a grilled-cheese sandwich

02:05:52.645 --> 02:05:56.015
filled with mac and cheese and bacon bits.

02:05:56.015 --> 02:05:59.084
We've just been discussing
double carbs and established

02:05:59.084 --> 02:06:01.887
that there are circumstances
where double carb is OK,

02:06:01.887 --> 02:06:05.457
but the bread-pasta combination
in this circumstance

02:06:05.457 --> 02:06:07.092
seems to just unsettle me

02:06:07.092 --> 02:06:09.061
for some reason I can't
really put a word to.

02:06:09.061 --> 02:06:11.797
Then our last exclusive
sandwich is the club sandwich.

02:06:11.797 --> 02:06:13.399
You guys do have a club
sandwich in the US,

02:06:13.399 --> 02:06:16.569
but I believe it has avocado,
whereas ours does not.

02:06:16.569 --> 02:06:20.606
We have a bunch of exclusive
sandwich options in the US.

02:06:20.606 --> 02:06:22.041
I mean, the website splits them into

02:06:22.041 --> 02:06:25.311
classic breakfast options and
meats and handheld options.

02:06:25.311 --> 02:06:27.279
All right, we'll start
with the breakfast one,

02:06:27.279 --> 02:06:30.149
the My Hammy Spice.

02:06:30.149 --> 02:06:33.485
It's the same thing except
it's got jalapeños in it.

02:06:33.485 --> 02:06:34.320
Look at that.

02:06:34.320 --> 02:06:37.856
This thing is just dripping with butter.

02:06:37.856 --> 02:06:39.258
And then we have the rest,
which I don't think are

02:06:39.258 --> 02:06:40.426
supposed to be eaten for breakfast.

02:06:40.426 --> 02:06:44.530
They do have a Brisk-B-Q
melt and a Brisk-It-All melt,

02:06:44.530 --> 02:06:46.198
which I was not able to get today,

02:06:46.198 --> 02:06:49.868
but what we do have is
the Cali club sandwich.

02:06:49.868 --> 02:06:52.371
We also got the Super Bird.

02:06:52.371 --> 02:06:54.506
What? What is this? Like ...

02:06:54.506 --> 02:06:56.875
Turkey, bacon, and tomato and cheese.

02:06:58.410 --> 02:06:59.511
Not bad.

02:06:59.511 --> 02:07:00.913
The Big Dipper melt.

02:07:00.913 --> 02:07:02.948
This is just a, what
looks to be a patty melt

02:07:02.948 --> 02:07:05.517
with about half a gallon of au jus.

02:07:05.517 --> 02:07:06.452
Look at that.

02:07:10.255 --> 02:07:12.424
I love a good patty melt.
That's a pretty good one.

02:07:12.424 --> 02:07:16.929
Next up is this monstrosity,
the fried cheese melt.

02:07:16.929 --> 02:07:19.798
Now, when I heard that
and put in for the order,

02:07:19.798 --> 02:07:21.900
I was assuming it was
going to be like, in a way,

02:07:21.900 --> 02:07:24.470
something like grilled
cheese, like they fried cheese

02:07:24.470 --> 02:07:27.106
or it's just a funny way
of saying grilled cheese.

02:07:27.106 --> 02:07:28.307
No, not at all.

02:07:28.307 --> 02:07:31.010
This is actually a
sandwich that consists of

02:07:31.010 --> 02:07:32.645
mozzarella sticks.

02:07:32.645 --> 02:07:35.114
Look at this. Are you
kidding me? Look at this.

02:07:35.114 --> 02:07:37.583
I'm going to take the
top off of one of these.

02:07:38.584 --> 02:07:39.418
Look at this.

02:07:39.418 --> 02:07:42.955
And it even comes with
marinara sauce, yeah.

02:07:42.955 --> 02:07:44.323
It even says in the
script that Harry wrote,

02:07:44.323 --> 02:07:45.557
"Mozzarella stick sandwich.

02:07:45.557 --> 02:07:46.792
You've got to be kidding me."

02:07:46.792 --> 02:07:48.293
We are not kidding you, apparently.

02:07:48.293 --> 02:07:49.294
We have one.

02:07:51.964 --> 02:07:53.899
That's the stupidest
thing I've ever eaten.

02:07:53.899 --> 02:07:58.237
Other sandwiches you can
get that I did not get

02:07:58.237 --> 02:08:01.807
include the Nashville hot chicken melt,

02:08:01.807 --> 02:08:02.941
the BLT,

02:08:02.941 --> 02:08:07.813
and the crispy chicken
bacon ranch sandwich.

02:08:07.813 --> 02:08:09.715
In one of the boxes when we
were unpacking everything,

02:08:09.715 --> 02:08:11.450
I just found three chicken tenders.

02:08:11.450 --> 02:08:12.818
I was a bit confused
because we didn't order

02:08:12.818 --> 02:08:15.387
any chicken tenders. I ate
them because I was hungry.

02:08:15.387 --> 02:08:17.956
And now looking back I
realize that that was part of

02:08:17.956 --> 02:08:19.992
one of our main options,
which is chicken and waffles.

02:08:19.992 --> 02:08:22.227
You get a portion of plain waffles

02:08:22.227 --> 02:08:24.296
and three chicken tenders
and some maple syrup.

02:08:24.296 --> 02:08:25.898
Combine them all, chicken and waffles.

02:08:25.898 --> 02:08:28.600
But unfortunately,
already gone. Sorry, guys.

02:08:28.600 --> 02:08:31.837
Moving on. We have the
barbecue bacon burger.

02:08:31.837 --> 02:08:35.240
It's a single cheeseburger with
two large rashers of bacon.

02:08:35.240 --> 02:08:38.310
For the vegetarians, UK Denny's
also has a veggie burger.

02:08:38.310 --> 02:08:40.646
Veggie burgers just always
look a bit sad, don't they?

02:08:40.646 --> 02:08:42.614
Also, where's the sauce, guys?

02:08:42.614 --> 02:08:44.850
Come on. This is dry as a bone.

02:08:44.850 --> 02:08:47.019
It smells almost like falafel,

02:08:47.019 --> 02:08:49.188
or maybe like a vegetable samosa.

02:08:49.188 --> 02:08:51.623
And our last sandwich
option is a chicken burger.

02:08:51.623 --> 02:08:53.392
General note here, Denny's,

02:08:53.392 --> 02:08:55.761
please sauce your burgers.

02:08:55.761 --> 02:08:57.563
These are all quite dry.

02:08:57.563 --> 02:08:59.398
But here we have two chicken tenders

02:08:59.398 --> 02:09:01.700
with a slice of cheddar cheese in a bun.

02:09:01.700 --> 02:09:03.469
This looks like a spaceship.

02:09:03.469 --> 02:09:08.440
Is there a "Star Wars" spaceship
that's shaped like this?

02:09:08.440 --> 02:09:10.843
That's shaped really, like,

02:09:10.843 --> 02:09:12.478
I don't know. I don't know what it is.

02:09:14.713 --> 02:09:16.048
Then for the health-conscious among us,

02:09:16.048 --> 02:09:17.416
we have two salad options,

02:09:17.416 --> 02:09:20.085
starting with the crispy chicken salad.

02:09:20.085 --> 02:09:22.321
And a grilled chicken salad.

02:09:22.321 --> 02:09:23.822
In the US, we also have a ton

02:09:23.822 --> 02:09:26.625
of main-course options
you won't find in the UK.

02:09:26.625 --> 02:09:27.860
Didn't get all of them.

02:09:27.860 --> 02:09:29.895
I will start with the burgers.

02:09:29.895 --> 02:09:33.499
In the US, we have bacon avocado burger.

02:09:33.499 --> 02:09:37.970
There's also the before-shown Slamburger.

02:09:37.970 --> 02:09:41.273
That's all the Grand Slam
breakfast in burger form.

02:09:41.273 --> 02:09:43.008
So weird, yet it exists.

02:09:43.008 --> 02:09:44.910
It's got a little egg hanging on here.

02:09:44.910 --> 02:09:46.311
Ah!

02:09:46.311 --> 02:09:48.480
And the flamin' five-pepper burger.

02:09:48.480 --> 02:09:50.516
There's also a bourbon bacon burger

02:09:50.516 --> 02:09:52.317
that was not available
at the time of filming.

02:09:52.317 --> 02:09:55.254
We also have bowls, bowls, bowls.

02:09:55.254 --> 02:09:56.321
So many bowls to choose from.

02:09:56.321 --> 02:09:57.689
I only got one.

02:09:57.689 --> 02:10:00.826
That's the Mama D's pot roast.

02:10:00.826 --> 02:10:03.829
I'm assuming the D stands for Denny's,

02:10:03.829 --> 02:10:06.632
or delicious, or deadly.

02:10:06.632 --> 02:10:08.400
There's also the crazy spicy bowl

02:10:08.400 --> 02:10:10.869
and the bourbon chicken bowl.

02:10:10.869 --> 02:10:13.172
Entrées, you saw a lot of
this in the breakfast section,

02:10:13.172 --> 02:10:14.573
so I don't have to waste
too much time on it.

02:10:14.573 --> 02:10:18.076
First thing we got here is the
Plate Lickin' fried chicken,

02:10:18.076 --> 02:10:20.646
and this one I got a
side of mashed potatoes

02:10:20.646 --> 02:10:22.347
and a little veggie medley.

02:10:22.347 --> 02:10:25.017
The next thing we got
here is the sirloin steak.

02:10:25.017 --> 02:10:28.053
Who told you to smother this in

02:10:28.053 --> 02:10:30.589
onions and mushrooms?

02:10:32.191 --> 02:10:33.025
This is a hockey puck.

02:10:33.025 --> 02:10:36.061
Other sides you can get:
fries and a veggie medley.

02:10:36.061 --> 02:10:39.231
T-bone steak, you've seen
it, with corn and vegetables.

02:10:39.231 --> 02:10:40.899
This right here,

02:10:40.899 --> 02:10:44.570
country-fried steak dinner.

02:10:44.570 --> 02:10:49.208
Two country-fried steaks
smothered in white sausage gravy,

02:10:49.208 --> 02:10:50.809
and, of course, comes with corn,

02:10:50.809 --> 02:10:52.411
and I think that's mashed potatoes.

02:10:52.411 --> 02:10:55.147
And you can also get
a wild Alaskan salmon.

02:10:55.147 --> 02:10:57.049
I'm not bringing cooked
fish in the studio.

02:10:57.049 --> 02:10:58.584
Not happening. All right?

02:10:58.584 --> 02:11:00.052
Use your imagination.

02:11:00.052 --> 02:11:01.854
And you can also get a Cobb salad.

02:11:01.854 --> 02:11:03.956
Didn't get that either
because it's a salad.

02:11:03.956 --> 02:11:06.191
What about the exclusive
starters and sides?

02:11:06.191 --> 02:11:08.427
Well, in the UK it's kind
of like a beige buffet.

02:11:08.427 --> 02:11:10.429
Here we have chicken poppers,

02:11:10.429 --> 02:11:12.164
just bite-size pieces of fried chicken.

02:11:13.465 --> 02:11:15.067
This food is so dry I'm having to

02:11:15.067 --> 02:11:16.969
skip ahead to the exclusives,

02:11:16.969 --> 02:11:18.904
which thankfully for me

02:11:20.272 --> 02:11:21.907
includes beer.

02:11:21.907 --> 02:11:25.010
Three of our UK exclusive sides
are actually forms of fries.

02:11:25.010 --> 02:11:26.678
Here we have cheesy fries.

02:11:26.678 --> 02:11:30.816
Chips and cheese is a
classic British dish,

02:11:30.816 --> 02:11:33.919
so I'm glad that they have
localized their menu to the UK.

02:11:33.919 --> 02:11:35.787
Then, in addition to the cheesy fries,

02:11:35.787 --> 02:11:38.490
you can add bacon to
create cheesy bacon fries.

02:11:38.490 --> 02:11:39.524
And on top of that,

02:11:39.524 --> 02:11:43.595
you can add jalapeños
to create loaded fries.

02:11:43.595 --> 02:11:47.132
This is like a Pokémon
evolving in its three stages.

02:11:47.132 --> 02:11:51.069
Cheese fries evolves
into bacon cheesy fries,

02:11:51.069 --> 02:11:53.538
evolves into loaded fries.

02:11:53.538 --> 02:11:55.207
The Charizard of fries.

02:11:57.476 --> 02:12:00.545
Then our last side dish
is a British classic.

02:12:00.545 --> 02:12:03.949
It's everyone's favorite, baked beans.

02:12:03.949 --> 02:12:05.083
There they are.

02:12:05.083 --> 02:12:07.352
These do smell like British baked beans,

02:12:07.352 --> 02:12:10.055
so kind of tomato-based
rather than barbecue.

02:12:11.089 --> 02:12:12.157
I don't have a spoon.

02:12:12.157 --> 02:12:15.260
Should I just sip from this
like a little shot glass?

02:12:15.260 --> 02:12:16.795
Leon: They're beans.

02:12:21.166 --> 02:12:22.067
They're beans.

02:12:22.067 --> 02:12:24.903
Leon: What's that meant
to go with on this menu?

02:12:24.903 --> 02:12:28.040
What wouldn't this go with
on the menu, is my question.

02:12:28.040 --> 02:12:30.309
Leon: Waffles, probably.
Beans and waffles?

02:12:30.309 --> 02:12:32.544
I reckon a bean pancake could work.

02:12:33.779 --> 02:12:34.947
You tempted fate here.

02:12:34.947 --> 02:12:36.214
Leon: What you're doing is sick.

02:12:36.214 --> 02:12:37.382
Charlie: Ugh, God.

02:12:38.583 --> 02:12:40.886
[Leon and Charlie laughing]

02:12:42.354 --> 02:12:44.089
No, that's bad.

02:12:44.089 --> 02:12:45.290
I can't even pretend that was good.

02:12:45.290 --> 02:12:47.059
Denny's has boneless wings.

02:12:47.059 --> 02:12:48.794
This is what they look like.

02:12:48.794 --> 02:12:50.329
I don't know what sauces
they have for dipping.

02:12:50.329 --> 02:12:51.196
Nobody asked.

02:12:51.196 --> 02:12:53.665
Other exclusive sides
you can get in the US,

02:12:53.665 --> 02:12:55.300
you saw all the ones from earlier.

02:12:55.300 --> 02:12:57.069
These are ones that you've
probably seen before.

02:12:57.069 --> 02:12:59.738
Biscuits and gravy, scones and gravy,

02:12:59.738 --> 02:13:03.275
an English muffin, ironically
not in England. That's weird.

02:13:03.275 --> 02:13:05.577
We also have right here

02:13:05.577 --> 02:13:08.613
this whole-grain rice.

02:13:08.613 --> 02:13:10.215
Other sides that we have

02:13:10.215 --> 02:13:13.752
either mixed within dishes
you've seen or not seen at all,

02:13:13.752 --> 02:13:17.122
wavy-cut french fries,
seasoned cut french fries,

02:13:17.122 --> 02:13:18.824
red rustic mashed potatoes.

02:13:18.824 --> 02:13:19.925
I saw those somewhere.

02:13:19.925 --> 02:13:23.295
The fresh vegetable medley
and the soup of the day,

02:13:23.295 --> 02:13:25.831
which is, from what I
remember, beef vegetable,

02:13:25.831 --> 02:13:28.100
and they told us couldn't
get it till after 11,

02:13:28.100 --> 02:13:31.403
and we picked up the food at 10:45.

02:13:31.403 --> 02:13:33.538
Now we're on to the desserts,
starting at the back here

02:13:33.538 --> 02:13:35.107
with chocolate fudge cake

02:13:35.107 --> 02:13:37.609
with what at one point was whipped cream.

02:13:37.609 --> 02:13:39.111
Then we have a few cheesecake options,

02:13:39.111 --> 02:13:41.513
starting with a Reese's cheesecake.

02:13:41.513 --> 02:13:43.982
Doesn't look very appealing.

02:13:43.982 --> 02:13:45.384
They've just kind of dumped

02:13:45.384 --> 02:13:46.918
what I assume is this kind of

02:13:46.918 --> 02:13:51.223
peanut-buttery, caramel-y
stuff on top of it.

02:13:51.223 --> 02:13:52.057
That's not bad.

02:13:52.057 --> 02:13:54.259
Moving on from Reese's, we
have an Oreo cheesecake,

02:13:54.259 --> 02:13:57.229
so the same cheesecake but with
Oreo pieces crumbled on top.

02:13:57.229 --> 02:13:58.930
And finally a Nutella cheesecake.

02:13:58.930 --> 02:14:00.332
It has fallen on its side,

02:14:00.332 --> 02:14:03.301
so, therefore, I can
prop it up, like a TV.

02:14:03.301 --> 02:14:05.003
Then we have some French toast options.

02:14:05.003 --> 02:14:07.105
I'm not sure why Denny's
classifies these as desserts,

02:14:07.105 --> 02:14:09.741
but apparently chocolaty
pancakes are a breakfast food.

02:14:09.741 --> 02:14:11.676
We'll start back here
with Oreo French toast.

02:14:11.676 --> 02:14:14.079
French toast, not much of
a thing here in the UK.

02:14:14.079 --> 02:14:16.448
What we have is eggy bread, which is like,

02:14:16.448 --> 02:14:19.584
the similar start, where
you take the bread,

02:14:19.584 --> 02:14:21.620
dunk it in egg, and fry it,

02:14:21.620 --> 02:14:23.655
but then we'll have it as a savory dish

02:14:23.655 --> 02:14:26.391
rather than as a breakfast/dessert.

02:14:26.391 --> 02:14:28.093
Then we have a banoffee French toast.

02:14:28.093 --> 02:14:29.161
For the uninitiated,

02:14:29.161 --> 02:14:32.264
banoffee is banana and
toffee amalgamated together.

02:14:32.264 --> 02:14:34.366
Then we have strawberry
dream French toast.

02:14:34.366 --> 02:14:36.835
Fresh strawberries and
some vanillary icing.

02:14:36.835 --> 02:14:38.537
Here's three exclusives
you can only get in the US

02:14:38.537 --> 02:14:41.239
and not the UK. New York-style cheesecake.

02:14:41.239 --> 02:14:44.042
Whoa! Hey, I'm walking here!

02:14:45.710 --> 02:14:47.279
The lava cookie skillet.

02:14:47.279 --> 02:14:48.647
I'm assuming that's this.

02:14:48.647 --> 02:14:49.948
I can't break it.

02:14:51.917 --> 02:14:54.719
And it comes with ice
cream, I'm sure for dipping.

02:14:54.719 --> 02:14:56.221
Yeah, pretty good.

02:14:56.221 --> 02:14:58.990
And the double chocolate pancake puppies.

02:14:58.990 --> 02:15:00.792
Like hush puppies, but pancake.

02:15:03.095 --> 02:15:04.930
Mm, eh.

02:15:04.930 --> 02:15:06.231
Then we have a a couple
more dessert options

02:15:06.231 --> 02:15:07.332
and some milkshakes.

02:15:07.332 --> 02:15:09.701
Here, we have a strawberry
ice cream sundae

02:15:09.701 --> 02:15:11.603
and a caramel ice cream sundae.

02:15:11.603 --> 02:15:12.771
Ignore the straw.

02:15:12.771 --> 02:15:14.573
I definitely did not
think it was a milkshake.

02:15:14.573 --> 02:15:17.042
I think we have identified all the shakes.

02:15:17.042 --> 02:15:19.077
I believe this is millionaire shortbread,

02:15:19.077 --> 02:15:20.345
peanut butter shake,

02:15:20.345 --> 02:15:22.347
a white chocolate and strawberry shake,

02:15:22.347 --> 02:15:25.083
cookie shake, a vegan vanilla shake,

02:15:25.083 --> 02:15:29.020
then this I think is
Bueno, and this is Nutella.

02:15:29.020 --> 02:15:30.422
I think my favorite would probably be

02:15:30.422 --> 02:15:31.857
the millionaire shortbread one.

02:15:31.857 --> 02:15:33.458
Very sweet but very tasty.

02:15:33.458 --> 02:15:37.462
And after all that, the
final exclusive, alcohol.

02:15:37.462 --> 02:15:38.663
Thank God.

02:15:40.365 --> 02:15:41.399
We can get a few beer

02:15:41.399 --> 02:15:43.068
and other alcohol options here in the UK,

02:15:43.068 --> 02:15:44.736
including this Coors Light.

02:15:44.736 --> 02:15:46.271
I think there's a Peroni beer

02:15:46.271 --> 02:15:48.707
and some Kopparberg fruity cider.

02:15:48.707 --> 02:15:49.774
Cheers, guys.

02:15:52.377 --> 02:15:53.879
According to Dennys.com,

02:15:53.879 --> 02:15:55.847
a website I now have an account with,

02:15:55.847 --> 02:15:59.551
the nearest Denny's to this
studio in Burbank, California,

02:15:59.551 --> 02:16:02.020
an All-American Slam

02:16:02.020 --> 02:16:05.357
will run you $15.29.

02:16:05.357 --> 02:16:08.560
An All-American Slam from
a UK Denny's costs £10.99,

02:16:08.560 --> 02:16:12.197
which at the time of
recording this was $13.23.

02:16:12.197 --> 02:16:13.298
That makes the American version

02:16:13.298 --> 02:16:15.967
15% more expensive than the UK's.

02:16:15.967 --> 02:16:18.069
But there's better value
to be found elsewhere

02:16:18.069 --> 02:16:21.406
on the US menu: a stack of pancakes.

02:16:21.406 --> 02:16:24.042
These very pancakes. Wow, is this right?

02:16:24.042 --> 02:16:26.378
Two of these cost $3.49.

02:16:26.378 --> 02:16:27.979
Bro, that is cheap.

02:16:27.979 --> 02:16:31.249
Two pancakes in the UK,
that'll cost you £5.79

02:16:31.249 --> 02:16:33.785
which is around $6.97.

02:16:33.785 --> 02:16:37.289
That means that the UK pancakes
are 99% more expensive.

02:16:37.289 --> 02:16:38.623
I don't consider Denny's fast food.

02:16:38.623 --> 02:16:41.593
I consider it more of a restaurant
chain, like TGI Fridays.

02:16:41.593 --> 02:16:44.629
Even though Denny's does
really lean into breakfast,

02:16:44.629 --> 02:16:46.398
it is 24 hours.

02:16:46.398 --> 02:16:48.433
So Denny's for me was always a place

02:16:48.433 --> 02:16:49.801
that you can go at any time.

02:16:49.801 --> 02:16:51.870
Just pretty much anything
you would find in a diner,

02:16:51.870 --> 02:16:53.371
you'll find at a Denny's.

02:16:53.371 --> 02:16:55.073
I used to go there a lot in high school

02:16:55.073 --> 02:16:57.275
because you could smoke in a Denny's,

02:16:57.275 --> 02:16:58.610
and it's open 24 hours.

02:16:58.610 --> 02:17:00.178
So we'd just drink
coffee, smoke cigarettes,

02:17:00.178 --> 02:17:03.048
split an appetizer, and
drive our waitress crazy.

02:17:03.048 --> 02:17:03.915
Harry wants to know,

02:17:03.915 --> 02:17:06.151
what time of day are
you going to a Denny's?

02:17:06.151 --> 02:17:07.052
I think it's more like

02:17:07.052 --> 02:17:09.688
what time of your life
are you going to Denny's?

02:17:09.688 --> 02:17:11.256
To me, I could be wrong,

02:17:11.256 --> 02:17:13.158
but the only people I see at Denny's

02:17:13.158 --> 02:17:15.560
are teenagers who want
to get out of the house

02:17:15.560 --> 02:17:18.063
and hang out and they
can't get into a bar yet,

02:17:18.063 --> 02:17:22.567
and retired people who want
to have a $4 breakfast.

02:17:22.567 --> 02:17:26.104
So once you come into
this world on your own,

02:17:26.104 --> 02:17:28.440
you start by going to
Denny's with your friends,

02:17:28.440 --> 02:17:30.809
then you go off, you live a life,

02:17:30.809 --> 02:17:32.744
you have a family, a career,

02:17:32.744 --> 02:17:34.279
you make an impact in the world,

02:17:34.279 --> 02:17:37.249
and once you retire,
back to the same Denny's.

02:17:39.217 --> 02:17:40.352
Full circle.

02:17:40.352 --> 02:17:43.822
I like the standalone diner from the '50s,

02:17:43.822 --> 02:17:46.992
has some name like Bertha's

02:17:46.992 --> 02:17:49.961
or Ethel's or Fred's,

02:17:49.961 --> 02:17:54.399
and you have as much
coffee as you want, right?

02:17:54.399 --> 02:17:57.068
And a patty melt, fries.

02:17:57.068 --> 02:17:59.504
Yeah. That to me — the chain is like, no.

02:17:59.504 --> 02:18:01.606
I like the standalone place.

02:18:01.606 --> 02:18:03.475
For me, I have to say
this is quite expensive

02:18:03.475 --> 02:18:04.342
for what it is.

02:18:04.342 --> 02:18:06.311
We don't really have a
diner culture in the UK,

02:18:06.311 --> 02:18:08.346
but what we do have is caffs.

02:18:08.346 --> 02:18:09.948
Caffs, or short for café,

02:18:09.948 --> 02:18:12.250
it's kind of like a
ubiquitous British thing.

02:18:12.250 --> 02:18:14.052
You'll find a couple
of caffs in every town

02:18:14.052 --> 02:18:16.621
where you can just get a
really cheap and cheerful meal

02:18:16.621 --> 02:18:18.089
on the go, in a hurry,

02:18:18.089 --> 02:18:19.357
and they'll really, really sort you out,

02:18:19.357 --> 02:18:20.725
generally for a lot less money

02:18:20.725 --> 02:18:21.693
than what this will run you.

02:18:21.693 --> 02:18:23.495
Between caffs and greasy spoons,

02:18:23.495 --> 02:18:25.196
which are similar but not quite the same,

02:18:25.196 --> 02:18:27.932
we really have breakfast
culture covered in that regard.

02:18:27.932 --> 02:18:29.467
That's where you're going
to get your full English,

02:18:29.467 --> 02:18:31.970
your toast, your kind
of terrible cup of tea

02:18:31.970 --> 02:18:33.672
but in quite a nice way.

02:18:33.672 --> 02:18:35.807
Yeah, so I'm not sure Denny's would really

02:18:35.807 --> 02:18:38.343
be bringing too much to the table.

02:18:38.343 --> 02:18:39.811
When I say we don't really
have much of a diner culture

02:18:39.811 --> 02:18:41.346
in the UK, I guess that's
evidenced by the fact

02:18:41.346 --> 02:18:43.982
that chains like Denny's really
haven't taken off over here.

02:18:43.982 --> 02:18:45.950
We had to actually travel to Wales,

02:18:45.950 --> 02:18:47.619
to Swansea to get this one

02:18:47.619 --> 02:18:50.322
because that's where our only
Denny's in the whole UK is.

02:18:50.322 --> 02:18:52.223
I gotta say, it was kind of
popular when we were there.

02:18:52.223 --> 02:18:53.258
It was pretty busy.

02:18:53.258 --> 02:18:55.660
Lots of families taking
their kids out for some food.

02:18:55.660 --> 02:18:57.796
I think maybe Denny's
currently is just more of a

02:18:57.796 --> 02:19:00.298
gimmicky American-style thing in the UK.

02:19:00.298 --> 02:19:02.233
If they did try to roll
out, I'm not sure that

02:19:02.233 --> 02:19:04.169
it would be really kind of filling a void

02:19:04.169 --> 02:19:06.504
that we have that isn't
already filled by caffs,

02:19:06.504 --> 02:19:07.806
greasy spoons, or something else.

02:19:10.442 --> 02:19:12.410
Unfortunately, Denny's in
the UK doesn't disclose

02:19:12.410 --> 02:19:14.145
any of its nutritional information.

02:19:14.145 --> 02:19:15.847
Denny's in the US does, however,

02:19:15.847 --> 02:19:19.050
so let's take a look
at some menu classics.

02:19:19.050 --> 02:19:21.553
One thing to note,
especially with the slams,

02:19:21.553 --> 02:19:22.887
is that customizing your order

02:19:22.887 --> 02:19:24.656
can drastically change the calories.

02:19:24.656 --> 02:19:27.325
For example, take this All-American Slam.

02:19:27.325 --> 02:19:29.461
If you choose turkey bacon as your meat,

02:19:29.461 --> 02:19:32.197
hash brown as your potato,
and white toast as your bread,

02:19:32.197 --> 02:19:36.334
it comes out to 1,050
calories. Respectable.

02:19:36.334 --> 02:19:39.637
On the flip side, you can
get the All-American Slam

02:19:39.637 --> 02:19:42.841
with sausage links, french
fries — french fries? Come on.

02:19:42.841 --> 02:19:44.209
And then upgrade your toast to an order

02:19:44.209 --> 02:19:46.411
of cinnamon roll pancakes,

02:19:46.411 --> 02:19:48.613
that doubles the calories of the meal,

02:19:48.613 --> 02:19:50.648
taking it to 2,300.

02:19:50.648 --> 02:19:53.585
That's 115% of your
daily recommended intake.

02:19:53.585 --> 02:19:54.919
And the main culprit here,

02:19:54.919 --> 02:19:57.522
if it wasn't obvious, the
cinnamon roll pancakes.

02:19:57.522 --> 02:20:01.092
Just two of these contain 1,100 calories.

02:20:01.092 --> 02:20:03.194
A nutritional-information
document from Denny's

02:20:03.194 --> 02:20:04.996
dated back in 2020

02:20:04.996 --> 02:20:07.399
also suggested that two
cinnamon roll pancakes

02:20:07.399 --> 02:20:10.802
with cream cheese icing
contains 157 grams of sugar.

02:20:10.802 --> 02:20:14.372
That's 254% of your daily allowance.

02:20:14.372 --> 02:20:15.673
Zoom in for effect.

02:20:15.673 --> 02:20:17.041
Gah!

02:20:17.275 --> 02:20:18.843
Harry: From calorie
count to portion sizes,

02:20:18.843 --> 02:20:20.245
we wanted to find out all the differences

02:20:20.245 --> 02:20:22.747
between Kit Kat in the US and the UK.

02:20:22.747 --> 02:20:24.416
This is "Food Wars."

02:20:26.951 --> 02:20:29.821
In the US, our Kit Kats
come in nine sizes.

02:20:29.821 --> 02:20:30.655
Yes, really.

02:20:30.655 --> 02:20:33.625
Down here we got the
smallest, the minis unwrapped.

02:20:33.625 --> 02:20:35.293
Then we go up to the thins.

02:20:35.293 --> 02:20:37.796
After that, miniatures.

02:20:37.796 --> 02:20:39.998
Right here, we got the snack size,

02:20:39.998 --> 02:20:43.268
and then the classic,
standard four-finger Kit Kat,

02:20:43.268 --> 02:20:44.969
and then the big Kat,

02:20:44.969 --> 02:20:47.472
the big Kat king size,

02:20:47.472 --> 02:20:49.007
the king size,

02:20:49.908 --> 02:20:53.812
and the XL.

02:20:53.812 --> 02:20:56.948
In the UK, classic Kit
Kat comes in three sizes.

02:20:56.948 --> 02:20:59.250
As these adorable little bites,

02:20:59.250 --> 02:21:00.985
as a two-finger Kit Kat,

02:21:00.985 --> 02:21:02.487
or as a four-finger Kit Kat.

02:21:04.422 --> 02:21:05.957
In the US, our Kit Kat sizes

02:21:05.957 --> 02:21:08.860
come in obnoxious varieties
of units and weights.

02:21:08.860 --> 02:21:11.429
Too many to show you today. See?

02:21:11.429 --> 02:21:13.198
But let's take a look
at some of the biggest

02:21:13.198 --> 02:21:15.867
two- and four-finger
portion sizes you can get.

02:21:15.867 --> 02:21:18.036
In the UK, the biggest size
of the two-finger Kit Kats

02:21:18.036 --> 02:21:19.437
is this 21-pack.

02:21:19.437 --> 02:21:22.674
All of these add up to
around 435 grams of Kit Kat,

02:21:22.674 --> 02:21:23.541
half a kilo.

02:21:23.541 --> 02:21:25.376
The biggest pack size for
the four-finger Kit Kats

02:21:25.376 --> 02:21:28.980
is a 24-pack, totaling
996 grams of Kit Kat,

02:21:28.980 --> 02:21:30.148
basically a kilogram.

02:21:30.148 --> 02:21:32.050
Although unfortunately, I
couldn't find that today.

02:21:32.050 --> 02:21:33.751
The UK will be stunned to learn

02:21:33.751 --> 02:21:36.454
the two-finger size is
not native to the US.

02:21:36.454 --> 02:21:38.223
The closest thing we
have is our snack size,

02:21:38.223 --> 02:21:40.558
which is 7.75 grams smaller.

02:21:40.558 --> 02:21:42.527
However, that being said, in the US,

02:21:42.527 --> 02:21:46.297
you can get a snack-size
bulk bag of 66 pieces,

02:21:46.297 --> 02:21:48.633
which is 916 grams.

02:21:48.633 --> 02:21:50.235
And then there's the four-finger size,

02:21:50.235 --> 02:21:55.173
which comes in a 36-pack
and is 1,512 grams.

02:21:55.173 --> 02:21:56.608
Kit Kat, I have a bone to pick with you.

02:21:56.608 --> 02:21:59.577
What is with the packaging
of these new Kit Kats?

02:21:59.577 --> 02:22:02.514
These two-finger ones had such
iconic packaging in the UK.

02:22:02.514 --> 02:22:04.015
It was wrapped in foil,

02:22:04.015 --> 02:22:06.317
and then had this band of
paper going around the outside.

02:22:06.317 --> 02:22:08.119
And now they've replaced it with plastic.

02:22:08.119 --> 02:22:09.220
Bring back the old packaging.

02:22:11.556 --> 02:22:14.292
A four-finger Kit Kat in
the UK will cost you £0.70,

02:22:14.292 --> 02:22:16.661
which is around $0.87 in the US.

02:22:16.661 --> 02:22:19.964
In the US, one of these costs $1.49,

02:22:19.964 --> 02:22:21.699
or £1.20.

02:22:21.699 --> 02:22:25.703
That's a 71% cost increase in the US.

02:22:25.703 --> 02:22:28.706
71% more expensive in the US!

02:22:28.706 --> 02:22:31.142
That's quite rare, particularly
when it comes to snacks.

02:22:31.142 --> 02:22:34.712
I feel like in the UK, we
tend to get stung for snacks,

02:22:34.712 --> 02:22:36.381
even more so than, like, fast food.

02:22:36.381 --> 02:22:38.783
So, hey, we're doing something right.

02:22:38.783 --> 02:22:41.986
Imagine if prices of these
went up by £0.50 in the UK.

02:22:41.986 --> 02:22:43.021
There would be riots.

02:22:43.021 --> 02:22:45.189
Yeah, the streets would be burning.

02:22:47.392 --> 02:22:50.161
Here are all the Kit Kat
exclusives you can get in the US

02:22:50.161 --> 02:22:52.497
you can't get in the
UK, unless, of course,

02:22:52.497 --> 02:22:54.866
your grocery store has
an American section.

02:22:54.866 --> 02:22:57.535
Here are all the UK Kit Kats
you can't get in the US,

02:22:57.535 --> 02:22:59.304
unless you have access to the internet.

02:22:59.304 --> 02:23:01.706
Just about every portion
size that we have,

02:23:01.706 --> 02:23:06.044
save for the four-finger
version, the UK does not have.

02:23:06.044 --> 02:23:08.146
Get a closer look. The
minis, the unwrapped.

02:23:08.146 --> 02:23:09.948
And they want to act
like this is for sharing,

02:23:09.948 --> 02:23:13.251
but once your hand goes in
there, it's yours, right?

02:23:13.251 --> 02:23:14.419
Also with the minis,

02:23:14.419 --> 02:23:17.188
they look a lot like your
UK bites from the outside.

02:23:17.188 --> 02:23:20.792
Now, from what I can tell,
the inside of one of these

02:23:20.792 --> 02:23:22.393
still kind of looks like a Kit Kat.

02:23:22.393 --> 02:23:24.028
Yours look like ...

02:23:24.028 --> 02:23:25.730
almost like a Crunch bar.
Does that make sense?

02:23:25.730 --> 02:23:28.232
Let's cut to Harry, where he's
just bitten inside of a bite,

02:23:28.232 --> 02:23:30.201
and tell us how it looks inside. Harry.

02:23:31.369 --> 02:23:32.370
Yeah.

02:23:33.404 --> 02:23:34.906
I don't know how much of this you can see,

02:23:34.906 --> 02:23:37.942
but you're not getting
the distinct wafer layers

02:23:37.942 --> 02:23:39.544
that you're used to from a Kit Kat.

02:23:39.544 --> 02:23:41.279
It's pretty much just solid chocolate

02:23:41.279 --> 02:23:44.782
with little pieces of biscuity
wafer in there instead.

02:23:44.782 --> 02:23:46.651
I'm not quite sure what
the point of the thins are,

02:23:46.651 --> 02:23:48.453
because the smaller one has less calories.

02:23:48.453 --> 02:23:49.454
But if you have a little bag of them,

02:23:49.454 --> 02:23:50.888
you're just going to eat
the whole bag, right?

02:23:52.423 --> 02:23:54.592
Oh, God. The hazelnut,

02:23:54.592 --> 02:23:56.394
that's not nearly as good
as a regular Kit Kat.

02:23:56.394 --> 02:23:57.795
Then we're on to my
personal favorite range,

02:23:57.795 --> 02:23:59.430
which is Kit Kat chunkies.

02:23:59.430 --> 02:24:01.399
Firstly, you can get a
standard Kit Kat chunky,

02:24:01.399 --> 02:24:03.067
but in a duo pack.

02:24:03.067 --> 02:24:05.403
This is just a standard
unflavored Kit Kat chunky,

02:24:05.403 --> 02:24:06.904
but in a two-pack.

02:24:06.904 --> 02:24:09.207
Although they're not
full-sized chunky bars.

02:24:09.207 --> 02:24:10.541
There's, like, kind of two,

02:24:10.541 --> 02:24:12.343
I guess, maybe two-thirds chunky bars.

02:24:12.343 --> 02:24:13.678
So it's still bigger than a standard one,

02:24:13.678 --> 02:24:15.713
but not an official double.

02:24:15.713 --> 02:24:19.150
Now, this next size we got is the big Kat.

02:24:19.150 --> 02:24:20.785
And I know what all you Kit Kat-heads

02:24:20.785 --> 02:24:22.420
are saying in the UK right now.

02:24:22.420 --> 02:24:23.821
It's not the chunky.

02:24:23.821 --> 02:24:27.625
Your chunky is 40 grams.
This one is 42 grams.

02:24:27.625 --> 02:24:31.996
And it says right here on the
package, "five crispy wafers."

02:24:31.996 --> 02:24:35.033
And, Yuelei, if you can get
a close-up on that pic there.

02:24:35.033 --> 02:24:37.702
That is in fact five crispy wafers.

02:24:37.702 --> 02:24:39.504
I'm looking at the pic of yours online.

02:24:39.504 --> 02:24:41.506
Y'all got four. We got five.

02:24:41.506 --> 02:24:44.375
Big, chunky, get outta here!

02:24:44.375 --> 02:24:46.811
Firstly, why do you guys
call these big Kats?

02:24:46.811 --> 02:24:48.379
Because chunky is a way better name.

02:24:48.379 --> 02:24:50.481
It's much more fun. Just
call them Kit Kat chunky.

02:24:50.481 --> 02:24:52.684
And then our biggest size, the XL,

02:24:52.684 --> 02:24:55.887
which from what I can
tell is three Kit Kats.

02:24:55.887 --> 02:24:57.088
It's 12 pieces.

02:24:57.088 --> 02:25:00.425
Put the price of a Kit Kat on-screen,

02:25:00.425 --> 02:25:02.960
then put the price of the XL on screen.

02:25:02.960 --> 02:25:04.595
Is it exactly three times?

02:25:04.595 --> 02:25:06.164
Maybe sending one of these to the ocean

02:25:06.164 --> 02:25:07.565
is better than sending three smaller ones.

02:25:07.565 --> 02:25:08.399
I really don't know.

02:25:08.399 --> 02:25:10.168
Then we're on to some of the
exclusive Kit Kat flavors

02:25:10.168 --> 02:25:11.636
you can find only in the UK.

02:25:11.636 --> 02:25:14.405
We'll start with this one,
which is a vegan Kit Kat.

02:25:14.405 --> 02:25:16.708
Hang on. Hang on a minute.

02:25:16.708 --> 02:25:18.076
I've only just gotten this.

02:25:18.076 --> 02:25:20.211
Vegan Kit Kat, and then right at the top,

02:25:20.211 --> 02:25:21.546
there's a little warning label that says,

02:25:21.546 --> 02:25:22.947
"May contain milk."

02:25:22.947 --> 02:25:24.482
You had one job, guys!

02:25:24.482 --> 02:25:26.250
I think I should do a blind taste test.

02:25:26.250 --> 02:25:28.519
Charlie has confirmed that
they do look different,

02:25:28.519 --> 02:25:31.055
so my eyes are staying closed.

02:25:31.055 --> 02:25:32.623
Thank you, Charlie.

02:25:32.623 --> 02:25:34.859
This one feels very smooth.

02:25:37.528 --> 02:25:39.997
I mean, I'm already pretty
sure that's the vegan one.

02:25:41.699 --> 02:25:44.402
I'm confident this is the regular one.

02:25:44.402 --> 02:25:45.436
But this isn't bad.

02:25:45.436 --> 02:25:46.971
Sometimes when you have a vegan option,

02:25:46.971 --> 02:25:48.439
it's, like, actively bad.

02:25:48.439 --> 02:25:50.842
This one isn't offensive by any means.

02:25:50.842 --> 02:25:52.076
Was I correct?
Charlie: Yes.

02:25:52.076 --> 02:25:53.878
I was correct. Cool.

02:25:53.878 --> 02:25:55.713
So, we have four flavor options in the UK

02:25:55.713 --> 02:25:57.749
which I believe you
will not find in the US.

02:25:57.749 --> 02:26:00.218
We have a white chocolate Kit Kat.

02:26:02.587 --> 02:26:04.789
That's fine. I'm not the
biggest white chocolate guy.

02:26:04.789 --> 02:26:06.557
An orange chocolate Kit Kat.

02:26:11.496 --> 02:26:14.298
See, I'm not normally a big
orange chocolate fan either,

02:26:14.298 --> 02:26:16.701
but that's not bad. It's
quite a subtle orange flavor,

02:26:16.701 --> 02:26:17.935
not too in-your-face.

02:26:17.935 --> 02:26:20.738
And here we have the caramel
Kit Kat, which I think is new.

02:26:24.909 --> 02:26:25.743
It's pretty good.

02:26:25.743 --> 02:26:28.279
I get more, like, honeycomb
than caramel from this.

02:26:28.279 --> 02:26:30.148
Definitely sweeter than
the standard Kit Kat.

02:26:30.148 --> 02:26:32.216
And a dark chocolate Kit Kat.

02:26:35.553 --> 02:26:36.821
I don't normally go for dark chocolate,

02:26:36.821 --> 02:26:38.756
but I will eat it sometimes,

02:26:38.756 --> 02:26:41.592
and that's not particularly
good dark chocolate.

02:26:41.592 --> 02:26:43.628
Four flavors that I have seen before

02:26:43.628 --> 02:26:46.097
that currently don't seem
available anywhere online,

02:26:46.097 --> 02:26:47.265
couldn't get my hands on them:

02:26:47.265 --> 02:26:50.434
apple pie Kit Kat, the
lemon crisp Kit Kat,

02:26:50.434 --> 02:26:52.737
the key lime Kit Kat, which is very good,

02:26:52.737 --> 02:26:55.406
and, of course, the birthday cake Kit Kat.

02:26:55.406 --> 02:26:59.010
But what I could get my hand
on are the Kit Kat duos,

02:26:59.010 --> 02:27:02.079
which are different chocolate flavors

02:27:02.079 --> 02:27:03.648
on the top and the bottom.

02:27:03.648 --> 02:27:05.783
OK, mint and dark chocolate.

02:27:05.783 --> 02:27:07.518
Oh, yeah, look at that.

02:27:07.518 --> 02:27:08.486
See, look at that.

02:27:13.791 --> 02:27:16.060
Yeah, like a Thin Mint.

02:27:16.060 --> 02:27:17.061
This is pretty good.

02:27:17.061 --> 02:27:19.463
Mocha and chocolate. Mocha and chocolate?

02:27:19.463 --> 02:27:21.032
What's the difference
between mocha and chocolate?

02:27:23.401 --> 02:27:25.002
That's the difference. Coffee.

02:27:25.002 --> 02:27:27.171
Ooh, last but not least,

02:27:27.171 --> 02:27:29.240
strawberry and dark chocolate.

02:27:29.240 --> 02:27:31.642
Oh, look, it's kind of
like my color palette.

02:27:31.642 --> 02:27:34.712
[ominous music]

02:27:34.712 --> 02:27:36.981
Mm.

02:27:36.981 --> 02:27:39.483
This is the best one.
This is the best one.

02:27:39.483 --> 02:27:40.418
The next exclusive flavor

02:27:40.418 --> 02:27:42.153
is the Kit Kat chunky peanut butter.

02:27:42.153 --> 02:27:43.588
These are incredible.

02:27:43.588 --> 02:27:45.590
These are one of my
favorite chocolate bars,

02:27:45.590 --> 02:27:46.991
I would say, in the UK.

02:27:48.392 --> 02:27:50.294
The king of chocolate bars.

02:27:50.294 --> 02:27:51.696
Can we get a little crown

02:27:51.696 --> 02:27:54.632
on the Kit Kat chunky
peanut butter, please?

02:27:54.632 --> 02:27:55.466
Thank you.

02:27:55.466 --> 02:27:58.135
The next exclusive chunky
flavor is the caramel.

02:27:58.135 --> 02:28:00.571
We also have this in the
standard Kit Kat version.

02:28:00.571 --> 02:28:02.640
But let's give the chunky
one a try real quick.

02:28:04.041 --> 02:28:05.710
Ooh!

02:28:05.710 --> 02:28:08.012
This is very different to
the two-finger Kit Kat.

02:28:08.012 --> 02:28:10.047
This one has an actual
layer of caramel in it,

02:28:10.047 --> 02:28:12.083
which is kind of what I was
expecting from these ones.

02:28:12.083 --> 02:28:12.917
But this one's good.

02:28:12.917 --> 02:28:15.319
Next up we have the Kit
Kat chunky white chocolate.

02:28:15.319 --> 02:28:17.622
And while I couldn't find
the individual bars today,

02:28:17.622 --> 02:28:20.825
you can also get a Lotus
Biscoff Kit Kat chunky.

02:28:20.825 --> 02:28:23.127
I was able to find this
in the form of bites,

02:28:23.127 --> 02:28:24.295
so I'll give one of these a try

02:28:24.295 --> 02:28:25.730
and give my thoughts on the flavor.

02:28:28.132 --> 02:28:30.234
I think because you get the
balance of the chocolate

02:28:30.234 --> 02:28:33.738
and a little bit of biscuit
in with the Biscoff flavoring,

02:28:33.738 --> 02:28:35.539
it's not that bad. It's not overwhelming.

02:28:35.539 --> 02:28:38.776
Is it enough to convince
me to start liking Biscoff?

02:28:38.776 --> 02:28:40.878
Probably not. But not bad.

02:28:40.878 --> 02:28:43.481
Also, you can get Kit Kat sundae cones

02:28:43.481 --> 02:28:45.950
and Kit Kat ice cream.

02:28:45.950 --> 02:28:46.918
We have no freezer.

02:28:46.918 --> 02:28:48.619
I didn't want them melting in the studio.

02:28:48.619 --> 02:28:50.721
We actually do have Kit
Kat ice cream in the UK.

02:28:50.721 --> 02:28:53.658
I was able to find some in
a Food Warehouse by Iceland.

02:28:53.658 --> 02:28:54.659
However, I didn't buy them

02:28:54.659 --> 02:28:57.261
because I wasn't going somewhere
with a freezer afterwards,

02:28:57.261 --> 02:28:59.864
so would've been melty
and a bit of a disaster.

02:28:59.864 --> 02:29:02.533
Here's what they do look like
if you do find them in the UK.

02:29:02.533 --> 02:29:04.769
In the UK, Kit Kat offers a
range of seasonal products

02:29:04.769 --> 02:29:06.237
depending on which season you're in.

02:29:06.237 --> 02:29:08.539
We're filming this in April,
so we've just had Easter,

02:29:08.539 --> 02:29:11.142
and they had these adorable
little Kit Kat bunnies on offer.

02:29:11.142 --> 02:29:13.311
These came either as a single one

02:29:13.311 --> 02:29:15.579
or as a little multipack.

02:29:15.579 --> 02:29:18.749
Slightly worryingly, I was able
to find a Christmas Kit Kat

02:29:18.749 --> 02:29:21.852
in one of the corner shops that I visited.

02:29:21.852 --> 02:29:23.888
Apparently, these are fine
until September this year,

02:29:23.888 --> 02:29:25.256
so we're fine.

02:29:25.256 --> 02:29:27.358
That's quite cute, actually.

02:29:27.358 --> 02:29:28.993
It's quite a nice little design.

02:29:28.993 --> 02:29:31.729
The final exclusive I was able
to track down is a fun one.

02:29:31.729 --> 02:29:33.664
It's Kit Kat breakfast cereal.

02:29:33.664 --> 02:29:35.433
As the packaging suggests, it's new.

02:29:35.433 --> 02:29:37.635
I don't think it's in every
supermarket or shop yet.

02:29:37.635 --> 02:29:40.137
I had to go to a Waitrose to find this.

02:29:40.137 --> 02:29:43.607
They look like little tiny cereal pillows.

02:29:46.544 --> 02:29:48.145
I know this is not the fairest

02:29:48.145 --> 02:29:50.047
and most accurate way to test cereal,

02:29:51.415 --> 02:29:52.750
but they're pretty good.

02:29:52.750 --> 02:29:55.886
I was actually able to find
two of your US exclusives, Joe.

02:29:55.886 --> 02:29:58.990
I have the Kit Kat birthday cake

02:29:58.990 --> 02:30:00.825
and the duos mocha and white chocolate.

02:30:00.825 --> 02:30:01.892
As many Brits will know,

02:30:01.892 --> 02:30:05.062
our high streets are plagued
by American candy stores,

02:30:05.062 --> 02:30:06.464
which are these bizarre shops

02:30:06.464 --> 02:30:09.333
which import American
snacks and chocolates

02:30:09.333 --> 02:30:10.968
and play really loud music

02:30:10.968 --> 02:30:14.038
and I'm pretty sure are a
front for something or other,

02:30:14.038 --> 02:30:17.108
but I was finally able to benefit
from them by buying these.

02:30:17.108 --> 02:30:18.709
This does have all of those

02:30:18.709 --> 02:30:20.277
lovely, forbidden food colorings

02:30:20.277 --> 02:30:21.812
that we don't usually get in the UK.

02:30:21.812 --> 02:30:24.882
So if I'm really hyperactive
after this, we'll know why.

02:30:24.882 --> 02:30:26.117
That is colorful.

02:30:31.489 --> 02:30:32.723
Yeah, that's pretty sweet.

02:30:32.723 --> 02:30:33.591
[clears throat]

02:30:33.591 --> 02:30:35.426
You guys don't hold back
on the sugar, do you?

02:30:35.426 --> 02:30:37.228
Yeah, that's, that's excessive.

02:30:37.228 --> 02:30:39.130
That's too much, guys. Chill out.

02:30:39.130 --> 02:30:40.698
After the birthday cake,

02:30:40.698 --> 02:30:43.134
I'm hoping for something
slightly more savory.

02:30:45.703 --> 02:30:46.904
Pretty strong coffee flavor.

02:30:46.904 --> 02:30:48.939
Yeah, this one's fine. I like this.

02:30:51.208 --> 02:30:54.278
A US Kit Kat bar is 210 calories.

02:30:54.278 --> 02:30:57.281
It's 11 grams of fat, 7
grams of saturated fat,

02:30:57.281 --> 02:31:00.251
20 milligrams of sodium,
28 grams of carbs,

02:31:00.251 --> 02:31:03.788
23 grams of sugar, and 2 grams of protein.

02:31:03.788 --> 02:31:06.323
In the UK, a standard Kit Kat
bar contains the following:

02:31:06.323 --> 02:31:08.726
209 calories, 10.2 grams of fat,

02:31:08.726 --> 02:31:11.062
of which 5.6 grams are saturated,

02:31:11.062 --> 02:31:14.131
40 milligrams of sodium,
26.1 grams of carbs,

02:31:14.131 --> 02:31:16.367
of which 21.3 grams are sugars,

02:31:16.367 --> 02:31:18.069
and 2.8 grams of protein.

02:31:18.069 --> 02:31:20.671
That's less in every category
other than protein and sodium,

02:31:20.671 --> 02:31:22.940
where for some reason we
have double the US figure.

02:31:22.940 --> 02:31:26.410
Our most calorific Kit
Kat is the Kit Kat XL.

02:31:26.410 --> 02:31:29.780
It contains a total of 640 calories.

02:31:29.780 --> 02:31:31.449
In the UK, our most calorific item

02:31:31.449 --> 02:31:33.284
is a peanut butter Kit Kat chunky.

02:31:33.284 --> 02:31:35.386
One of these contains 226 calories,

02:31:35.386 --> 02:31:38.289
which is still less than
half of the US Kit Kat XL.

02:31:40.458 --> 02:31:42.493
While Kit Kats are now
beloved all around the world,

02:31:42.493 --> 02:31:43.894
they were invented in the UK.

02:31:43.894 --> 02:31:45.629
The first modern Kit Kat bar was created

02:31:45.629 --> 02:31:48.265
by the Rowntree company back in 1935,

02:31:48.265 --> 02:31:50.668
although then it was
called a chocolate crisp.

02:31:50.668 --> 02:31:52.236
It wasn't until 1937

02:31:52.236 --> 02:31:53.671
that they first used the name Kit Kat,

02:31:53.671 --> 02:31:55.906
renaming it to the Kit
Kat chocolate crisp.

02:31:55.906 --> 02:31:57.975
The bar exploded in popularity, so much so

02:31:57.975 --> 02:32:00.544
that it even survived rationing
during the Second World War.

02:32:00.544 --> 02:32:01.679
Despite milk shortages,

02:32:01.679 --> 02:32:03.380
rather than halting production completely,

02:32:03.380 --> 02:32:04.715
the Rowntrees changed the recipe

02:32:04.715 --> 02:32:06.083
to use plain chocolate instead.

02:32:06.083 --> 02:32:08.285
So as not to confuse
customers with the new taste,

02:32:08.285 --> 02:32:10.955
they changed the packaging
to a blue wartime color.

02:32:10.955 --> 02:32:12.556
After the war, when rationing was lifted

02:32:12.556 --> 02:32:13.891
and normal production resumed,

02:32:13.891 --> 02:32:15.526
they adopted the iconic red color

02:32:15.526 --> 02:32:16.594
that we know and love today.

02:32:16.594 --> 02:32:18.496
The popularity of Kit
Kat continued to grow,

02:32:18.496 --> 02:32:20.397
and they were exported all over the world.

02:32:20.397 --> 02:32:22.500
In the 1970s, Rowntree gave Hershey

02:32:22.500 --> 02:32:25.436
a license to manufacture and
distribute Kit Kats in the US.

02:32:25.436 --> 02:32:26.837
This agreement remained in place

02:32:26.837 --> 02:32:29.874
even after Nestlé
acquired Rowntree in 1988.

02:32:29.874 --> 02:32:31.876
The popularity of Kit Kat
has actually turned out to be

02:32:31.876 --> 02:32:33.811
something of a double-edged
sword for Hershey.

02:32:33.811 --> 02:32:35.246
As part of their deal with Rowntree,

02:32:35.246 --> 02:32:36.614
if the company is ever sold,

02:32:36.614 --> 02:32:39.150
they lose their license to
manufacture and produce Kit Kat.

02:32:39.150 --> 02:32:40.885
Kit Kat is the single most popular product

02:32:40.885 --> 02:32:42.586
sold by Hershey in the US,

02:32:42.586 --> 02:32:44.421
so it makes it much
harder to sell the company

02:32:44.421 --> 02:32:45.956
should they ever want to.

02:32:45.956 --> 02:32:47.458
My kingdom for a Kit Kat.

02:32:49.660 --> 02:32:52.229
In the US, a Kit Kat is made up of sugar,

02:32:52.229 --> 02:32:54.765
wheat flour, cocoa butter, nonfat milk,

02:32:54.765 --> 02:32:57.601
chocolate, refined palm kernel oil,

02:32:57.601 --> 02:32:59.737
lactose (milk), milk fat,

02:32:59.737 --> 02:33:03.140
and contains 2% or less of soy lecithin,

02:33:03.140 --> 02:33:05.476
PGPR, which is an emulsifier,

02:33:05.476 --> 02:33:07.111
yeast, artificial flavor,

02:33:07.111 --> 02:33:10.214
salt, and sodium bicarbonate.

02:33:10.214 --> 02:33:12.383
A UK Kit Kat has the
following ingredients:

02:33:12.383 --> 02:33:13.851
sugar, wheat flour,

02:33:13.851 --> 02:33:17.421
which contains calcium,
iron, thiamine, and niacin,

02:33:17.421 --> 02:33:19.557
milk powders (whole and skimmed),

02:33:19.557 --> 02:33:22.760
cocoa mass, cocoa butter, vegetable fats,

02:33:22.760 --> 02:33:26.197
lactose and proteins
from whey, whey powder,

02:33:26.197 --> 02:33:29.099
emulsifier sunflower lecithin, yeast,

02:33:29.099 --> 02:33:31.202
raising agent sodium bicarbonate,

02:33:31.202 --> 02:33:33.404
butterfat, and natural flavorings.

02:33:33.404 --> 02:33:34.538
If you've seen the Snickers episode,

02:33:34.538 --> 02:33:35.639
you might remember that in the UK,

02:33:35.639 --> 02:33:37.708
we tend to feel our chocolate
is of a higher quality

02:33:37.708 --> 02:33:39.076
than that found in the US.

02:33:39.076 --> 02:33:41.078
It's generally a bit
richer and a bit smoother.

02:33:41.078 --> 02:33:43.514
The reason for this is a
higher cocoa and fat content

02:33:43.514 --> 02:33:44.648
found in our chocolate.

02:33:44.648 --> 02:33:45.983
According to UK rules,

02:33:45.983 --> 02:33:50.020
chocolate must contain no
less than 25% cocoa solids

02:33:50.020 --> 02:33:51.555
to be considered milk chocolate.

02:33:51.555 --> 02:33:53.390
The milk used in each
country's Kit Kat production

02:33:53.390 --> 02:33:54.592
also differs slightly.

02:33:54.592 --> 02:33:56.961
In the UK, Nestlé uses milk crumb,

02:33:56.961 --> 02:33:59.964
which is a dehydrated, slightly
sweetened milk product.

02:33:59.964 --> 02:34:02.933
In the US, Hershey uses
nonfat milk and milk fat.

02:34:02.933 --> 02:34:04.134
And in the US, the rules

02:34:04.134 --> 02:34:05.736
are our milk chocolate must contain

02:34:05.736 --> 02:34:08.305
no less than 10% of chocolate liquor,

02:34:08.305 --> 02:34:09.873
which is roughly equal part mix

02:34:09.873 --> 02:34:12.009
of cocoa solids and cocoa butter.

02:34:12.009 --> 02:34:14.678
Unlike most US chocolates,
like Snickers for instance,

02:34:14.678 --> 02:34:16.914
our Kit Kats do contain sugar

02:34:16.914 --> 02:34:19.016
and not high-fructose corn syrup.

02:34:19.016 --> 02:34:20.050
Really?

02:34:22.119 --> 02:34:23.087
Yeah.

02:34:23.087 --> 02:34:24.488
It's worth pointing out that in the UK,

02:34:24.488 --> 02:34:25.789
Kit Kats are made by Nestlé,

02:34:25.789 --> 02:34:27.658
while in the US they're made by Hershey.

02:34:27.658 --> 02:34:29.226
Furthermore, in 2015,

02:34:29.226 --> 02:34:32.229
Hershey did a deal with
Let's Buy British Imports

02:34:32.229 --> 02:34:35.833
to stop importing all Cadbury's
chocolate made overseas,

02:34:35.833 --> 02:34:38.402
and in the same deal
agreed to halt imports

02:34:38.402 --> 02:34:41.472
of so many British
chocolates, like Kit Kat.

02:34:41.472 --> 02:34:43.240
Also, and this can be for another episode,

02:34:43.240 --> 02:34:46.176
the license agreement allows
Hershey to make, for example,

02:34:46.176 --> 02:34:47.945
Cadbury chocolate in the US

02:34:47.945 --> 02:34:50.547
with the same packaging as in the UK,

02:34:50.547 --> 02:34:52.349
but with a different recipe.

02:34:52.349 --> 02:34:53.384
Ooh.

02:34:53.384 --> 02:34:55.019
Harry: From calorie
count to portion sizes,

02:34:55.019 --> 02:34:56.420
we wanted to find out all the differences

02:34:56.420 --> 02:34:59.123
between Costco food in the US and the UK.

02:34:59.123 --> 02:35:00.424
This is "Food Wars."

02:35:02.493 --> 02:35:04.762
Here is an iconic Costco
hot dog in the UK.

02:35:04.762 --> 02:35:05.596
Ah, yes.

02:35:05.596 --> 02:35:08.165
The famous Costco hot dog.

02:35:08.165 --> 02:35:11.902
In the UK, the length of
a hot dog is 8 inches.

02:35:11.902 --> 02:35:12.903
Don't laugh.

02:35:14.204 --> 02:35:15.372
Joe: 8 inches.

02:35:15.372 --> 02:35:16.874
Almost exactly 8-inch dog.

02:35:16.874 --> 02:35:18.942
It's also advertised as a
quarter-pounder hot dog.

02:35:18.942 --> 02:35:19.877
Let's see if that's true.

02:35:20.911 --> 02:35:22.279
So, with the bun and some onions,

02:35:22.279 --> 02:35:24.348
the whole thing weighs 250 grams.

02:35:24.348 --> 02:35:26.183
I want to take the sausage
out and weigh that on its own

02:35:26.183 --> 02:35:27.951
to see if that is a quarter pounder.

02:35:27.951 --> 02:35:29.420
Turns out that without
the bun and the toppings,

02:35:29.420 --> 02:35:31.488
it does weigh exactly
a quarter of a pound.

02:35:31.488 --> 02:35:32.389
That's pretty impressive.

02:35:32.389 --> 02:35:34.625
I know it's manufactured
and mass-made by machines,

02:35:34.625 --> 02:35:36.694
but, you know, still cool.

02:35:36.694 --> 02:35:39.029
Oh, my God.

02:35:39.029 --> 02:35:41.398
It's exactly 4 ounces.

02:35:41.398 --> 02:35:42.499
Wow!

02:35:42.499 --> 02:35:43.600
They kept it a quarter pound

02:35:43.600 --> 02:35:44.568
after it's cooked and everything.

02:35:44.568 --> 02:35:45.402
See?

02:35:45.402 --> 02:35:47.638
Costco. It's not impossible.

02:35:47.638 --> 02:35:49.239
All these people watch
this and they're like,

02:35:49.239 --> 02:35:51.475
"Mm, it's a quarter of a
pound before you cook it."

02:35:51.475 --> 02:35:53.243
Well, they said 4 ounces.

02:35:53.243 --> 02:35:55.446
Whatever they're doing, after it's cooked,

02:35:55.446 --> 02:35:57.881
it is the advertised 4 ounces.

02:35:57.881 --> 02:35:59.083
Way to go, Costco.

02:35:59.083 --> 02:36:03.253
In the UK, a Costco pizza
is 17 inches in diameter.

02:36:03.253 --> 02:36:06.156
That makes the surface
area 227 square inches.

02:36:06.156 --> 02:36:09.059
In the US, our Costco pizza should also be

02:36:09.059 --> 02:36:11.428
18 inches in diameter.

02:36:11.428 --> 02:36:14.131
Let's measure it!

02:36:14.131 --> 02:36:16.667
More like 17 ½, Costco.

02:36:16.667 --> 02:36:19.036
It's still $9.99.

02:36:19.036 --> 02:36:20.671
That's a ridiculous deal.

02:36:20.671 --> 02:36:22.639
You can keep that half an inch.

02:36:22.639 --> 02:36:24.541
Our pizza today was cut into six pieces.

02:36:24.541 --> 02:36:26.076
I'd say for a pizza of this size,

02:36:26.076 --> 02:36:27.978
it's kind of uncommon
to see only six slices.

02:36:27.978 --> 02:36:29.780
I would expect maybe eight
or 10, like at Domino's.

02:36:29.780 --> 02:36:31.014
But we're going to weigh one slice

02:36:31.014 --> 02:36:32.015
and find out how big it is.

02:36:32.015 --> 02:36:34.284
Now let's weigh one slice.

02:36:37.621 --> 02:36:39.456
That is a dense slice of pizza.

02:36:39.456 --> 02:36:40.758
There's some citation needed,

02:36:40.758 --> 02:36:42.860
but this might be the
heaviest slice of pizza

02:36:42.860 --> 02:36:44.928
we've ever weighed on "Food Wars."

02:36:44.928 --> 02:36:49.099
That's a big layer of cheese.
Not a ton of tomato sauce.

02:36:49.099 --> 02:36:52.903
I would say it's maybe 70% bread.

02:36:52.903 --> 02:36:55.305
So I don't know if you're
getting a ton of value for money

02:36:55.305 --> 02:36:56.607
when it comes to toppings.

02:36:57.941 --> 02:36:59.910
I quite like it.

02:36:59.910 --> 02:37:03.180
It's got that nostalgic,
cheap-frozen-pizza quality.

02:37:03.180 --> 02:37:05.249
The chicken bake.

02:37:05.249 --> 02:37:06.784
I don't know what the origin of this is,

02:37:06.784 --> 02:37:08.552
but it's a pretty good idea.

02:37:08.552 --> 02:37:11.054
It's just, like, a giant
chicken Hot Pocket, right?

02:37:14.858 --> 02:37:16.660
The guy holding up the
fish that he's just caught.

02:37:16.660 --> 02:37:18.395
We've already used this
gag in a recent episode,

02:37:18.395 --> 02:37:19.463
but we can reuse it.

02:37:21.932 --> 02:37:23.233
I am curious.

02:37:26.236 --> 02:37:27.337
Oh, why is this so good?

02:37:27.337 --> 02:37:28.605
This is so good.

02:37:28.605 --> 02:37:31.275
I will say, I love stodgy food.

02:37:32.309 --> 02:37:33.977
So I feel like I am the target audience

02:37:33.977 --> 02:37:35.012
for all of these foods.

02:37:35.012 --> 02:37:36.847
The fountain drinks in
the UK come in one size,

02:37:36.847 --> 02:37:38.982
and it's supposedly 22 fluid ounces.

02:37:38.982 --> 02:37:40.083
Of course, we have to check it.

02:37:42.619 --> 02:37:44.221
So, in what seems to be an increasingly

02:37:44.221 --> 02:37:45.556
rare occurrence on "Food Wars,"

02:37:45.556 --> 02:37:47.558
that is actually as much
drink as we were promised.

02:37:47.558 --> 02:37:48.725
That's 22 ounces.

02:37:48.725 --> 02:37:52.095
But the fountain drinks in
the US are 20 fluid ounces.

02:37:54.998 --> 02:37:56.266
Look at that. It's exactly 20 ounces.

02:37:56.266 --> 02:37:57.868
And I filled it up at the thing.

02:37:57.868 --> 02:38:02.439
Man, Costco is razor-sharp
with the portions, right?

02:38:02.439 --> 02:38:04.608
They're not leaving anything to chance.

02:38:04.608 --> 02:38:06.176
Thank you, Costco.

02:38:08.679 --> 02:38:10.547
Here are all the Costco
menu items in the UK

02:38:10.547 --> 02:38:11.915
that you won't find in the US.

02:38:11.915 --> 02:38:14.351
Here are all the Costco
menu items in the US

02:38:14.351 --> 02:38:16.119
you won't find in the UK.

02:38:16.119 --> 02:38:18.255
Quick disclaimer that the
menus seem to vary slightly

02:38:18.255 --> 02:38:20.357
depending on where you
are in the UK or the US.

02:38:20.357 --> 02:38:21.992
I got these from the Chingford location

02:38:21.992 --> 02:38:23.093
just outside of London,

02:38:23.093 --> 02:38:25.896
and Joe's got his from the
Burbank location in California.

02:38:25.896 --> 02:38:28.198
We have one exclusive pizza
option in the UK from Costco,

02:38:28.198 --> 02:38:30.000
and it's this one, the
barbecue chicken pizza.

02:38:30.000 --> 02:38:32.069
As the name suggests, it's
a barbecue chicken pizza,

02:38:32.069 --> 02:38:33.837
which also comes with
some green bell peppers

02:38:33.837 --> 02:38:35.172
and some red onion.

02:38:35.172 --> 02:38:36.740
When I see a barbecue pizza in the UK,

02:38:36.740 --> 02:38:39.076
I usually grimace because it tends to mean

02:38:39.076 --> 02:38:41.478
that the sauce is barbecue,
and I don't like that.

02:38:41.478 --> 02:38:43.580
But I think here, they've
actually just kept

02:38:43.580 --> 02:38:45.649
the same cheese and tomato base

02:38:45.649 --> 02:38:47.084
but added the barbecue toppings on top,

02:38:47.084 --> 02:38:49.319
which in my opinion is what
a barbecue pizza should be.

02:38:51.421 --> 02:38:52.723
Leon does not agree.

02:38:52.723 --> 02:38:54.758
It still feels pretty hefty.

02:38:54.758 --> 02:38:56.593
Maybe not quite as dense or as hefty

02:38:56.593 --> 02:38:57.895
as the cheese pizza did.

02:38:57.895 --> 02:39:00.497
The dough seems to be not quite as thick.

02:39:00.497 --> 02:39:02.599
Try just the chicken on its own first.

02:39:02.599 --> 02:39:03.534
It's not bad. I'm not getting much

02:39:03.534 --> 02:39:05.335
barbecue flavor from that.

02:39:05.335 --> 02:39:07.137
It's more just like a
sort of grilled chicken.

02:39:09.273 --> 02:39:11.508
Usually my biggest
complaint of barbecue pizzas

02:39:11.508 --> 02:39:13.110
is that they're too barbecuey,

02:39:13.110 --> 02:39:15.546
whereas this one actually
isn't very barbecuey at all.

02:39:15.546 --> 02:39:16.547
That means that I like it.

02:39:16.547 --> 02:39:18.048
But if you do normally like quite a strong

02:39:18.048 --> 02:39:20.117
barbecue-sauce flavor from your pizzas,

02:39:20.117 --> 02:39:21.485
this one might not be enough for you.

02:39:21.485 --> 02:39:23.086
In the UK, you can also get whole pizzas

02:39:23.086 --> 02:39:24.588
as part of a family bundle.

02:39:24.588 --> 02:39:26.590
The bundles come with a full-size pizza,

02:39:26.590 --> 02:39:29.626
one of these gigantic garlic breads,

02:39:29.626 --> 02:39:31.962
two of these garlic-and-herb dips,

02:39:31.962 --> 02:39:34.398
and also a 2-liter bottle of Pepsi Max,

02:39:34.398 --> 02:39:37.301
half of which I have spilled
on the floor of the studio.

02:39:37.301 --> 02:39:38.869
Twisted churro.

02:39:38.869 --> 02:39:40.637
We got these, you guys don't.

02:39:40.637 --> 02:39:42.172
It's not a lot of stuff. All right.

02:39:42.172 --> 02:39:44.608
This thing, churro, cinnamon, dough.

02:39:46.476 --> 02:39:48.445
Mm.

02:39:48.445 --> 02:39:51.748
Next up we've got Costco's
take on a classic British dish,

02:39:51.748 --> 02:39:52.749
cottage pie.

02:39:52.749 --> 02:39:55.285
Now, our American viewers may
have heard of shepherd's pie.

02:39:55.285 --> 02:39:57.321
Cottage pie is basically the same thing

02:39:57.321 --> 02:40:00.357
in that it's a layer of
some cheese on top, usually,

02:40:00.357 --> 02:40:01.992
some mashed potato,

02:40:01.992 --> 02:40:04.761
but instead of the lamb-mince mixture,

02:40:04.761 --> 02:40:06.597
cottage pie contains beef mince.

02:40:06.597 --> 02:40:08.065
Now, this is a classic British dish,

02:40:08.065 --> 02:40:11.468
and we do feel pretty passionately
about things like this.

02:40:11.468 --> 02:40:14.004
So let's hope Costco have done it justice.

02:40:14.004 --> 02:40:18.008
The strategy seems to be
sell large quantities of food

02:40:18.008 --> 02:40:20.811
but really pack it with
the kind of cheap stuff.

02:40:20.811 --> 02:40:22.279
So, for example, there's a small amount

02:40:22.279 --> 02:40:23.914
of cheese on top here,

02:40:23.914 --> 02:40:27.117
a very small amount of beef on the bottom,

02:40:27.117 --> 02:40:30.387
and I'd say, like, 80% of
this is just mashed potato.

02:40:30.387 --> 02:40:31.555
Let's give it a try.

02:40:33.056 --> 02:40:34.625
It's actually quite tasty.

02:40:40.030 --> 02:40:41.798
I don't work for Costco, I just,

02:40:41.798 --> 02:40:43.066
I'm a truth seeker.

02:40:43.066 --> 02:40:44.534
Again, the beef is, like,

02:40:44.534 --> 02:40:46.937
it's very rich, it's quite thick,

02:40:46.937 --> 02:40:49.039
but there's a real meaty flavor to that.

02:40:49.039 --> 02:40:51.441
Is it the best cottage
pie you've ever had?

02:40:51.441 --> 02:40:52.709
No, probably not.

02:40:52.709 --> 02:40:56.446
But is it an affordable, filling version

02:40:56.446 --> 02:40:59.449
that's fairly true to the original?

02:40:59.449 --> 02:41:00.817
I'd have to kind of say yeah.

02:41:00.817 --> 02:41:01.818
You do get kind of more filling

02:41:01.818 --> 02:41:02.753
as you go into the middle as well.

02:41:02.753 --> 02:41:04.821
It wasn't all like that, thankfully.

02:41:04.821 --> 02:41:05.722
Yeah, I don't know.

02:41:05.722 --> 02:41:08.125
I actually don't think they've
done too bad a job here.

02:41:08.125 --> 02:41:08.992
Next up we have this one,

02:41:08.992 --> 02:41:11.161
which is the double
chicken fillet sandwich.

02:41:11.161 --> 02:41:14.398
Considering the theme of just hefty foods,

02:41:14.398 --> 02:41:17.134
this thing is absolutely massive.

02:41:17.134 --> 02:41:18.001
Look at it!

02:41:18.001 --> 02:41:19.603
Yeah, I think maybe they were supposed to

02:41:19.603 --> 02:41:21.872
stack the chicken patties

02:41:21.872 --> 02:41:23.140
instead of laying them side by side,

02:41:23.140 --> 02:41:24.975
'cause the bun barely covers any of it.

02:41:24.975 --> 02:41:26.843
They've also only put one
slice of cheese on it,

02:41:26.843 --> 02:41:29.880
so only about 40% of it
is covered in cheese.

02:41:29.880 --> 02:41:32.449
I might have to do some quick
tactical rearrangement here.

02:41:32.449 --> 02:41:33.617
Oh, there's maybe ...

02:41:33.617 --> 02:41:35.385
oh, there's another bit
of cheese on the bottom,

02:41:35.385 --> 02:41:37.054
so you get cheese.

02:41:37.054 --> 02:41:37.854
Oh, God.

02:41:37.854 --> 02:41:39.322
But then it's like, can you eat this?

02:41:39.322 --> 02:41:41.958
Because that is also a
logistical nightmare to eat.

02:41:41.958 --> 02:41:43.627
I think whichever way you stack this,

02:41:43.627 --> 02:41:45.395
it's going to be quite tricky to eat.

02:41:45.395 --> 02:41:47.698
But this is the double
chicken fillet sandwich.

02:41:47.698 --> 02:41:50.734
There are two chicken
fillets, two slices of cheese,

02:41:50.734 --> 02:41:52.669
some lettuce, and some tomato.

02:41:55.539 --> 02:41:57.541
Extremely dry.

02:41:57.541 --> 02:41:58.909
Very bland.

02:41:58.909 --> 02:42:02.479
Like, none of the components
taste of anything, somehow.

02:42:02.479 --> 02:42:03.313
It's a bit of a miss.

02:42:03.313 --> 02:42:07.350
Again, it's like, it's
big. It would fill you up.

02:42:07.350 --> 02:42:09.720
Next up we have the
Korean barbecue beef bake.

02:42:09.720 --> 02:42:10.620
So it's like the chicken bake

02:42:10.620 --> 02:42:11.922
in that it's kind of a baguette

02:42:11.922 --> 02:42:13.890
with some cheese on top filled with meat,

02:42:13.890 --> 02:42:15.125
but instead of chicken and bacon,

02:42:15.125 --> 02:42:17.427
this one has Korean barbecue beef.

02:42:17.427 --> 02:42:20.163
I imagine it's going to be a
similar level of stodginess

02:42:20.163 --> 02:42:22.699
to the chicken bake and
also to everything else

02:42:22.699 --> 02:42:23.900
that we've eaten today.

02:42:23.900 --> 02:42:25.969
The filling on its own
doesn't really taste of much,

02:42:25.969 --> 02:42:28.071
which is slightly disappointing.

02:42:29.639 --> 02:42:31.575
That's bland. That's disappointing.

02:42:31.575 --> 02:42:34.311
I'm still eating it, but it's bland.

02:42:34.311 --> 02:42:37.047
It's just, like, nothing
that jumps out to me

02:42:37.047 --> 02:42:39.216
as Korean flavors in this.

02:42:39.216 --> 02:42:40.550
If you're going to make
something that bland,

02:42:40.550 --> 02:42:42.152
I think don't drag Korea through the mud,

02:42:42.152 --> 02:42:44.254
just call it a beef bake
and be done with it.

02:42:44.254 --> 02:42:45.589
There's one other classic British dish

02:42:45.589 --> 02:42:46.656
on the UK Costco menu,

02:42:46.656 --> 02:42:48.258
which unfortunately they
forgot to give me today,

02:42:48.258 --> 02:42:49.559
and it's jacket potatoes.

02:42:49.559 --> 02:42:50.827
There's a note in the
script where Joe says

02:42:50.827 --> 02:42:52.129
that he doesn't know
what a jacket potato is,

02:42:52.129 --> 02:42:54.164
so I'll do my best to just
explain it to you now.

02:42:54.164 --> 02:42:56.299
As the name suggests, it's
basically just a potato

02:42:56.299 --> 02:42:58.735
that you keep in your jacket
in case you get hungry.

02:42:58.735 --> 02:43:00.170
These can either be boiled or baked.

02:43:00.170 --> 02:43:01.571
You'll usually wrap it in some foil

02:43:01.571 --> 02:43:03.140
just so that it doesn't
kind of touch anything else

02:43:03.140 --> 02:43:04.141
that's in your pocket.

02:43:04.141 --> 02:43:05.642
Keep it on you, and then
whenever you get hungry

02:43:05.642 --> 02:43:07.577
during the day, you have
a nice snack with you.

02:43:07.577 --> 02:43:08.478
As the name suggests,

02:43:08.478 --> 02:43:11.248
it's basically a potato that
you keep in your jacket.

02:43:11.248 --> 02:43:13.650
[crew laughing]

02:43:13.650 --> 02:43:16.319
We also have two exclusive
dessert style options in the UK,

02:43:16.319 --> 02:43:18.388
including a caramel fudge sundae

02:43:18.388 --> 02:43:19.956
and a coffee caramel frappé.

02:43:19.956 --> 02:43:21.258
I didn't get either of them today,

02:43:21.258 --> 02:43:23.360
but here's what they look like.

02:43:23.360 --> 02:43:25.662
Ahem.

02:43:25.662 --> 02:43:30.534
Two cold drinks you can
get here in the US Costco

02:43:30.534 --> 02:43:31.968
is the fruit smoothie.

02:43:35.172 --> 02:43:37.407
Oh, my God, that's great.

02:43:37.407 --> 02:43:39.376
Mm!

02:43:39.376 --> 02:43:40.977
Wow, that's really good.

02:43:40.977 --> 02:43:43.980
And the cold brew mocha freeze.

02:43:45.182 --> 02:43:47.450
Oh, boy, that's melted.

02:43:47.450 --> 02:43:48.952
I'm really surprised how
good these cold drinks are.

02:43:48.952 --> 02:43:51.621
I mean, their food is good,
but these are really good.

02:43:52.956 --> 02:43:54.624
Mm.

02:43:54.624 --> 02:43:55.659
Yeah, that's picking me up.

02:43:55.659 --> 02:43:57.727
That's picking me up, Yuels!

02:43:57.727 --> 02:43:58.962
Let's go!

02:44:00.330 --> 02:44:01.331
Ah!

02:44:01.331 --> 02:44:04.634
Now I need to calm down a little bit.

02:44:04.634 --> 02:44:05.569
And finally in the UK,

02:44:05.569 --> 02:44:07.204
we also have mango smoothies on the menu,

02:44:07.204 --> 02:44:08.738
although today their machine was broken.

02:44:08.738 --> 02:44:09.673
They weren't serving them.

02:44:09.673 --> 02:44:11.408
Here's what they look like.

02:44:11.408 --> 02:44:13.276
Want to take this moment
to talk about Kirkland,

02:44:13.276 --> 02:44:15.178
Costco's signature brand that provides

02:44:15.178 --> 02:44:18.181
a wide variety of products for a low cost.

02:44:18.181 --> 02:44:20.750
Over the years, the brand has
developed a loyal fan base

02:44:20.750 --> 02:44:22.185
among Costco members.

02:44:22.185 --> 02:44:26.022
It would be impossible to
feature all the Kirkland

02:44:26.022 --> 02:44:29.559
food and beverage items exclusive
to the US not in the UK.

02:44:29.559 --> 02:44:32.729
And believe me, I begged management

02:44:32.729 --> 02:44:36.967
to let me sample Kirkland's
many alcohol options,

02:44:36.967 --> 02:44:39.903
to which they said, "No way."

02:44:39.903 --> 02:44:43.940
So here are a few non-alcohol
Kirkland signature

02:44:43.940 --> 02:44:46.509
favorite exclusives in the US.

02:44:46.509 --> 02:44:48.478
Going to start here: animal crackers.

02:44:48.478 --> 02:44:50.914
I mean, come on, UK.

02:44:50.914 --> 02:44:52.949
Who doesn't love animal crackers?

02:44:52.949 --> 02:44:55.185
Are animal crackers popular
in the United Kingdom?

02:44:55.185 --> 02:44:56.953
Oh, my God, let's do the animal review.

02:44:56.953 --> 02:44:59.489
I think monkey. Gorilla?

02:44:59.489 --> 02:45:00.690
Orangutan?

02:45:00.690 --> 02:45:02.859
This looks like a hippo.

02:45:02.859 --> 02:45:04.394
We got hippo.

02:45:04.394 --> 02:45:06.897
Oh, this is most certainly a koala.

02:45:06.897 --> 02:45:08.265
I've seen that guy already.

02:45:08.265 --> 02:45:09.699
We're already getting repeats.

02:45:09.699 --> 02:45:10.967
Alligator, I think.

02:45:10.967 --> 02:45:12.569
Possibly a dragon.

02:45:12.569 --> 02:45:15.505
A Brookfield Zoo all
on your fingertips here

02:45:15.505 --> 02:45:17.240
in cracker form. Fantastic.

02:45:17.240 --> 02:45:21.478
And the US is not playing
with their cheese selection.

02:45:21.478 --> 02:45:22.379
So many.

02:45:22.379 --> 02:45:24.047
And the one according to the internet

02:45:24.047 --> 02:45:25.949
that just everyone is raving about

02:45:25.949 --> 02:45:29.920
is, of course, the Parmigiano-Reggiano.

02:45:29.920 --> 02:45:32.689
Parmigiano-Reggiano.

02:45:32.689 --> 02:45:33.990
1 ½ pounds.

02:45:33.990 --> 02:45:36.626
How much do you think a 1 ½-pound

02:45:36.626 --> 02:45:40.330
block of Parmigiano-Reggiano costs?

02:45:40.330 --> 02:45:41.298
Go.

02:45:43.466 --> 02:45:44.434
What do you think?

02:45:46.403 --> 02:45:47.804
Actually, it was $16.

02:45:47.804 --> 02:45:49.940
Jeez, both of you.

02:45:49.940 --> 02:45:51.808
I thought everyone was
going to be like, "$50!"

02:45:51.808 --> 02:45:53.877
No, $16. That's still really good.

02:45:53.877 --> 02:45:55.578
16 bucks for all this?

02:45:55.578 --> 02:45:56.846
I mean, this is going to last, man.

02:45:56.846 --> 02:46:01.851
This will last many of your
wine and cheese parties.

02:46:01.851 --> 02:46:05.021
And, of course, Costco has a
fantastic selection of wine,

02:46:05.021 --> 02:46:07.090
all of which I'm not allowed
to go near, apparently.

02:46:07.090 --> 02:46:09.492
According to management.

02:46:09.492 --> 02:46:12.128
All right? This video would
be a lot more entertaining

02:46:12.128 --> 02:46:14.064
if we were doing the wine review.

02:46:14.064 --> 02:46:16.132
Peanut butter, peanut
butter, peanut butter.

02:46:16.132 --> 02:46:19.936
When I went to the UK,
I'm not kidding you,

02:46:19.936 --> 02:46:21.638
every person I talked to

02:46:21.638 --> 02:46:23.106
when they realized I was an American,

02:46:23.106 --> 02:46:26.009
which was literally one second
after I opened my mouth,

02:46:26.009 --> 02:46:27.444
they all asked me the same thing.

02:46:27.444 --> 02:46:30.347
"What is with Americans
and peanut butter?"

02:46:30.347 --> 02:46:32.449
Is peanut butter not popular in the UK?

02:46:32.449 --> 02:46:34.517
They were like, "You guys put
peanut butter in everything."

02:46:34.517 --> 02:46:36.219
We kind of do.

02:46:36.219 --> 02:46:37.387
This is really good peanut butter.

02:46:37.387 --> 02:46:39.522
Please forgive me, all the
peanut butter heads watching.

02:46:39.522 --> 02:46:41.658
Do you want it this liquidy?

02:46:41.658 --> 02:46:43.326
'Cause I'm thinking
peanut butter sandwiches,

02:46:43.326 --> 02:46:45.795
peanut butter and jelly,
peanut butter and honey,

02:46:45.795 --> 02:46:47.630
whatever you're mixing the
peanut butter with, right,

02:46:47.630 --> 02:46:49.899
you want some thickness to
it to stay on the bread.

02:46:49.899 --> 02:46:51.434
Do we want thin peanut butter?

02:46:51.434 --> 02:46:52.936
I don't know. I'm asking you, the viewer.

02:46:52.936 --> 02:46:56.706
What is the preferred
viscosity of peanut butter?

02:46:56.706 --> 02:46:58.775
I mean, this is creamy,

02:46:58.775 --> 02:47:02.112
but I mean, like, cream creamy.

02:47:02.112 --> 02:47:05.281
Italian sparkling mineral water

02:47:05.281 --> 02:47:08.018
with carbonation added.

02:47:08.018 --> 02:47:12.622
If anyone was wondering
just how boring I am,

02:47:12.622 --> 02:47:17.594
my favorite sparkling water
is actually the non-flavored.

02:47:17.594 --> 02:47:18.595
Right?

02:47:18.595 --> 02:47:20.897
Like, LaCroix, my
favorite one's the plain.

02:47:20.897 --> 02:47:22.565
That's right, you better "ugh."

02:47:22.565 --> 02:47:24.968
I just like the bubbles in the water.

02:47:26.336 --> 02:47:27.937
Mm.

02:47:27.937 --> 02:47:29.005
Smells Italian.

02:47:32.409 --> 02:47:34.744
Oh, yeah, it's really
harsh. This is very good.

02:47:35.979 --> 02:47:36.813
Joe: Mm-hmm.

02:47:36.813 --> 02:47:39.149
Like, I want that
harshness of the bubbles.

02:47:39.149 --> 02:47:40.517
What are you "ewwing" about?

02:47:40.517 --> 02:47:44.654
Speaking of Italy, pesto.

02:47:44.654 --> 02:47:45.655
So, the basil was imported,

02:47:45.655 --> 02:47:47.157
but I don't think this was made in Italy.

02:47:47.157 --> 02:47:48.892
Basil. People swear by this stuff.

02:47:48.892 --> 02:47:50.794
They swear by it.

02:47:50.794 --> 02:47:52.062
Dried mango slices.

02:47:52.062 --> 02:47:54.230
This right here, look how many
of these they gave me, man.

02:47:54.230 --> 02:47:56.433
This is 2 ½ pounds

02:47:56.433 --> 02:47:59.502
of dried organic mango slices.

02:47:59.502 --> 02:48:01.237
I am a mango boy.

02:48:03.006 --> 02:48:04.274
That's an impressive list of stuff.

02:48:04.274 --> 02:48:06.242
We don't have that many
Kirkland exclusives in the UK,

02:48:06.242 --> 02:48:08.111
but there is one interesting one I found,

02:48:08.111 --> 02:48:09.813
which is this hazelnut spread.

02:48:09.813 --> 02:48:11.781
This is just Costco's version of Nutella.

02:48:11.781 --> 02:48:12.916
Not "new-tell-uh."

02:48:12.916 --> 02:48:13.750
Well, it was interesting

02:48:13.750 --> 02:48:15.552
because I was looking at
the ingredients of this,

02:48:15.552 --> 02:48:17.687
and the percentages kind
of piqued my interest.

02:48:17.687 --> 02:48:19.355
So out of interest, we
googled what the contents

02:48:19.355 --> 02:48:21.458
of real Nutella are,
and the ingredients said

02:48:21.458 --> 02:48:23.793
that there were 13%
real hazelnuts in there

02:48:23.793 --> 02:48:26.529
as well as 7.4% fat-reduced cocoa powder.

02:48:26.529 --> 02:48:28.798
So if we compare it to this one,

02:48:28.798 --> 02:48:31.367
Leon, how much hazelnut
do you think is in this?

02:48:34.270 --> 02:48:36.005
Thirteen percent.

02:48:36.005 --> 02:48:37.207
Exactly the same.

02:48:37.207 --> 02:48:39.109
Fat-reduced cocoa powder, 7.4%.

02:48:39.109 --> 02:48:41.578
So on paper, this has
basically identical ingredients

02:48:41.578 --> 02:48:42.412
to real Nutella.

02:48:42.412 --> 02:48:44.414
I mean, it smells and
looks a lot like Nutella.

02:48:45.648 --> 02:48:47.684
I would struggle to tell
this apart from real Nutella

02:48:47.684 --> 02:48:50.220
in a blind taste test, and it is cheaper.

02:48:50.220 --> 02:48:52.322
So, hey, next time you're around

02:48:52.322 --> 02:48:54.057
and you really, really love Nutella,

02:48:54.057 --> 02:48:55.758
you can buy it in bulk here,
and you won't really know.

02:48:55.758 --> 02:48:57.427
I also found some products
which weren't Kirkland brand

02:48:57.427 --> 02:48:58.561
but did pique my interest.

02:48:59.562 --> 02:49:00.396
Marmite.

02:49:00.396 --> 02:49:02.966
I found this kind of
catering-size tub of Marmite,

02:49:02.966 --> 02:49:04.467
which I could not resist.

02:49:04.467 --> 02:49:06.269
I assume this is an exclusive

02:49:06.269 --> 02:49:07.570
and not something that
you'd find in the US.

02:49:07.570 --> 02:49:08.805
Not 100% sure.

02:49:08.805 --> 02:49:10.974
Made Marmite pasta and put
it on Instagram yesterday

02:49:10.974 --> 02:49:14.310
and people got upset, so it felt relevant.

02:49:14.310 --> 02:49:16.246
And I also found some
American products at Costco

02:49:16.246 --> 02:49:18.281
that you wouldn't normally
see on British shelves.

02:49:18.281 --> 02:49:21.317
For example, Skippy brand peanut butter.

02:49:21.317 --> 02:49:24.954
This isn't bad, but, like,
there's so much oil in here.

02:49:24.954 --> 02:49:27.257
You can see it's, like,
running off the top,

02:49:27.257 --> 02:49:29.659
and it's kind of made the
whole thing go very liquidy.

02:49:29.659 --> 02:49:30.793
According to the ingredients,

02:49:30.793 --> 02:49:33.763
this is 10% hydrogenated palm oil,

02:49:33.763 --> 02:49:35.098
which might go some way to explaining

02:49:35.098 --> 02:49:37.133
why it's so liquidy at room temperature.

02:49:37.133 --> 02:49:39.235
These caught my eye while
I was browsing the shelves.

02:49:39.235 --> 02:49:40.970
Smucker's Goober?

02:49:40.970 --> 02:49:43.506
Neither of those are
real words, first of all.

02:49:43.506 --> 02:49:46.943
But this is peanut butter
and grape jelly stripes.

02:49:46.943 --> 02:49:49.913
Is this what Americans
are putting in PB&amp;Js?

02:49:49.913 --> 02:49:52.582
It claims to be "America's
favorite combination

02:49:52.582 --> 02:49:54.117
peanut butter and jelly."

02:49:54.117 --> 02:49:56.452
How much competition do
they have in this field?

02:49:56.452 --> 02:49:57.554
I'd love to know.

02:49:57.554 --> 02:49:59.923
Americans love grape-flavor things,

02:49:59.923 --> 02:50:02.892
and it's really not common in
the UK for whatever reason.

02:50:02.892 --> 02:50:03.993
I mean, it's quite pretty.

02:50:03.993 --> 02:50:05.728
I'd love to see the machine that

02:50:05.728 --> 02:50:08.031
puts this into the jar in that pattern.

02:50:08.031 --> 02:50:09.432
This is a lot more solid.

02:50:09.432 --> 02:50:11.467
I think they've added gelling
agents and stuff to this

02:50:11.467 --> 02:50:13.169
to keep it in that uniform shape

02:50:13.169 --> 02:50:14.270
with the cool color pattern.

02:50:14.270 --> 02:50:16.372
The grape jelly is extremely sweet,

02:50:16.372 --> 02:50:18.508
and the peanut butter,
even I think on its own,

02:50:18.508 --> 02:50:20.810
is quite sweet compared
to the Skippy as well.

02:50:20.810 --> 02:50:21.744
I want to give a disclaimer.

02:50:21.744 --> 02:50:23.046
Although this is the exclusive section,

02:50:23.046 --> 02:50:26.683
I don't think these are exclusive.

02:50:26.683 --> 02:50:29.018
I just know that one awesome thing

02:50:29.018 --> 02:50:31.321
about the Costco here in the US,

02:50:31.321 --> 02:50:33.423
I don't know if it's in the
UK, Harry can confirm this,

02:50:33.423 --> 02:50:35.959
is they have ridiculously
good baked goods.

02:50:35.959 --> 02:50:39.395
Costco's in the US is also
famous for having a sheet cake.

02:50:39.395 --> 02:50:41.030
Couldn't get it. You gotta
order it ahead of time.

02:50:41.030 --> 02:50:42.799
I'm sorry. Let's get a
picture of that on the screen.

02:50:43.933 --> 02:50:44.901
With my face on it.

02:50:45.902 --> 02:50:49.806
But they have so many
muffins and croissants

02:50:49.806 --> 02:50:51.107
and other things.

02:50:51.107 --> 02:50:52.075
I heard really good things about

02:50:52.075 --> 02:50:53.176
the bakery section of Costco,

02:50:53.176 --> 02:50:55.044
so I also had to give that a try.

02:50:55.044 --> 02:50:57.647
This goes out to Katya's dad.

02:50:57.647 --> 02:50:59.015
Our producer Katya,

02:50:59.015 --> 02:51:01.584
apparently her dad really
loves Costco croissants.

02:51:01.584 --> 02:51:03.753
I feel like these would
benefit significantly

02:51:03.753 --> 02:51:04.587
from being heated up.

02:51:04.587 --> 02:51:07.557
It's not bad, as far as
pre-packaged croissants go.

02:51:07.557 --> 02:51:10.326
And finally, these cookies.

02:51:10.326 --> 02:51:12.161
You get chocolate chip,

02:51:12.161 --> 02:51:14.864
double chocolate, and white choc chip.

02:51:16.366 --> 02:51:18.534
In the UK, a lot of our
pre-packaged cookies,

02:51:18.534 --> 02:51:21.304
for whatever reason,
tend to be really solid,

02:51:21.304 --> 02:51:23.573
and you can snap them
rather than chew them.

02:51:23.573 --> 02:51:26.376
But this is the much softer
American-style cookie,

02:51:26.376 --> 02:51:27.410
which is really good.

02:51:27.410 --> 02:51:29.178
Full disclosure, this is the first time

02:51:29.178 --> 02:51:30.546
I've ever shopped at a Costco.

02:51:30.546 --> 02:51:31.547
And it's not a snob thing.

02:51:31.547 --> 02:51:34.217
See, I grew up, my dad
worked for a grocery chain,

02:51:34.217 --> 02:51:36.586
and then I move out into the world,

02:51:36.586 --> 02:51:39.455
and the thought of having
a case of toilet paper

02:51:39.455 --> 02:51:42.692
or bottled water in my
shoebox apartment was crazy.

02:51:42.692 --> 02:51:45.662
Also, $60 for a membership?

02:51:45.662 --> 02:51:46.796
I mean, I was just scraping by,

02:51:46.796 --> 02:51:48.931
so coming up with $60
to go grocery shopping

02:51:48.931 --> 02:51:51.067
was madness for me, so.

02:51:51.067 --> 02:51:55.004
And then just never went
until now for this video.

02:51:55.004 --> 02:51:56.806
And I think Costco's really awesome.

02:51:56.806 --> 02:51:58.641
I like it now. Shout-out to Kirkland.

02:51:58.641 --> 02:52:00.176
Costco in the UK is a little bit weird

02:52:00.176 --> 02:52:03.313
because not just anyone can
actually walk into a Costco.

02:52:03.313 --> 02:52:06.249
You have to actually apply
for warehouse membership,

02:52:06.249 --> 02:52:08.851
which is different to just
standard online membership.

02:52:08.851 --> 02:52:10.520
And to do that, you have to be working

02:52:10.520 --> 02:52:12.588
in a certain number of
limited professions.

02:52:12.588 --> 02:52:14.457
Some of the professions make sense.

02:52:14.457 --> 02:52:16.326
It's things like teachers,
who maybe work in a school

02:52:16.326 --> 02:52:17.393
and need to buy supplies,

02:52:17.393 --> 02:52:18.528
and some of them are really random.

02:52:18.528 --> 02:52:21.164
Things like airline
workers are allowed in.

02:52:21.164 --> 02:52:23.299
I think I was technically
allowed in as a journalist,

02:52:23.299 --> 02:52:25.368
so this is journalism, if anyone asks.

02:52:25.368 --> 02:52:27.670
I believe a year of standard
individual membership

02:52:27.670 --> 02:52:30.239
costs around £30, maybe slightly more.

02:52:30.239 --> 02:52:31.374
There's different tiers as well.

02:52:31.374 --> 02:52:32.842
You can get, like, executive membership,

02:52:32.842 --> 02:52:34.544
where you unlock certain perks.

02:52:34.544 --> 02:52:36.079
Honestly, I don't really
know why it's set up

02:52:36.079 --> 02:52:37.580
exactly this way in the UK.

02:52:37.580 --> 02:52:39.282
I guess they want to
kind of have some control

02:52:39.282 --> 02:52:40.883
over the foot traffic in the stores.

02:52:40.883 --> 02:52:43.086
They don't want everybody
just piling into the store.

02:52:43.086 --> 02:52:46.389
I went at 11 a.m. on a Tuesday,
and it was really busy,

02:52:46.389 --> 02:52:47.457
and I asked someone on the till,

02:52:47.457 --> 02:52:49.792
and they said that that wasn't
even busy by their standards.

02:52:49.792 --> 02:52:51.160
I think this is what it's like in the US,

02:52:51.160 --> 02:52:53.996
but the shop itself was just
basically an enormous warehouse

02:52:53.996 --> 02:52:55.131
with stuff everywhere.

02:52:55.131 --> 02:52:57.300
It wasn't organized hugely well.

02:52:57.300 --> 02:52:59.802
The aisles weren't particularly labeled.

02:52:59.802 --> 02:53:00.870
There were numbers on the aisles,

02:53:00.870 --> 02:53:02.238
but didn't say what was in them.

02:53:02.238 --> 02:53:03.773
So I just kind of had to snake around

02:53:03.773 --> 02:53:05.041
and try and find what I could find.

02:53:05.041 --> 02:53:07.210
Things were slightly
cheaper in there than usual,

02:53:07.210 --> 02:53:10.012
but I don't even think things
were massively discounted,

02:53:10.012 --> 02:53:11.447
particularly the branded stuff

02:53:11.447 --> 02:53:13.216
compared to the Kirkland stuff.

02:53:13.216 --> 02:53:14.517
So I think you're more just going

02:53:14.517 --> 02:53:16.152
because you need to buy things in bulk

02:53:16.152 --> 02:53:17.420
and it's slightly more convenient,

02:53:17.420 --> 02:53:19.489
rather than because you're
trying to save a lot of money

02:53:19.489 --> 02:53:20.757
on your day-to-day groceries.

02:53:20.757 --> 02:53:22.358
For me to be able to sign up for this,

02:53:22.358 --> 02:53:23.793
they needed to see a pay slip

02:53:23.793 --> 02:53:25.895
so they could prove who I was employed by.

02:53:25.895 --> 02:53:26.729
Kind of weird.

02:53:28.664 --> 02:53:32.068
A whole pizza from a UK
Costco will cost you £9.99,

02:53:32.068 --> 02:53:34.904
which at the time of recording was $12.38.

02:53:34.904 --> 02:53:38.474
A Costco pizza in the US is $9.95,

02:53:38.474 --> 02:53:41.210
or £8.03.

02:53:41.210 --> 02:53:45.748
That's a 19.9% price decrease in the US.

02:53:45.748 --> 02:53:47.617
The Costco hot dog here in the US

02:53:47.617 --> 02:53:51.154
with a 20-ounce soda is $1.50,

02:53:51.154 --> 02:53:54.190
the same price it's been since 1985.

02:53:54.190 --> 02:53:56.125
How has Costco managed to sell them

02:53:56.125 --> 02:53:58.428
for so low for all these years?

02:53:58.428 --> 02:53:59.662
In an age where seemingly everything

02:53:59.662 --> 02:54:00.830
has been hit by inflation,

02:54:00.830 --> 02:54:02.064
the Costco hot dog has become

02:54:02.064 --> 02:54:03.433
somewhat of a viral phenomenon.

02:54:03.433 --> 02:54:05.968
Their commitment to keeping
the hot-dog combo at $1.50

02:54:05.968 --> 02:54:07.770
is so strong that, as the story goes,

02:54:07.770 --> 02:54:09.939
when the current CEO
approached the old CEO

02:54:09.939 --> 02:54:11.407
about possibly raising the price,

02:54:11.407 --> 02:54:14.410
he said, "If you raise the
price of the f---ing hot dog,

02:54:14.410 --> 02:54:16.112
I will kill you. Figure it out."

02:54:16.112 --> 02:54:16.946
And they did.

02:54:16.946 --> 02:54:18.881
Costco would soon switch from selling

02:54:18.881 --> 02:54:21.017
Hebrew National hot dogs
in their food courts

02:54:21.017 --> 02:54:22.485
to manufacturing their own.

02:54:22.485 --> 02:54:25.555
They opened a hot-dog factory
in LA, then in Chicago,

02:54:25.555 --> 02:54:27.824
reducing production costs
and keeping the hot dog

02:54:27.824 --> 02:54:29.826
at the $1.50 price point today.

02:54:29.826 --> 02:54:32.762
It is fair to point out that
our hot dog costs £1.50,

02:54:32.762 --> 02:54:34.630
which is more like $1.86.

02:54:34.630 --> 02:54:36.299
It does come with two more ounces of soda,

02:54:36.299 --> 02:54:37.333
so maybe that's why,

02:54:37.333 --> 02:54:39.001
or maybe Costco just likes the aesthetic

02:54:39.001 --> 02:54:40.603
of having 1.50 on the sign.

02:54:42.905 --> 02:54:46.909
A slice of pepperoni pizza from
a UK Costco is 826 calories,

02:54:46.909 --> 02:54:50.179
while a slice of cheese pizza is 751.

02:54:50.179 --> 02:54:51.547
The most calorific thing on the menu

02:54:51.547 --> 02:54:53.049
is a whole pepperoni pizza.

02:54:53.049 --> 02:54:56.786
A whole pepperoni pizza is 4,962 calories,

02:54:56.786 --> 02:54:59.589
which is 248% of your daily allowance.

02:54:59.589 --> 02:55:04.160
A slice of pepperoni at Costco
in the US is 650 calories.

02:55:04.160 --> 02:55:06.529
A slice of cheese roughly the same size

02:55:06.529 --> 02:55:08.264
will be 710 calories.

02:55:08.264 --> 02:55:09.899
That's 60 calories more.

02:55:09.899 --> 02:55:10.800
Hm.

02:55:10.800 --> 02:55:12.101
Does that make sense that the cheese

02:55:12.101 --> 02:55:13.870
is more calories than the pepperoni?

02:55:13.870 --> 02:55:14.904
I gotta.

02:55:15.805 --> 02:55:16.639
Mwah.

02:55:16.639 --> 02:55:19.575
A UK chicken bake is 911 calories.

02:55:19.575 --> 02:55:22.879
An entire US chicken bake is 840 calories.

02:55:24.013 --> 02:55:26.883
A UK hot dog is 602 calories.

02:55:26.883 --> 02:55:29.585
The hot dog and 20-ounce soda in the US

02:55:29.585 --> 02:55:34.323
is 580 to 850 calories
depending on the drink you get.

02:55:34.323 --> 02:55:36.325
So least calories would
be, of course, diet Pepsi,

02:55:36.325 --> 02:55:37.727
which has zero calories.

02:55:37.727 --> 02:55:40.429
If you got a regular Pepsi,
that'd be 250 calories.

02:55:40.429 --> 02:55:43.399
And if you wanted to get the
most calories in your drink,

02:55:43.399 --> 02:55:46.636
that of course would be 280 extra calories

02:55:46.636 --> 02:55:49.171
if you got the Tropicana fruit punch.

02:55:49.205 --> 02:55:53.042
I've been asked by my producer

02:55:53.042 --> 02:55:54.443
to wipe up the crumbs.

02:55:54.443 --> 02:55:57.380
One thing Little Caesars
didn't provide were napkins.

02:55:57.380 --> 02:55:58.281
That's OK.

02:55:58.281 --> 02:56:00.016
Let me wipe my mouth real quick.

02:56:00.016 --> 02:56:03.719
Mm!

02:56:03.719 --> 02:56:07.123
This video, sponsored by Domino's.

02:56:07.123 --> 02:56:08.858
Ah!

02:56:08.858 --> 02:56:10.426
Caesar!

02:56:10.426 --> 02:56:11.928
Et tu, Brute?

